{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade","id":1466535,"title":"What Goals do the Camarilla Have (beyond survival/Masquerade)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-03T16:48:27-07:00","id":1466535,"title":"What Goals do the Camarilla Have (beyond survival/Masquerade)","content":"Survival is an <i>Imperative</i>, something that you must do (unless you are standing in field just before dawn, regretting your undead existence). The Masquerade is a function of the Camarilla's Survival Imperative - no small thing. A <i>Goal</i> is something that you aspire to that, if achieved, would make you or the world better and helps to define you in a concrete way. A simplistic position to take would be to say that if the Camarilla as a whole does not have a clearly defined Goal beyond survival, it isn't a valid Sect and then ask for evidence of a collectively understood Goal. That's not the direction I am aiming at in this post.<br /> <br /> VtM, for me, is something I left behind in terms of play, but still have this lingering thirst for that I'm trying to satisfy through informative discussion. New and mostly oblivious to V5, I had my kneejerk reaction to some V5 lore discussions, &quot;Lasombra what?!&quot;. I used to play that Clan and it is the attempt to imagine them switching from the Sword of Caine to the Status Quo Sect that leads me to formulate this question. Rather than &quot;Does <i>the</i> Camarilla...&quot;, I'm asking, Do <i>they</i> have Goal<u>s</u>?<br /> <br /> In V5 lore, are there Camarilla Vampires significant to the setting in power or influence who are attempting to rally others in the sect to undertake some meaningful quest, whether or not there is universal or majority agreement?<br /> <br /> If so, what are those Goals and what progress has been made toward them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":26467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","user":"HorizonParty2021","date":". 11-03-2021, 08:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T17:11:54-07:00","id":1466538,"title":"","content":"Besides getting money and power, I don't think the Camarilla leadership has any goals aside from survival.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T17:39:43-07:00","id":1466550,"title":"","content":"The Camarilla generally has the goal of establish itself as the sole power among vampires. It may look like they've ditched that in 5th Edition but that is something they haven't given up on. It's just they have ejected the Brujah because they weren't willing to play ball and they want to eradicate the Sabbat and Anarchs.<br /> The Camarilla would like every vampire in the world to be part of its organization.<br /> <br /> That's the only way they can permanently enforce the Masquerade and make sure everyone is under the auspices of the Inner Council. It's why they also hate the Antediluvians as a concept. Until they became undeniable, they were an existential threat to Kindredom and thus made people more afraid of them then the Camarilla.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T18:59:49-07:00","id":1466575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1466538#post1466538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides getting money and power, I don't think the Camarilla leadership has any goals aside from survival.</div> </div> </div> </div>Money and assets in large quantity that they have no legal claim to. It's kinda like they have built a house of cards. Surely, there must be famous Camarilla Vampires who have inspired others toward some great ideal or mission. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1466550#post1466550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Camarilla generally has the goal of establish itself as the sole power among vampires. It may look like they've ditched that in 5th Edition but that is something they haven't given up on. It's just they have ejected the Brujah because they weren't willing to play ball and they want to eradicate the Sabbat and Anarchs. The Camarilla would like every vampire in the world to be part of its organization.<br /> <br /> That's the only way they can permanently enforce the Masquerade and make sure everyone is under the auspices of the Inner Council.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I were a member of the Camarilla, I would be <i>against</i> it achieving global dominion, even if I could only hold that position in the secrecy my skull affords. As organizations get bigger and more powerful, they become less tolerant of deviancy from their rules and more tyrannical. In the Sabbat Chronicle I played, I was trying to delay my own sect's conquest of a neighboring Camarilla city, because European Sect Elders were waiting to install a Bishop who had done nothing to assist the war and would likely mistreat those who had fought under their privileged rule. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1466550#post1466550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's why they also hate the Antediluvians as a concept. Until they became undeniable, they were an existential threat to Kindredom and thus made people more afraid of them then the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm misunderstanding the last sentence. How were they a unifying threat <i>Until</i> their existence became undeniable? It seems to imply that they were more of a boogieman then and leaves the question open as to what effect Antediluvians' existence being proven has on Kindred Society - the Camarilla's position. I know what the old Sabbat's position was; that the Camarilla are pawns or willing minions of the Antediluvians. Are the V5 Camarilla concerned about their own image in relation to this existential threat?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T19:11:14-07:00","id":1466579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1466575#post1466575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm misunderstanding the last sentence. How were they a unifying threat <i>Until</i> their existence became undeniable? It seems to imply that they were more of a boogieman then and leaves the question open as to what effect Antediluvians' existence being proven has on Kindred Society - the Camarilla's position. I know what the old Sabbat's position was; that the Camarilla are pawns or willing minions of the Antediluvians. Are the V5 Camarilla concerned about their own image in relation to this existential threat?</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that they're undeniable, the Camarilla has gone completely 180 and is doing things like Ancestor cults and rituals to venerate them. They just hope the Antediluvians never show up.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T19:23:51-07:00","id":1466582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1466579#post1466579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that they're undeniable, the Camarilla has gone completely 180 and is doing things like Ancestor cults and rituals to venerate them. They just hope the Antediluvians never show up.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sabbat are right. Destroy the Camarilla in the name of <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />Humanity<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T20:28:01-07:00","id":1466598,"title":"","content":"Individual ancients have goals, some of them petty, some of them grand, and some of them nightmarish, but the Camarilla as a whole is just devoted to survival, power, and wealth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T20:48:03-07:00","id":1466601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1466582#post1466582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sabbat are right. Destroy the Camarilla in the name of <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />Humanity<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the Antes are far more a threat to other vampires than to humanity.<br /> <br /> Anyway, keeping mainly to pre-V5 Camarilla, but it also applies to V5: the Camarilla does have a lofty goal. They don't just want safety. They don't want to create a stable territory. They want to create a stable <b>world</b>.<br /> <br /> They want to be a system, more than an organization, something anyone can rely on and guarantee safety for the vampires around the world. And through that free vampires to do their stuff without worrying too much beyond following a few sensible laws.<br /> <br /> In that sense, the Camarilla isn't so much the structure above cities, but the idea that one day every city will follow their Traditions and recommendations, that every city will be a safe Domain under its own Prince.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T21:06:56-07:00","id":1466604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1466601#post1466601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Antes are far more a threat to other vampires than to humanity.<br /> <br /> Anyway, keeping mainly to pre-V5 Camarilla, but it also applies to V5: the Camarilla does have a lofty goal. They don't just want safety. They don't want to create a stable territory. They want to create a stable <b>world</b>.<br /> <br /> They want to be a system, more than an organization, something anyone can rely on and guarantee safety for the vampires around the world. And through that free vampires to do their stuff without worrying too much beyond following a few sensible laws.<br /> <br /> In that sense, the Camarilla isn't so much the structure above cities, but the idea that one day every city will follow their Traditions and recommendations, that every city will be a safe Domain under its own Prince.</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked Nines Rodriguez's description of the Camarilla too.<br /> <br /> &quot;It's a Pyramid scheme to get everyone sending money and power up to the top while getting those beneath to make shit run downhill.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T21:45:20-07:00","id":1466610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1466601#post1466601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Antes are far more a threat to other vampires than to humanity.<br /> <br /> Anyway, keeping mainly to pre-V5 Camarilla, but it also applies to V5: the Camarilla does have a lofty goal. They don't just want safety. They don't want to create a stable territory. They want to create a stable <b>world</b>.<br /> <br /> They want to be a system, more than an organization, something anyone can rely on and guarantee safety for the vampires around the world. And through that free vampires to do their stuff without worrying too much beyond following a few sensible laws.<br /> <br /> In that sense, the Camarilla isn't so much the structure above cities, but the idea that one day every city will follow their Traditions and recommendations, that every city will be a safe Domain under its own Prince.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's the most convincing description so far. It is still hard to separate a System from Territorial Ambition when the former requires the latter on a global scale. World domination has drawbacks, even if it is only a means to a noble end. <br /> <br /> When I was playing a Sabbat Chronicle, I made hefty payments to the Nosferatu for information about unjust rulings and bias in Camarilla courts. I used this strategy, because Princes are often not neutral arbiters of justice. They are somebody's pawn or Thrall. A Vampire of low standing who frenzies and breaches the Masquerade could expect to be executed. A higher status Vampire who does the same has a good chance of their crime being forgiven. As it turned out in that Chronicle, my Storyteller had it that a Brujah Vampire had been executed for the same crime that an Elder had committed without consequence. <br /> <br /> We had captured and impersonated an Archon and used that cover to unravel past coverups. Basically, I devised a strategy of winning by forcing the Camarilla's own justice system to operate as intended. This strategy worked, seeing some powerful Camarilla Vampires put to death by their peers. The false Archon became known as a champion of justice in the Camarilla. Back home in Sabbat-land, my character had some intense confrontations with thirsty diabolists in the know about my plan, which diminished the number of viable targets for diablerie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T21:47:13-07:00","id":1466611,"title":"","content":"So the first thing to get out of the way is this: Hypocrisy runs rampant amongst vampires, and so when talking about the ideals and goals of any vampire sect, you are going to have to acknowledge that there is, or at least should be, a sharp distinction between what a sect wants its ideals and goals to be, and what that all the same can express itself in practice. No sect is immune to that.<br /> <br /> That said, the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Ultimately the Camarilla's goals can be looked at from a few perspectives that were given nuance over the run of VtM (we're talking pre V5 here, because in V5 the Camarilla is frankly basically an incompetent cartoonishly evil joke in a lot of ways, and for people that liked to do Cam games, sigh. But we're getting off topic).<br /> <br /> In the main, the entire sect was founded on a belief that Vampires should be far less overt in their manipulation and control of mortals than they generally were in the Dark Ages period. Much of this was certainly from a &quot;because otherwise we'll be frigging killed&quot; issue. However some of it was that the Camarilla is in some ways the outright inheritor of things like the Iconoclastic movement of Antonius the Gaul, which believed that things like vampires setting up blood cults and or ruling other vampires themselves as religious figures and gods was morally wrong/outright horrifying and needed to be suppressed (which is a thing that makes me sigh about the Cam now being full of blood cults in V5, but again, we'll be here all day on that change, so). And so in that sense the Camarilla, while not certainly all that humane, does as far as what ideals and goals could be ascribed to it, like to fancy itself a check against outright monstrosity, and in some ways, sure. That the structure and society it establishes helps suppress the more monstrous aspects of vampires and prevents both them and humans from being done up into blood cults. That a variety of vampires with something like ethics and morals regarded it as the least of all evils to support (but still evil because, you know, vampires), because they believe in a state of chaos, Vampires often become monstrously self indulgent, which brings the beast to the fore, which furthers blood cults, which furthers cities going to war, which furthers vampires being exposed to and getting killed out by hunters, etc. etc. etc., all the things the Camarilla was founded as a reaction against. Which is to say, a lot of the Camarilla's goals and ideology can be looked at as bound up and founded from being reactive.<br /> <br /> And so as related, The Camarilla's great big goal is Order with a capital O. It regards all vampires as default Camarilla as its stated position because as Monteparnas noted, it seeks to have a universal vampiric society. The Beast disrupts Order, thereby the Camarilla creates law and an outright ornate social order as a check against the beast, to provide peaceable venues like Elysium where vampires can interact without opting to open warfare as a ready default. Again, the sect was founded in the face of the Dark Ages, with its Long Night and War of Princes, and in many ways the sect was still driven by reacting to the idea that those times could come again if it blinked too hard.<br /> <br /> In some ways what the Camarilla was trying to do was construct an elaborate shell game of an entire sociopolitical system against the Beast to keep it distracted. That whole &quot;A beast I am, lest a beast I become&quot; thing, writ large onto an entire system/society. <br /> <br /> I know people are going to look at that and go &quot;but the Camarilla's wrong because X, Y, Z&quot; and that is going to miss my point by a mile. The Camarilla, right or wrong, hypocritical or not, self delusional or not, did indeed have some ideals and goals going on beyond just &quot;make it so we can live to the next night.&quot; The degree of hypocrisy, delusion, failure or simply being incorrect that underlied those goals is something else completely.<br /> <br /> (Also in any case in a larger sense all the sects are basically wrong to strong extents for all that they can get a couple things right sometimes, the whole point of redemption stories is that anyone who buys into the &quot;Beast I am&quot; riddle that vampires like to promote is already failing their own soul)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T00:26:34-07:00","id":1466616,"title":"","content":"The leaders of the Cam don't want it too powerful, because nobody wants to lose power in their own domains. Even if Inner Circle member A and B thought his position very stable and that he'd never leave the IC (unlikely, given how easy it'd be to push him out if he went into a very likely torpor) he'd have to concern himself with the other IC members and the veritable amount of powerful assassins that'd come knocking if he ever threatened the rule of princes on a large scale or if he tried to use the Camarilla to tangle with someone powerful. Most IC members probably think they're likely to retire at some point and really wouldn't want to set up a precedent that gets in the way of them ruling a small domain. From a cost/benefit analysis, it's an absolutely stupid idea for the Cam to get heavy handed. <br /> <br /> I believe the Cam was founded to deal with modernity. After all it was created at the start of the Renaissance, a time of rapid social change and technological progress. The Anarch revolt happened because too many opportunities appeared at once and neonates adapted fast enough to challenge Elders. The Cam keeps elders safe by providing some semblance of structure, backing power and legitimacy to a prince's rule, it also succeeds by appeasing the neonates a little more in quantifying rules better. <br /> <br /> <br /> So, onto the main question: OTHER GOALS the Camarilla has. <br /> <br /> -It promotes the OG 7 clans at the expense of outsiders. The other clans just aren't so good for the sect's promotion of the Masquerade and the Road of Humanity that champions the Masquerade. Assamites, FoS, Ravnos and Lasombra are inherently destabilizing clans with masquerade raping powers. Tzmisce don't make big waves but are very difficult to control, and Giovanni are.. well.. they know what they did. And then there's Caitiff... <br /> <br /> -It cracks down on Vicissitude. The source of a lot of trauma, a tell-tale sign of sabbat infiltrators, possibly a magic space disease, and ultimately a very transgressive discipline that allows one to change the body that was cursed to stay the same. <br /> <br /> -It supports the Tremere desire <s>for a monopoly </s> to keep Kindred safe from bad magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T07:28:25-07:00","id":1466647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1466610#post1466610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the most convincing description so far. It is still hard to separate a System from Territorial Ambition when the former requires the latter on a global scale. World domination has drawbacks, even if it is only a means to a noble end.</div> </div> </div> </div>The key here is to understand what the Camarilla <b>is</b> as an institution.<br /> <br /> Camarilla isn't a country. It isn't a religion. It isn't a territory holder. We like to talk about Camarilla territory, <b><u>but there's no such a thing</u></b>.<br /> <br /> As an organization, they have no territory at all.<br /> <br /> What the Camarilla is more like the UN. They are definitely a political body, but have their members' sovereignty as one of their stated assumptions and goals. Their power don't extend over Princes, it derives from them. It invites every Domain to accept a body of rules for their common good and use the tools it offers to solve their issues.<br /> <br /> If a common threat arises, a common response is organized. But they have few to no solders of their own. The members of the Inner Circle are powerful Princes in their own right, and they may use the organization to further their influence, but they don't exert overt control through it.<br /> <br /> Justicars? As the Interpol they are empowered by acceptance. They must follow the rules of each domain, they bow to the Princes, need permission. They are the eyes of the global organization, and a Prince must take care around them to a degree, but they have no official authority over any Prince and not only once a Justicar was sent to headquarters staked by a pissed off Prince.<br /> <br /> So a world &quot;dominated&quot; by the Camarilla isn't a world where this powerful \u00fcber-government controls everything, but just a world where every Domain accepts those common rules to keep their own personal sovereignty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T12:39:15-07:00","id":1466696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1466616#post1466616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The leaders of the Cam don't want it too powerful, because nobody wants to lose power in their own domains. Even if Inner Circle member A and B thought his position very stable and that he'd never leave the IC (unlikely, given how easy it'd be to push him out if he went into a very likely torpor) he'd have to concern himself with the other IC members and the veritable amount of powerful assassins that'd come knocking if he ever threatened the rule of princes on a large scale or if he tried to use the Camarilla to tangle with someone powerful. Most IC members probably think they're likely to retire at some point and really wouldn't want to set up a precedent that gets in the way of them ruling a small domain. From a cost/benefit analysis, it's an absolutely stupid idea for the Cam to get heavy handed.<br /> <br /> I believe the Cam was founded to deal with modernity. After all it was created at the start of the Renaissance, a time of rapid social change and technological progress. The Anarch revolt happened because too many opportunities appeared at once and neonates adapted fast enough to challenge Elders. The Cam keeps elders safe by providing some semblance of structure, backing power and legitimacy to a prince's rule, it also succeeds by appeasing the neonates a little more in quantifying rules better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually it wasn't that simple. The Revolt and the Inquisition killed a lot of vampires, particularly the younger, less powerful ones. Less then a decade after the Camarilla was formally formed, the Anarchs were beaten. They couldn't continue fighting. The Convention of Thorns was basically a peace treaty. The Sabbat was formed by the most radical of the Anarchs who even in the face of defeat refused to accept it hence why they are so utterly inhuman and monstrous compared to the modern Anarchs despite both originating from the same source.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1466616#post1466616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-It promotes the OG 7 clans at the expense of outsiders. The other clans just aren't so good for the sect's promotion of the Masquerade and the Road of Humanity that champions the Masquerade. Assamites, FoS, Ravnos and Lasombra are inherently destabilizing clans with masquerade raping powers. Tzmisce don't make big waves but are very difficult to control, and Giovanni are.. well.. they know what they did.</div> </div> </div> </div>What? How are the Assamites, Settites, Ravnos and Lasombra 'inherently destabilizing clans with masquerade raping powers'? I mean I can get 'Masquerade-raping powers' bit with the Ravnos and the Lasombra but Quietus and Serpentis? Yeah, they have some powers that can be Masquerade breaches but then so does the Disciplines among the Cam 7. Hell, Serpentis has some overlap with Protean and even before V5, people speculated that it was an offshoot of Protean.<br /> <br /> As for the 'inherently destabilizing' bit, again I can kind of see that with the Followers of Set, the Sabbat Lasombra and some Ravnos that play into the outsider stereotype of the Clan but the Assamites are a different story. They're one of the more ordered Clans that largely keep to themselves and stay out of wider Kindred politics. It's just that they are often hired by others as assassins, a service that the Cam itself has long made use of. Whether in the Rev Ed or V5, the Cam were likewise willing to accept the Assamites into the Sect. At most they were feared for their assassination skills and practices of diablerie.<br /> <br /> So at the very least the Assamites shouldn't be on that list.<br /> <br /> As for the Tzimisce being 'too hard to control', this is the Sect who's founding Clans included the Brujah, Gangrel and Malkavians yet the Tzimisce were too much to handle? A Clan that has an offshoot that is basically ruled by a bunch of old Elders still playing at Feudal Lords? That V5 basically declaring screw and putting at least the Old Clan and some Sabbat defectors in the Cam while V20 established that there were Anarch Tzimisce that never left the Movement and therefore were for a time between First and Second Revolts where they were nominally under the Cam.<br /> <br /> As for the Giovanni, the funny thing was that several of the Founders and many of the pro-Cam Elder Venture were quietly supporting Augustus' usurpation of Cappadocius as they had become frustrated with the direction he was leading the Clan, namely away from being their Seneschals for a more spiritual/mystical path. They thought Augustus would bring the Clan back to that former state. Of course Augustus has his own plans beyond just taking over the Clan.<br /> <br /> Plus it would be rather blatantly hypocritical for them to reject the Giovanni for the diablerie of Cappadocius while getting into bed with the Tremere, a Clan long stigmatized for be usurpers.<br /> <br /> Though I will say, the neutrality of the Promise having a time limit in V5 actually makes sense and is a retcon I'm completely fine with. For the Camarilla Elders they figured that in five hundred years time they would be the dominant force in Kindred politics and power, with either the Giovanni realizing that they can't compete and that they're better off joining or easily forcing them to submit when the Promise ends. For their part, Augustus and his lieutenants believed they would have Endless Night well before that, securing them dominance over the world. Of course the situation has radically changed and now both groups are not in the best position to take advantage of the upcoming end of the Promise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T15:42:02-07:00","id":1466710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1466616#post1466616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, onto the main question: OTHER GOALS the Camarilla has.<br /> <br /> -It promotes the OG 7 clans at the expense of outsiders. The other clans just aren't so good for the sect's promotion of the Masquerade and the Road of Humanity that champions the Masquerade. Assamites, FoS, Ravnos and Lasombra are inherently destabilizing clans with masquerade raping powers. Tzmisce don't make big waves but are very difficult to control, and Giovanni are.. well.. they know what they did. And then there's Caitiff...<br /> <br /> -It cracks down on Vicissitude. The source of a lot of trauma, a tell-tale sign of sabbat infiltrators, possibly a magic space disease, and ultimately a very transgressive discipline that allows one to change the body that was cursed to stay the same.<br /> <br /> -It supports the Tremere desire <s>for a monopoly </s> to keep Kindred safe from bad magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>None of those are sect goals for the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> 1- OoC the Camarilla is limited to main membership of the 7 OG clans just because they're OG. It's a stupid restriction writers created for themselves just to make their work easier, but goes against the Cam stated purposes and have no weight on how it worked pre-V5. IC the idea of a clan asking for membership wasn't even a thing until Revised. Everyone is a member by default and the only thing keeping other clans from having Justicars and Councilors is lack of suitable candidates.<br /> <br /> 2- It never did that. Like, ever. This was the True Black Hand.<br /> <br /> 3- No, it doesn't. The clan always did it by itself. The other Camarilla members never cared about this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T15:46:22-07:00","id":1466711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1466710#post1466710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">None of those are sect goals for the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> 1- OoC the Camarilla is limited to main membership of the 7 OG clans just because they're OG. It's a stupid restriction writers created for themselves just to make their work easier, but goes against the Cam stated purposes and have no weight on how it worked pre-V5. IC the idea of a clan asking for membership wasn't even a thing until Revised. Everyone is a member by default and the only thing keeping other clans from having Justicars and Councilors is lack of suitable candidates.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean the Players Handbook made it explicit in 2nd Edition that the Independent Clans didn't see THEMSELVES as part of the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> * The Assamites were a bunch of diablerie-hungry fanatics who hated the Camarilla and Tremere especially.<br /> * The Followers of Set were, well, the Followers of Set.<br /> * The Giovanni seemed like they'd fit right in, which is probably why Justin Achilli made them plan to destroy the world via Cthulhuoid ritual.<br /> * The Ravnos were, well, people the Camarilla hated and vice versa<br /> <br /> So the Camarilla considering themselves to have authority over the Independent Clans in their cities while the latter actively rejecting it stems from the earliest days of the gameline.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T16:14:36-07:00","id":1466720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1466647#post1466647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an organization, they have no territory at all.<br /> <br /> What the Camarilla is more like the UN. They are definitely a political body, but have their members' sovereignty as one of their stated assumptions and goals. Their power don't extend over Princes, it derives from them. It invites every Domain to accept a body of rules for their common good and use the tools it offers to solve their issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>Got it. That's why, in my Sabbat Campaign, I had to pull off this incredibly complex ruse to induce European Camarilla Princes to send heavy hitting reinforcements to a city they still thought to be under the control of the local Prince (we had the airports and were waiting to capture). Each Prince is mostly concerned with their own city and a city being lost on the other side of the pond seems like a distant concern.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":26467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","user":"HorizonParty2021","date":". 11-04-2021, 09:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T18:09:47-07:00","id":1466732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1466711#post1466711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the Camarilla considering themselves to have authority over the Independent Clans in their cities while the latter actively rejecting it stems from the earliest days of the gameline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but we're talking Camarilla ideology, the point isn't that it wasn't explained in the setting, but that it wasn't due to a Camarilla decision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T19:13:48-07:00","id":1466739,"title":"","content":"Under <i>Our Mission Statement</i> in V5's guide, there are a few paragraphs and a speech about this. The former says that it organises kindred and by extension, humanity, to &quot;improve our common world&quot; based on the &quot;single will&quot; of the Inner Council. The latter describes how kindred conserved culture through the Dark Ages and will be able to conserve civilisation through global warming or nuclear armageddon. Both come across a bit unsubstantiated, but there's room for aspiration in the Camarilla, at least along its middle ranks, and it helps if you consider humanity to be incapable of looking after itself, but still valuable in some way. They also make the point that survival as a goal doesn't justify itself; they need purpose or failing that, to feel like they serve a purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T20:25:23-07:00","id":1466746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1466710#post1466710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1- OoC the Camarilla is limited to main membership of the 7 OG clans just because they're OG. It's a stupid restriction writers created for themselves just to make their work easier, but goes against the Cam stated purposes and have no weight on how it worked pre-V5. IC the idea of a clan asking for membership wasn't even a thing until Revised. Everyone is a member by default and the only thing keeping other clans from having Justicars and Councilors is lack of suitable candidates.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you are on to something here.<br /> <br /> I make the distinction between the Camarilla as a global conspiracy that theoretically govern all vampires, and the clans that set on the Inner Circle. So on a certain level, it's never been about &quot;these clans are <i>in</i> the Camarilla&quot; it's about &quot;these clans are <i>represented</i> on the <i>Inner Circle</i>.&quot; I think that's an important difference. In addition to the Camarilla itself, there's also what I call the &quot;Camarilla system&quot; which extends beyond it. <br /> <br /> The Camarilla's relationship to the Assamites and Giovanni are good examples of that. Despite being Independent Clans, both clans were in fact heavily regulated by the Camarilla. The Treaty of Tyre explicitly controlled a lot of actions the Assamites could take. It regulated their hunts and regulated interactions the Assamites could do among the Camarilla domains. In the original clan description it stated the Assamites were called in as assassins by the Justicars, Archons, and Princes. So even though they were independent, the Camarilla had a lot of control over them. They operated within the system the Camarilla had created. The Assamites could theoretically have joined and been on the Inner Circle and become just like any other clan, but didn't want to because they preferred their weird diablerie religion and preferred to be heavily regulated contract assassins instead.<br /> <br /> The Giovanni had a similar system. While the Promise of 1528 wasn't created until later, even in the original clan description we knew there had been a deal between them and the Camarilla. In exchange for not being destroyed, the Giovanni would have to be &quot;neutral&quot; and not interfere in Kindred affairs, aka not go against the Camarilla. Then we learned about restrictions like not embracing more than 3 Kindred every generation, and while not explicitly tied to the first part, it always made sense to me that was the reason for it. So again, while independent and not participating in Camarilla politics, the clan was regulated to a heavy degree. It was left alone provided it obeyed the rules. (This pretty much was thrown outside the window once Justin Achilli wrote the first Giovanni tribebook. As a result, I've encountered a lot of players who don't see how the Promise of 1528 controlled anything the Giovanni did - which completely ignored the original presentation.)<br /> <br /> The other two independent clans didn't have anything like that, so obviously there were gaps. The nomadic Ravnos were just tolerated, but the clan had no organization at all so there was really nothing that could be done. Without some kind of organ that could speak of behalf of the clan, there was no way relations could be regulated. On the other hand, the Sabbat was equally ignored by the Ravnos. <br /> <br /> The Followers of Set were an interesting case because originally they seemed to have been built as the &quot;big bad&quot; of the setting given their role as priests of the Wyrm. Whenever compared against the Sabbat, the Setites were supposed to come out as more evil. The most we get about their relationship with the Camarilla is a quote that the Camarilla wishes to use the Setites, but it is the Setites who are using them. Later in the Sabbat quote about the Setites, a Tzimisce elder complains that the Camarilla don't realize what a threat the Setites are, and that you &quot;don't use a snake.&quot; That implies some kind of one hand washes the other thing is going on between the Camarilla and Setites. In the first Followers of Set clanbook gave us the interesting detail that the Ventrue actually invited them to join the Camarilla at the beginning. We're told IC that the Setites refused, but for all we know the other clans vetoed it after telling Hardestadt he was crazy for inviting the Setites. We also know that the Setites are also an enemy of the Sabbat since the Sabbat took in the Serpents of the Light. So we have a vague undefined relationship between the Camarilla and the Setites. The Setites are doing something that the Camarilla wants done.<br /> <br /> So it's very clear - the Independent Clans are not the enemy of the Camarilla, and in fact work with them to some degree. They have their own reasons why they're not members, but still have regulations governing them and individual members could in theory work within Camarilla domains. Two of them have agreements, backed by force, that explicitly defines certain behavior. Another has some kind of quid pro quo relationship. All have some kind of autonomy. They don't have to worry about some Justicar coming up and judging their internal works, but it's very likely two or even three of these clans could have a Justicar show up to enforce a potential violation of some other agreement. Only the nomadic and unorganized Ravnos are ignored being left to the local domains to do with whatever they wanted. There's a system in place that govern these relationships. They don't affect internal Camarilla politics directly except by individuals showing up to Conclaves (since we're told those are open to all Kindred), and in return are left autonomous with their own internal affairs.<br /> <br /> Now let's look at the Lasombra antitribu. We don't get details on them until much later. But it's very apparent that these Lasombra are in fact members of the Camarilla. They just don't have a set on the Inner Circle or have a Justicar. Presumably they have Princes and even have members who are archons. So that's another clan that excepts the authority of the Camarilla. Presumably if there were enough of them, they could have representation.<br /> <br /> The Old Clan Tzimisce do their own thing in the Oradea League (or hidden among the True Black Hand). But I don't believe there isn't some kind of <i>arrangement</i> between the Oradea League and the Camarilla since they have common enemies in the Sabbat, and the two aren't in conflict. Just enough so there is recognition on borders and what to do if there's trouble between vampires between them. And of course we know there are some very few Tzimisce in the Camarilla itself, but probably so few as to be negligible in influence.<br /> <br /> So it's never been the case that the Camarilla was actually only limited to 7 clans. It's just that only those seven clans actually had <i>influence enough to sit on the Inner Circle</i> and be politically important. The Assamites and Giovanni were heavily regulated and denied a spot at the table for a reason. The Setites could have been sitting on the Inner Circle, but didn't for plot purposes. But as the game got away from the idea that they were the Big Bad Guys of the setting in Revised, it made less and less sense that they wouldn't be members. And the only thing that prevented the Lasombra antitribu from having a seat at the Inner Circle was that there were just too few of them, but you could always change that in an organic way that still respected the setting. That really only left the Ravnos and Old Clan Tzimisce outside the system, mostly because they're numbers were small and they didn't organize among themselves.<br /> <br /> Now this isn't how the game actually developed once the Revised era was reached. At that point, any subtle relationships were ditched so the metaplot railroad could go move from station to station. The Treaty of Tyre and the Blood Curse was jettisoned, the Promise of 1528 seemed to not restrict Giovanni in any conceivable way begging the question of what was its purpose then, clans could begin willy nilly leave and join the Camarilla just by having one of its members say so. But in the actual core setting, we do have some inkling of the Camarilla fulfilling its potential as an actual worldwide conspiracy of vampires. In practice, the Justicars and archons are too few and not powerful enough to enforce everything they want. But there is certainly quite a number of vampires who at least theoretically accept the Camarilla's authority (in some capacity) despite their clan not being on the Inner Circle or having a Justicar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T00:34:35-07:00","id":1466751,"title":"","content":"Is survival still really an issue when you're centuries or even millenia old? Is it something you consider on a daily basis? Sure, you don't want to be obliterated, and you've probably become accustomed to your condition over time and grown fond of it, but survival is very much a notion to the frail - or those in a frail situation. Camarilla Elders are rarely in that category. Particularly not in modern nights.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I find the question interesting, as I'm running a Victorian Age campaign, where I have to find the main purpose for the Camarilla in a growing London with tons of new technology and innovations. In this setting I have made the Cam's main purpose to affect and in some cases control innovations and creations, so that it fits the Vampire world underneath. I don't see them as a sect or the UN (as suggested) - I simply see them as a group of Elders who're using old conventions as a mean to control younger vampires, who they use as pawns to further their goals. The Masquerade is still in effect, but where the younger vampires (who are often more frail) consider it a mean for survival and keeping the Sabbat at bay, the Elders mainly see it as a way to keep the younger vampires and possible intruders in check.<br /> <br /> But that's just one take on it, I guess.<br /> <br /> V","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;They do say, Mrs. M, that verbal insults hurt more than physical pain. They are of course wrong, as you will soon discover when I stick this toasting fork into your head.&quot;<br /> <br /> --E. Blackadder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24273-vincent","name":"Vincent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24273_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T01:37:50-07:00","id":1466755,"title":"","content":"Indeed, all clans and bloodlines are included in the Camarilla (bar maybe the ones with treaties, I don't know what's going on in there) Legaly speaking there's nothing to stop a Ravnos from becoming a Camarilla prince or Archon. The Camarilla claims to represent all vampires all over the world, at least on paper. <br /> However, most don't have much political representation at the higher level. And for the Clans that DO have political representation at a higher level, it's in their best interest to keep the status quo not only for their own possitions, but because yes, the other clans are destabilizing. <br /> <br /> The FOS are a corruption cult dedicated to bringing down the world. They also break the masquerade in front of their cult members in their acts of pretending to be Gods. <br /> <br /> Assamites are wanton diablerists with delusions of grandeur concerning their role as judges of law and order. Imagine being policed by people who want to eat you. (who ironically have dark skin that they believe marks them as a morally superior species) <br /> <br /> Ravnos are addicted to vice. While there are likely many cases where the vice isn't so disruptive, as a clan they're a massive liability. The vice addiction is also very likely responsible for the clan's adoption of paths that despise humanity; vice keeps them from reaching a high level of humanity, so they naturally reject it. <br /> <br /> Lasombra are very often:<br /> A: naturally drawn to religious extremes (The Abyss will put the fear of God into you) <br /> B: Low humanity assholes who lean in on Potence and Dominate. <br /> C: A walking masquerade breach without a reflection and no natural talent with obfuscate to make up for it. <br /> D: Far too competitive for an environment that values cooperation and stability. <br /> <br /> The Antitribu are OK because they're few in number, very selective, and largely pretend they're not Lasombra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T03:38:49-07:00","id":1466758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1466739#post1466739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Under <i>Our Mission Statement</i> in V5's guide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Despite my personal opinion on how the Cam changed in V5, this does highlights one important aspect the sect always had, that is its &quot;guidance&quot; of the mortal world.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla want a stable world, and that isn't just about safety, but also progress. And they understand that in this regard excessive depredation must be controlled, because Kindred prosperity derives from Human prosperity.<br /> <br /> Which comes first and if you see this as primary a moral or practical stand is besides the point. For the Camarilla the strength of society is paramount and the mortal side can't be ignored. Corruption is obviously accepted, as they are still hypocrites, but greater depredation must be tamed. After all a vampire only benefits from a herd that is healthy and can provide luxury.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1466746#post1466746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I make the distinction between the Camarilla as a global conspiracy that theoretically govern all vampires, and the clans that set on the Inner Circle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I like the <i>Camarilla as Compromise</i> more than the <i>Camarilla as Global Conspiracy</i>, but even keeping the later the notion of membership in it wasn't that straightforward before Revised.<br /> <br /> The history of membership is convoluted mostly due to Doylist decisions that had to be then justified from the Watsonian perspective against original intent. But even then, we're talking mostly about how <i>Clans</i> decide to react to them instead of how <i>the Cam</i> receives the clans.<br /> <br /> All the non-Camarilla clans are so because <i>they</i> decided that. Assamites and Giovanni chose to enter a pact to operate <i>in</i> a Prince's Domain but keep their clan business independent. Followers of Set just don't show up in any big event, but their individual members usually follow the rules of a Camarilla city they're in. Ravnos can't really answer as a clan outside India, period. Even the Sabbat clans just don't have enough numbers in the Camarilla, they're not <b>legally</b> regarded as Sabbat clans instead of Camarilla.<br /> <br /> You can picture this difference clearly in the <i>Promise</i>, despite it being a later development. At first it seems like the <i>Promise</i> is just the Camarilla imposing a limit on the Giovanni, but... actually, it is the pre-approval of their Embraces on a global level, so they can do so without asking (but of course informing) the local Prince. A Giovanni that decides to live full on as Camarilla don't need to follow the <i>Promise</i>. They just ask to the Prince like everyone else.<br /> <br /> None of those things apply to individuals. If any individual Kindred decides to just take part in Camarilla society, they follow the same rules and have the same rights as everyone else. Of course that things may not be simple in practical terms, but no actual rule or above-Prince decision keep them from achieving anything or occupying any position. You could have a city with a loyal Camarilla Tzimisce or Assamite Prince and that's that.<br /> <br /> Indeed this happens at Archon level. Justicars may nominate anyone they want as Archons and almost everything have some precedence here. Karl Schrekt, the Tremere Justicar that established many of the practices of the office and in the nomination of Archons already had a Setite under his command, so anything goes.<br /> <br /> Revised started to change things to railroad metaplot, and created the very notion of a clan leaving or joining the Camarilla. V5 fully embraced the idea. Of course this is all well for anyone who likes it, and makes a lot of sense if you think the Cam as a closed organization as the Sabbat is, which is good to emphasize sect conflicts. I personally don't like it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vincent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1466751#post1466751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is survival still really an issue when you're centuries or even millenia old?</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course it is, depending on how you define survival. The Camarilla makes safety a simpler issue for everyone, so even the Elder with the power to never have to worry about dying have the benefit of not having to devote any effort in this regard.<br /> <br /> Also, times change, hunting changes, wealth change, influence change. Keeping with this to protect your position and assets is also survival. It is just a more broad definition of survival, even if you don't worry about risks like Inquisitions and Diablerists. Which by lore most Elders do.<br /> <br /> There is also the simpler question of stated purpose vs practical use. I doubt the Camarilla in your game have the subjugation of neonates as its stated purpose even if the Elders use it that way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1466755#post1466755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's in their best interest to keep the status quo not only for their own possitions, but because yes, the other clans are destabilizing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I may talk about how I see the matter in more detail later, but for now I'll explain why I think this notion ridiculous.<br /> <br /> 1- The Followers are dealers, the end. Everything else is, <b>from an IC perspective</b>, just wild speculation, emphasis on wild.<br /> <br /> 2- Yes, their cults breach the Masquerade, but also contextualize this breach so their cultists are hardly in a position to do something. By the way, they're not bigger than your regular detachment of Blood Dolls and Ghouls, just more organized, which is actually good.<br /> <br /> 3- Pre-Revised Assamites can't diablerize, so that's not a point. Revised Assamites are mostly painted as more talk than actual action unless if they're crazy fanatics that won't join anyway.<br /> <br /> 4- Ravnos are a liability because they're addicted to vice? <b>Serious?</b> Brujah regularly frenzy, Ventrue can't vary their diet to cover their traces, Malkavians have self-control issues, Nosferatu can't show their ugly faces, Gangrel are full of telltale signs of supernatural influence, and <b>vices are a liability!?</b><br /> <br /> 5- Of all the checkbox in your Lasombra presentation, the Gangrel don't check the first, and I don't see why it is particularly a problem anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T06:38:52-07:00","id":1466766,"title":"","content":"I think Monteparnas has pretty much covered my view of the camarilla as a group of independent nations who've all agreed on a common rule set to get along.<br /> A common ruleset that provides some protection from mortals, but also protection from other kindred (including those claiming membership to the Cam).<br /> So I don't think that there is a central enough board to legislate any real goals, although I imagine there are plenty of elders who will tell you that they are in charge and have their own view on where things should go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25078-brickman","name":"Brickman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T07:31:44-07:00","id":1466771,"title":"","content":"1: Pretty easy to uncover the truth of that<br /> 2: &quot;Contextualize&quot;, like, who gives a damn about context when you're looking for pretence? A good chunk of the Cam's issues is how they over punish neonates on marginal masquerade violations to keep them in line. That doesn't work so well when you've got Thola Ram setting precedent.<br /> 3- &quot;They'll be fine, don't worry&quot; - The Second city.<br /> 4- Nosferatu have obfuscate, Ventrue control their backgrounds to perfection, malkavians get weird looks, Brujah don't leave witnesses (and are honestly a little too scary to punish too harshly). Ravnos get arrest warrants and blood hunts and it just doesn't do to ally with a clan of petty criminals. despite often living outside of cities, Gangrels are rarely nomads, they just keep farflung territories. Ravnos are nomads because they're on the run. That and the whole Path Of Paradox thing being extremely hostile to the Camarilla promotion of the Path of Humanity. Not to mention that, y'know, Prejudice and stereotypes will work to exaggerate a clan's flaws. <br /> (also the whole &quot;Ravnos are a big thing in India&quot; is pure writer fiat)<br /> 5: It's amazing how wrong you can be.<br /> B: Animalism isn't Dominate. Fortitude is quite a different attitude from Potence. The curse actually does a good job in keeping Gangrel more humane, given the beast has bigger consequences for them.<br /> C: No reflection is something you determine from miles away. Animal features are usually something you have to inspect the body for.<br /> D: Gangrel are honestly one of the least competitive clans out there so I don't know what the fuck you're talking about. Their modus operandi is literally &quot;Ok, you guys go compete for the rack, I'm going to hang in the areas you wouldn't be able to survive in&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T10:59:16-07:00","id":1466791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (also the whole &quot;Ravnos are a big thing in India&quot; is pure writer fiat) </div> </div> </div>The idea of the Ravnos being a big thing in India was an outright needed &quot;writer fiat&quot; as far as adding further culture and dimension to the Ravnos beyond the stereotypes they had existed and been used as previous to it, and frankly even V20 had itself started to do some interesting and evocative things with that in Beckett's Jyhad Diary before that plotline (and the clan) got re-exploded in V5, and there was interesting use of it in the DAV20 stuff besides.<br /> <br /> It was actually a really good example of changing things in VtM that added depth without having to blow anything up to facilitate that change. Not a lot had been done with India in VtM, so there was certainly room to maneuver to add details there and weave them into the overall setting. Revised edition took what was a seed of an idea in 2e, that the Ravnos had a depth of heritage, elders and the like in India that they'd become disconnected with, and worked it in a lot of ways to something viable and interesting, even if they coupled it with also blowing up the clan (though the dark ages line at the time, unhindered by the kerblooey, took those ideas further as far as exploring them and their implications and meaning in the Ravnos' Libellus book.)<br /> <br /> V20 then removing the week of nightmares further allowed those ideas to be explored and used. This was an interesting thing, and its functional removal, while one of the more relatively minor annoyances of V5, is one of the sadder regressions of V5 as far as &quot;let's make things as narrow and basic as possible&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 11-05-2021, 02:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T11:12:08-07:00","id":1466795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1466771#post1466771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1: Pretty easy to uncover the truth of that<br /> 2: &quot;Contextualize&quot;, like, who gives a damn about context when you're looking for pretence? A good chunk of the Cam's issues is how they over punish neonates on marginal masquerade violations to keep them in line. That doesn't work so well when you've got Thola Ram setting precedent.<br /> 3- &quot;They'll be fine, don't worry&quot; - The Second city.<br /> 4- Nosferatu have obfuscate, Ventrue control their backgrounds to perfection, malkavians get weird looks, Brujah don't leave witnesses (and are honestly a little too scary to punish too harshly). Ravnos get arrest warrants and blood hunts and it just doesn't do to ally with a clan of petty criminals. despite often living outside of cities, Gangrels are rarely nomads, they just keep farflung territories. Ravnos are nomads because they're on the run. That and the whole Path Of Paradox thing being extremely hostile to the Camarilla promotion of the Path of Humanity. Not to mention that, y'know, Prejudice and stereotypes will work to exaggerate a clan's flaws.<br /> (also the whole &quot;Ravnos are a big thing in India&quot; is pure writer fiat)<br /> <b>5: It's amazing how wrong you can be.</b><br /> B: Animalism isn't Dominate. Fortitude is quite a different attitude from Potence. The curse actually does a good job in keeping Gangrel more humane, given the beast has bigger consequences for them.<br /> C: No reflection is something you determine from miles away. Animal features are usually something you have to inspect the body for.<br /> D: Gangrel are honestly one of the least competitive clans out there so I don't know what the fuck you're talking about. Their modus operandi is literally &quot;Ok, you guys go compete for the rack, I'm going to hang in the areas you wouldn't be able to survive in&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>Don't be aggressive to fellow posters. </b></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T12:53:21-07:00","id":1466809,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> <br /> <br /> 1- Easy how? What steps can be taken in character that are both reasonable to begin with and likely to produce reliable evidence?<br /> <br /> 2 - You're reversing the order of things here, I'm asking why they would care and you're saying they don't need to care because they already want to. You still didn't answer the question: why they would care?<br /> <br /> 3 - The Second City is a mythical place from the Bronze Age. Please bring an actual argument.<br /> <br /> 4 - Still not making a point about any Ravnos who actually tried to join. Yes, they suffer prejudice. And yes, the game made them rarely care. A Ravnos that don't care, though, is already a criminal in the city, so it is pointless. Why would they want to refuse a Ravnos that actually tried?<br /> <br /> The Ravnos need to obfuscate what? In what controlling Backgrounds change the ease of finding the source of a weird anemia epidemic that only affect people with cockney accent? Witnesses of what, a con? I don't think <i>not leaving witnesses</i> is that good a cover up for every situation...<br /> <br /> Path of Paradox isn't something every Ravnos is required to have and isn't a bigger problem than any other Path the Camarilla had to deal with.<br /> <br /> You are, again, saying how they can justify not accepting the Ravnos and not answering why they would bother.<br /> <br /> (also, the whole VtM is pure writer fiat)<br /> <br /> 5 - <br /> B: Animalism isn't Dominate. Instead of erasing memories from witnesses it makes everyone in the city see animals behaving in very, <b>very</b> strange ways.<br /> <br /> Fortitude is quite a different attitude from Potence. Instead of lifting cars with one hand you survive car crashes with light bruises.<br /> <br /> <b>Protean, on the other hand</b>, is quite a freak fest. And living alone doesn't make a lot for your Humanity, either. I never saw that many Gangrel worried with being Humane or feign. Lasombra at least feign.<br /> <br /> C: No reflection is something you determine from <u><b>miles</b></u> away!?<br /> I don't know you, but I don't know many people that obsessively verify people's reflexes from a 10 meters distance, I can barely see a <b>person</b> half a kilometre away, much less if they're casting reflexes!<br /> <br /> You're being quite forceful in saying animal features are less noticeable than reflexes. Not to say that reflexes can be avoided simply by not standing next to mirrors.<br /> <br /> Of course, a vampire with no reflexes must adapt a lot of their lives to account for that. But so does vampires with most other weaknesses.<br /> <br /> D: Gangrel are as competitive when they are around as anyone else, but frequently with added fangs and claws in their way to settle things. How disruptive is that, especially if you consider that as much as they like outskirts, in the end they're feeding on humans like everyone else most of the time?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T12:04:17-07:00","id":1466969,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m coming a bit late although I do think that leaving aside the Masquerade as a given alongside general survival does it\u2019s importance as a mission statement some disservice.<br /> <br /> [*Disclaimer: most of my understanding is based on pre-V5 lore so YMMV as far as V5 is concerned]<br /> <br /> [**Disclaimer II: This post does not take into account any other gamelines]<br /> <br /> The Masquerade is best understood as both a passive and active goal imo. Obviously the passive is very important in that breaches need to be covered to prevent individual vampires from being found out or vampiric society as a whole being revealed.<br /> <br /> I do think though that if you look at the Masquerade as an active goal of the Camarilla it gives an insight into the mindset of the elders and the sect\u2019s goals. <br /> <br /> The founders of the Camarilla touted the Masquerade as a banner for vampirdom to rally behind. All the elders of Christendom were wary of ceding any of their hard won and maintained power but circumstances were truly desperate. Warfare, plague, and general calamity had devastated the mortals and so the hunting fields had been winnowed while a sense of apocalyptic hysteria was in the air. The Inquisition represented both the reaction of the mortal institutions of Christendom against the chaos of the time and vampires would be on the block as a cause, but even more then the Papacy\u2019s desperate efforts to restore order the general populace feared that the Time of Judgement was near at hand. A desperate and zealous people were relatively easy to provoke into either revolt or monster hunting - after all their souls would surely be redeemed if they lost their lives pursuing the destruction of demonic forces. This environment would have been bad enough if it were the mortals alone in tumult but the young had risen up in revolt against their elders because of these material circumstances and violence tore through every clan in Christendom. To the Noddists it would have been one more sign that the promised reckoning of Gehenna was near at hand.<br /> <br /> It was in this environment of fear and desperation that the elders were susceptible to a revolutionary proposal. The Founders of the Camarilla provided that proposal and the Masquerade would be a linch pin for their argument: these catastrophes had happened because vampires had rejected ancient wisdom and exposed themselves to the Children of Seth. If there was ever to be peace again then every kindred vampire needed to unite their power to hide themselves from humanity. They would have to guide from the shadows, lest they one day be totally destroyed. It would require not only a confederacy of elders to accomplish this but a centralized body with the power to enforce the Masquerade and the other necessary traditions for ensuring peace. Enough elders were convinced and so the Camarilla was born.<br /> <br /> In the centuries since the Camarilla formed the Masquerade was the central focus: not only as a passive mandate but in active measures. The Camarilla had a vested interest in supporting every possible measure which would not only hide individual vampires from the herds but would persuade humanity that vampires did not exist at all. Supporting the Protestant Reformation would be critical to undermining the power of the Catholic Church in Christendom - one organization so vested in the mystical world that it would be effectively impossible to remove belief in demons and vampires from them. They supported the rise of the Italian Renaissance, which also formed the basis for much of the tradition Camarilla social system. Humanism, Rationalism, Enlightenment, and the Scientific Revolution. Every one of these received support from the gestalt resources of the Camarilla so that they could succeed.<br /> <br /> The goals of the Camarilla hasn\u2019t changed. It benefits them to bankroll a world without any place for the mystical or unnatural. So they continue to dedicate resources into actively creating a world governed by philosophies which reject even the remotest possibilities of their existence.<br /> <br /> I think that through the lenses of the Masquerade you can learn a great deal about the mind of the Camarilla and what motivates it to act tonight as much as it motivated it to act before. The Camarilla has always been a gothic allegory for institutions of power and the Masquerade provides a key part of the explanation for why it invests as actively as it does in those institutions of power to these very nights.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T00:14:31-07:00","id":1467018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1466809#post1466809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a><br /> Woosh</div> </div> </div> </div>I think your arguments here are pretty weak, but the main issue is you're overestimating how much I think the Camarilla doesn't like minority clans. You're thinking Jews in Nazi Germany, I'm just thinking blacks in the USA (with lots of regional/time period variations depending on local attitudes) You don't need infallible arguments to justify systemic prejudice, you just need enough of an argument to convince people that don't know better, and Vampires live in a lot of ignorance while also benefiting from any environment that squeezes out competition: Lasombra consider themselves direct competitors to Ventrue, why would Ventrue want them around? (honestly, I think the Lasombra are really more in competition with Brujah, and V5 seems to think so too. Why would Brujah want Lasombra around?) <br /> <br /> Harsher sentences and biased rulings, devalued prestation, lower rewards, subpar domains, no permision to embrace, Trigger happy sherrifs... Nobody's openly ruling that all Ravnos must die, but if they can find an excuse, they'll likely to use it. Of course, if your city has an uncommonly powerful minority (Try hate on Lasombra in Montano's city) or the minority has a great relationship with a well established clan (Samedi-Nosferatu, Gargoyle-Tremere) then things are fine for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T01:49:50-08:00","id":1467028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467018#post1467018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think your arguments here are pretty weak</div> </div> </div> </div>It's reciprocated, but besides the point.<br /> <br /> You're the one making the statement that the non-OG clans are destabilizing, you're the one who have to offer argument for your thesis.<br /> <br /> Calling my arguments weak doesn't change that you're refusing to engage with the examination of the thesis instead of defending it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467018#post1467018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but the main issue is you're overestimating how much I think the Camarilla doesn't like minority clans.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the main issue is that you didn't understood my question at all.<br /> <br /> What I don't believe is that the Camarilla have particularly more prejudice against those clans than they have against many already present among the OG-7.<br /> <br /> You don't have to explain to me how systemic prejudice works, I know. But I'm not convinced that the other clans suffer more systemic prejudice than Nosferatu, Malkavian, Brujah or Gangrel.<br /> <br /> I'm also not convinced that systemic prejudice would be enough to keep the other clans outside the Camarilla instead of &quot;just&quot; heavily weakened, or that it would even be so systemic with all the OG-7 comprising this system, as I'm not convinced that they would share such prejudices.<br /> <br /> But above all, I'm not convinced of your original thesis. Because you're pretty much changing goal posts here. You didn't talked about systemic prejudice, you said the listed clans are destabilizing. I don't see it beyond a pretty narrow view of them and willfully ignoring what the OG-7 already do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T10:41:32-08:00","id":1467072,"title":"","content":"(post might need a little work I needed to finish in a rush) <br /> <br /> Ok<br /> The Assamites are currently addicted to Diablerie. And when they were under the Tremere curse, it was only a matter of time. A bloodline that looks at the other clans like a buffet is a massive danger. The Assamites are also very specialized within their caste system: Warriors are Warriors, and if they're not doing Warrior things, they're essentially betraying their caste. You really don't want a Diablerie addict as a sherrif though, and an Assassin? That's not something a civilized society like the Camarilla should have around. . The greatest issue with Assamites is that because they're so extremely specialized they've learnt to be interdependent on the other Assamite Castes. Assamites essentially form highly insular cells that set them apart from the other kindred (which, y'know, the Tremere do, but the Tremere aren't A clan of <s>Diablerists</s> warriors)<br /> Viziers require intense scrutiny to really be seperated from warriors, the kind of intense scrutiny vampires really don't like. And Viziers also offer convenient bases for warriors so... not a great idea to give them free reign.<br /> <br /> The Lasombra have a well deserved reputation as complete and utter bastards. They're far too competitive. Far too cruel to the kine. Far too likely to get religious in a sect that promotes being secular, and Obtenebration is some really shady stuff. What function would the Lasombra provide for the Cam that another clan can't do better? Nothing*. What harm could they do? Quite a lot.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ravnos? Jesus fuck where do I even begin? This is a clan of evil shapeshifting clowns (And I love them, they're one of my favourites)<br /> 1: If the vice is bad, and it is, it's a vice, it'll get you in a whole load of trouble, or it'll make you profilic, or it'll put you at odds with humanity. Think about it, Imagine you can't even keep humanity 6 because you've just got to steal. Even if you're skilled and never get caught, you just can't get to humanity 7. You can't be <i>normal</i>. You are <i>cursed </i>to steal. Now imagine how that feels in a sect that hypocritically touts good morals and humanity. Oh sure they don't mean it, but everyone but you can achieve high humanity, and they know it. Everyone else has a choice, but you're a natural degenerate. Imagine how that shapes everyone's attitude towards you. Imagine how that shapes your attititude towards them. And yeah, this is only theft. There's so many more serious vices to be concerned about. It's completely-fucking-natural that the majority of Ravnos reject humanity. And a good chunk of vices are exploitable. Gambling addiction? The Camarilla will milk you.<br /> (also, Chimistry is philosophically interesting, and puts you in the same gravity for religious nuttery as the Lasombra)<br /> <br /> Giovanni? Actually not really bad at all, minus the whole corpse-fucking shtick they've got going on. But the whole capadocian genocide is too dangerous a precedent.<br /> FoS: at the very least, it's a kindred religion, and it sets precedent for all those Gehenna cults the Cam doesn't want. All that dark hidden lore is unwelcome in polite society.<br /> <br /> Of the OG 7 clans. The Brujah are by far the most destabilizing, beating the runner up (probably the Toreador) by leaps and bounds.<br /> Tremere, Ventrue, Nosferatu and Gangrel are all very pro-stablility clans. Malks might stray from the path, but historically have been one of the cam's strongest supporters. Toreador do FA for their neonates and cause a lot of petty disputes, pushing many to anarch status.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Brujah have one huge advantage over other the trouble clans.<br /> They're easy to make, there's a fucking lot of them, and they're scary.<br /> Ravnos and Tzmisce are loners. Lasombra don't work well together, Assamites are interdependent with their caste system and work in small teams that one can collectively target. The Brujah are an army. You can Target one, but you can't target the clan. It's a pyrrhic uphill battle.<br /> The Brujah are also a clan that greatly benefit from maturity. They're stereotyped as thugs because some of the clan are really loud about it, but they're disparate enough that a lot of them are probably low key and hardly distinguishable from any other Camarilla vampire. The Jyhad kills the stupid and thus with age, an Older Brujah is more likely to be your friend and ally, while an Elder from one of the outsider clans is simply the same guy, more dangerous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T12:13:32-08:00","id":1467084,"title":"","content":"So, some things. As far as the Lasombra and the Tzimisce to start with, the whole point of the Convention of Thorns was that the proto Camarilla did in fact want a whole bunch of clans around, as many of them as possible (barring really the Setites), and that two of those clans in particular went &quot;go fuck yourself&quot; in response to that and rallied what was left of the Anarchs who didn't surrender to become the Sabbat. The Assamites refused to join and thus had the Treaty of Tyre functionally imposed on them instead for being in a far more compromised position than the Lasombra and Tzimisce (i.e. terrified that Alamut had been compromised/was on the verge of being compromised depending on what edition it is, and also the Tremere getting together to throw the blood curse down).<br /> <br /> The Camarilla has always been desirous of folding in as many clans as they officially can. Witness how in revised the only people who really objected to the Schismatic Assamites being folded in were the Tremere, and they did it out of blood sorcery jealousy/fear of revenge getting taken upon them. And that said Schismatics in Revised otherwise folded in fine really, to the point that Tegyrius was getting nascently floated around as a name for justicar.<br /> <br /> In V20, one of the last plot developments with the Ravnos that was interesting before V5 decided &quot;naaah, explosions! explosions Ravnos for one thousand years!&quot; was that they *were* starting to join the Camarilla in numbers, and finding themselves in positions like primogen and the like. That while there were certainly exceptions because grudges and prejudices do exist within the Camarilla, the Camarilla as a whole was starting to go &quot;eh, sure, why not.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Lasombra have a well deserved reputation as complete and utter bastards. They're far too competitive. Far too cruel to the kine. Far too likely to get religious in a sect that promotes being secular, and Obtenebration is some really shady stuff. What function would the Lasombra provide for the Cam that another clan can't do better? Nothing*. What harm could they do? Quite a lot. </div> </div> </div>A healthy majority of the clans are complete and utter bastards and have well deserved reputations for such. The game is a game about vampires. But setting that aside... Again, the goal of the Camarilla at Thorns was to fold clans like the Lasombra, into the Camarilla. At that, for all this attempted line of reasoning, the Camarilla lets in the Lasombra antitribu just fine. One of the most respected and valued members of the Victorian London Camarilla court, basically the most powerful Camarilla city in the world at the time, was indeed, a Lasombra antitribu. Who was so valued vampires of other clans would go out of their way to kill the living hell out of Sabbat that tried to come for him.<br /> <br /> As for &quot;what would the Lasombra bring to the Camarilla?&quot; The Lasombra being part of the Camarilla would let the Camarilla have that much more support for their claim of universality. Every clan that joins the Camarilla lets the Camarilla make itself look inevitable and inexorable, to the point that something had to be as outre as the Followers of Set for the nascent sect to go &quot;Ew, no to that&quot;. The idea that the Camarilla, pre v5 do not value every chance they get to further support proclaiming themselves the defining overstate of being a vampire, doesn't jive with the Camarilla. Part of how the Camarilla wanted to enforce peace in a post Thorns world was by the idea of &quot;y'all are now either Camarilla, or acknowledge its authority by some other way.&quot; The only reason the Lasombra did not join the Camarilla at Thorns was the choice of the Lasombra themselves to proclaim &quot;eat a dick&quot; (which the Tzimisce decided to proclaim to the Camarilla much more literally).<br /> <br /> But since the premise of your arguments is not to let actual setting writing get in the way of them (I know, I know &quot;writer fiat&quot;), I guess let's move on from there..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and an Assassin? That's not something a civilized society like the Camarilla should have around. . </div> </div> </div>The Camarilla has a healthy proportion of people whose unlife is made up of functionally murdering some other vampire for hire, or, if they have a title to go along with that capacity, murder someone else on official command. Most vampire combat as preferred by the Camarilla, if they can't get it done by day raiding ghouls or indirect influence, is to assassinate their enemies by unfair ambush and other skullduggery. The Camarilla (kinda rightfully) considers having to get into a direct straight fight to be a sign that all other options have failed/they managed to get maneuvered into having to direct straight fight. &quot;Assassin&quot; is just putting a label on practices the Camarilla itself gets up to, a lot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Brujah have one huge advantage over other the trouble clans.<br /> They're easy to make, there's a fucking lot of them, and they're scary. </div> </div> </div>This didn't stop the huge chunk of Anarch Brujah from being on the losing side of the first anarch revolt, somehow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can Target one, but you can't target the clan. It's a pyrrhic uphill battle. </div> </div> </div>See First Anarch revolt. They started strong as a sizable group. They lost such that chunks of their own clan ended up being a founding clan for seeing which way the wind was blowing/the Brujah who didn't go anarch being the winning side.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Brujah are an army. </div> </div> </div>No, certainly not pre V5. They aren't in any grand larger organized sense. They're in many ways the furthest thing from an army because as clans go, they're themselves pretty fractious as far as splits between old and young, anarch and camarilla, rabble and philosopher, and in general the way many brujah will react to another brujah attempting to assert authority over them. As far as what passes for a clan culture goes, it is in many ways easier for a given brujah to grudgingly submit to an authority from outside their clan, than one within their clan because the first thing that gets lobbied pretty frequently at a brujah trying to assert themselves over other brujah is &quot;you fucking sellout.&quot; This was canonically, pre V5, what drove Tara for example to join the Camarilla, her own clan in the city preferring to let San Diego be unmanageable chaos rather than acknowledge structure from a Brujah onto other Brujah. It's one of the particular flaws and weak points of the clan.<br /> <br /> Also, your rationale here is extremely thin besides because &quot;scary so the Camarilla lets it go&quot; could be flipped onto any other clan you're trying to claim &quot;The Camarilla would not let it go&quot; over. You seem to want to ignore the implications of your own logic, such as it is.<br /> <br /> The Ravnos, for example, are also scary, ask any city that has suffered the Treatment. Which while we're there is one of the things that kept such prejudice against them as might be, from getting entirely out of hand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ravnos? Jesus fuck where do I even begin? This is a clan of evil shapeshifting clowns (And I love them, they're one of my favourites)<br /> 1: If the vice is bad, and it is, it's a vice, it'll get you in a whole load of trouble, or it'll make you profilic, or it'll put you at odds with humanity. Think about it, Imagine you can't even keep humanity 6 because you've just got to steal. Even if you're skilled and never get caught, you just can't get to humanity 7. You can't be <i>normal</i>. You are <i>cursed </i>to steal. Now imagine how that feels in a sect that hypocritically touts good morals and humanity. Oh sure they don't mean it, but everyone but you can achieve high humanity, and they know it. Everyone else has a choice, but you're a natural degenerate. Imagine how that shapes everyone's attitude towards you. Imagine how that shapes your attititude towards them. And yeah, this is only theft. There's so many more serious vices to be concerned about. It's completely-fucking-natural that the majority of Ravnos reject humanity. And a good chunk of vices are exploitable. Gambling addiction? The Camarilla will milk you.<br /> (also, Chimistry is philosophically interesting, and puts you in the same gravity for religious nuttery as the Lasombra) </div> </div> </div>You can pretty much switch in Ventrue with really bad/extreme feeding restrictions for this attempted line of narrative and logic, and yet somehow the Ventrue manage to both manage themselves and function. If it was this regularly bad for the Ravnos as you claim just to exist, if that many of them had a *really* bad vice instead of, for example, shit like plagiarism (actual canon npc vice example), they would not be able to have kept existing as a clan (and the only thing that kept them from doing that in the end was getting exploded). You seem to want to exaggerate the state of the Ravnos (odd for a guy talking about them being one of his favourites) while ignoring how that can get flipped on to almost any other clan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but they're disparate enough that a lot of them are probably low key and hardly distinguishable from any other Camarilla vampire. </div> </div> </div>I'd like you to try and take a step back and examine that your arguments boil down to &quot;look at this clan and the most extreme reading on them possible that the entire clan should be defined by.&quot; and then at the same time &quot;but it would be incorrect to define the Brujah by the most extreme reading of them&quot;<br /> <br /> There is a very sizable amount of double standards and contradictions in your attempted arguments, just to have them exist. And no, I don't mean &quot;well the Camarilla has tons of double standards&quot; which I feel like is what you would try to defend this by, I mean your posts. The foundational logic in them seems to unavoidably rest in going &quot;I get to define this clan in the worst way possible while saying this clan should not be defined in the worst way possible, even though by my logic, it totally could be.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 11-07-2021, 03:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T12:15:12-08:00","id":1467085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467072#post1467072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(post might need a little work I needed to finish in a rush)<br /> <br /> Ok<br /> The Assamites are currently addicted to Diablerie. And when they were under the Tremere curse, it was only a matter of time. A bloodline that looks at the other clans like a buffet is a massive danger. The Assamites are also very specialized within their caste system: Warriors are Warriors, and if they're not doing Warrior things, they're essentially betraying their caste. You really don't want a Diablerie addict as a sherrif though, and an Assassin? That's not something a civilized society like the Camarilla should have around.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Banu Haqim are more than diablerie addicts, they wouldn't be a major part of the Ashirra if they were so, and it is a civilized society as much as the Camarilla. They aren't that dependent on different castes as well. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467072#post1467072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lasombra have a well deserved reputation as complete and utter bastards. They're far too competitive. Far too cruel to the kine. Far too likely to get religious in a sect that promotes being secular, and Obtenebration is some really shady stuff. What function would the Lasombra provide for the Cam that another clan can't do better? Nothing*. What harm could they do? Quite a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since when does the Camarilla cares about cruelty to kine? A Toreador can be as cruel to a ghoul they grew bored, or a Ventrue to a servant that failed them. They also aren't generally drawn to religion out of actual faith, but opportunism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467072#post1467072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Brujah have one huge advantage over other the trouble clans. ... The Jyhad kills the stupid and thus with age, an Older Brujah is more likely to be your friend and ally, while an Elder from one of the outsider clans is simply the same guy, more dangerous.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Brujah get this benefit of the doubt, yet the Banu Haqim are slaves to their Bane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T12:18:55-08:00","id":1467088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lasombra have a well deserved reputation as complete and utter bastards. They're far too competitive. Far too cruel to the kine. Far too likely to get religious in a sect that promotes being secular, and Obtenebration is some really shady stuff. What function would the Lasombra provide for the Cam that another clan can't do better? Nothing*. What harm could they do? Quite a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chicago by Night says the Lasombra have extensive influence in the church and other areas that can be used against the Second Inquisition. Also, that they are an addition of an additional Clan of bodies when the Ivory Tower is lacking them. But the greatest benefit of the Lasombra is for every defection, their enemies go down by two while their allies go up by one. Every Lasombra working for the Ivory tower is one less working for the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Even vampires understand the importance of peace making...sometimes.<br /> <br /> As for being too cruel to kine, that attitude among the Camarilla is more like, &quot;Stop playing with your food, Carmelita. Its unbecoming.&quot; Not genuine revulsion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of the OG 7 clans. The Brujah are by far the most destabilizing, beating the runner up (probably the Toreador) by leaps and bounds.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Toreador are the most destabilizing but also the most stabilizing. Vampire culture does not exist without them as no one would piss on another vampire if they were on fire, generally, unless they were the same Clan and that's only the Nosferatu or Tremere. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The Toreador have made the idea they should all sit together drinking vitae from glasses and listen to the Harpies gossip.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Assamites are currently addicted to Diablerie. And when they were under the Tremere curse, it was only a matter of time. A bloodline that looks at the other clans like a buffet is a massive danger. The Assamites are also very specialized within their caste system: Warriors are Warriors, and if they're not doing Warrior things, they're essentially betraying their caste. You really don't want a Diablerie addict as a sherrif though, and an Assassin? That's not something a civilized society like the Camarilla should have around. . The greatest issue with Assamites is that because they're so extremely specialized they've learnt to be interdependent on the other Assamite Castes. Assamites essentially form highly insular cells that set them apart from the other kindred (which, y'know, the Tremere do, but the Tremere aren't A clan of Diablerists warriors)<br /> <br /> Viziers require intense scrutiny to really be seperated from warriors, the kind of intense scrutiny vampires really don't like. And Viziers also offer convenient bases for warriors so... not a great idea to give them free reign.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, you're describing the Web of Knives versus the Assamites as a whole. The Web of Knives has also become the Shepherds of Ur-Shulgi and they are at war with every other Kindred in the world right now, which is not a great thing to be as the Sabbat are entirely capable of taking that fight. The rest of the Banu Haqim are quite willing to sit down in Elysium to shoot the shit like other Harpies.<br /> <br /> As for their addiction to vitae, I'm pretty sure the only thing they need to do there is not ever try to share blood with them. Otherwise, they're not going to be diablerists at Elysium.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-07-2021, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T13:05:05-08:00","id":1467099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467072#post1467072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(post might need a little work I needed to finish in a rush)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll keep that in mind.<br /> <br /> <br /> Before the Tremere Curse was lifted there was no reason to think it was a matter of time. And even before it was a thing the Assamites had a history as not being as different from other vampires despite their beliefs.<br /> <br /> So much so that they worked just fine with the Ashirra, no greater concerns whatsoever. Actually, the Assamites' greater concern for the well being of mortals would be of great interest to the Camarilla, as it is to the Ashirra.<br /> <br /> <br /> Lasombra not only aren't universally as competitive as to be dumb, neither as badly seen by the Camarilla, that they actually got recognized as a Cam Clan of sorts through their <i>Antitribu</i>, and their eldest Methuselah is in the sect.<br /> <br /> Their tendencies to being over-competitive and cruel, and to be religious, are also overplayed. They're not a cultural monolith and they're usually not dumb, being perfectly capable of understanding the notion of compromise. They wouldn't be as successful if they couldn't control their impulses at least.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ravnos suffer from completely human compulsions, even if you go by their classic weakness. You can't be less generally disruptive than that. They're addicted to completely normal behavior and have a reasonable chance to resist it in any particular opportunity.<br /> <br /> Of course, it is even better with the V20 variation, but it can't be compared with propensity for frenzy and risk of random manic episodes, for example. It's a huge exaggeration to say they're naturally more disruptive than anyone else.<br /> <br /> Even more of a problem when you consider that their typical behaviors are actually old authors having quite a racist view on Gipsies, especially Roma. What they did with the Ravnos in India as &quot;author fiat&quot; is actually taking one of the most simplistic and cartoonish stereotypes in the game and making something that actually makes sense. So instead of dismissing that version, I personally think it far more useful to dive in it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Giovanni don't have a more dangerous precedent than the Tremere, pure and simple. They were known diablerists even before locking target on the Salubri, and the other clans knew it. In fact, they were far worst criminals than the Assamites were under just the Baali Curse.<br /> <br /> <br /> Followers are business first among the Kindred, to emphasize so much their cults is to ignore that they keep those cults low profile. That, again, if you even assume that every FoS is literally a cultist, or that everyone take their name at face value.<br /> <br /> Your typical FoS lore isn't widespread knowledge. They keep their actual religion to themselves unless they find a suitable target, and even then it is pretty tame compared to some other things that happen at the hands of other clans. Their main thing, beyond having a true and tested system for keeping Blood Dolls and Ghouls, is to work as dealers for others.<br /> <br /> <br /> While we're at that, look at most OG clans weaknesses and typical behaviors. I particularly don't see the Gangrel even <i>pretending</i> to be pro-stability as a clan. Malks couldn't be if they wanted, again, not as a clan. Nosferatu actively blackmail others regularly, and Brujah are prone the worst possible vice in terms of keeping the Masquerade, as a Kindred in Frenzy is simply going for a basic and quite obvious display of power. The Ventrue weakness makes for a trail that's too obvious after a time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T13:24:01-08:00","id":1467101,"title":"","content":"I always tend to view the Lasombra as a contrast to the Followers of Set. The Lasombra generally view religion through the lens of an opiate of the masses and a tool to control the weak-minded. There's some genuinely religious super-Catholics and people who worship the Stygian abyss but the majority of them are con men and shysters holding out their hat for the Lord. Which is part of the reason that I had no difficulty buying the defection as I assumed it was them realizing that the mob was now expecting them to drink the Kool-Aid the same as them.<br /> <br /> The Followers of Set, by contrast, are WEIRD by Kindred cult leader standards as virtually all of them genuinely believe in what they're teaching and are willing to sacrifice for it. There's a bunch of people genuinely shocked at the fact their fellow Followers believe this bullshit but probably the same ratio inverse to the Lasombra true believers.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T22:07:27-08:00","id":1467153,"title":"","content":"The disconnect, I think, is that y'all think I'm exaggerating the worst of the other clans and understating the excesses of the Camarilla clan, creating unfair caricatures<br /> I am doing that in stride.<br /> Vampires aren't an enlightened people. Most Vampires believe what their sire tells them, and their sire isn't going to tell them anything that's against the best interest of the sire which usually means they won't tell the childe anything that goes against the values of the sect. Smart vampires might have doubts, but they're probably smart enough not to ask too much.<br /> <br /> Giovanni destroyed the Capadoccians? <i>Those Giovanni are monsters</i><br /> <i>T</i>remere destroyed the Salubri (if it even gets brought up) <i>The Salubri were monsters that deserved it. </i><br /> <br /> Your average Camarilla neonate will be exposed to the OG 7, but not the other clans. Even in the Sabbat, you probably don't have all the exotic clan flavours in your area (nevermind bloodlines) Thus your vampire will know the reality of Brujah, but only the legend of Ravnos. And people tend to focus on differences more than similarities. Assamites, The Ravnos weakness or Settite dogma can become sensational topics and there isn't likely to be an Assamite/Ravnos or Settite around to fix the misconceptions. If anything, there's more likely going to be an enemy of these clans adding spice to the mix.<br /> <br /> Perception is more important than reality in this case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can pretty much switch in Ventrue with really bad/extreme feeding restrictions for this attempted line of narrative and logic, and yet somehow the Ventrue manage to both manage themselves and function. If it was this regularly bad for the Ravnos as you claim just to exist, if that many of them had a *really* bad vice instead of, for example, shit like plagiarism (actual canon npc vice example </div> </div> </div>\u200bPlagiarism is the Ravnos equivalent of a Shanghai Ventrue being restricted to Chinese blood. Weak. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I always tend to view the Lasombra as a contrast to the Followers of Set. </div> </div> </div>In the sense that Settites have a CE religion and Lasombra gravitate towards LE religions with a big hierarchical focus?<br /> True believers or not? Well. Settites are garanteed to start off as cult members. Lasombra are scared into faith by the INFINITE DARKNESS.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, you're describing the Web of Knives versus the Assamites as a whole. </div> </div> </div>No, the Assamites as a whole have used a structure of close knit interdependent cells with Viziers bankrolling and managing the logistics of warriors and the ocassional sorcerer. They annoyingly used an arabic word for it so I forgot what it was called. To my knowledge The Web of Knives only differs in training and attitude and otherwise integrates well with the rest of the loyalist population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 11-08-2021, 01:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T22:36:06-08:00","id":1467155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Perception is more important than reality in this case. </div> </div> </div>You have multiple paragraphs where you talk about the extreme perception being the reality for the clans in question as far as their viablity/disruptiveness and this is some very late stage goal post shifting to instead say you only ever meant you were saying what vampires would think about these clans. You have multiple attempts to speak about these things as objective detail, to the point of attempting to make what come off as objective contrast to how other clans function, to the point of multiple posters quoting you doing so, and it really muddies the idea of participating in some discussion with you on these things if you're at a point of seeming to want to retcon your own posts.<br /> <br /> The &quot;disconnect&quot; comes of multiple people reading the content of your posts and responding to them based on what they said, not what you now say they mean. Otherwise if you are baffled that numerous posters are responding to your posts in a particular way you wish that they were not, then you are left with having to consider that your posts to this point have been poorly phrased for any possible meaning salvaged from them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampires aren't an enlightened people. Most Vampires believe what their sire tells them, and their sire isn't going to tell them anything that's against the best interest of the sire which usually means they won't tell the childe anything that goes against the values of the sect. Smart vampires might have doubts, but they're probably smart enough not to ask too much. </div> </div> </div>They won't tell the childe anything that goes against the values of the sect that, again, specifically wants to view itself as ecumenical over all vampires and fold in as many clans as it can, and indeed tried to do so at its founding?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If anything, there's more likely going to be an enemy of these clans adding spice to the mix. </div> </div> </div>The actual setting material disagrees with you as far as the impact you think this has. Ravnos were joining the Camarilla just fine as a potential plot thread in V20 in BJD, the only thing that stopped that going further was the Week of Nightmares being recanonized in V5.<br /> <br /> The actual setting material disagrees with you as far as the impact you think this has. The Schismatic Assamites joined the Camarilla in revised just fine and the only people that especially raised a stink about it as a bloc (and failed to get much traction, since the schismatic Assamites joined the Camarilla in revised despite this) were the Tremere.<br /> <br /> Both examples from different editions without even having to dip into something like V5 as far as clans getting into the Camarilla that you claim would/should never get into the Camarilla due to the perspectives of the Camarilla (and/or an effort to argue how infeasible those clans would be from a standpoint of mechanics/discipline spreads/their own attitudes, but you now seem to want to walk that back as &quot;things vampires would say&quot;). The game simply disagrees with you. Repeatedly. In at this point three different editions of said game.<br /> <br /> Thereby, what remains of your point here? That you dislike Revised, V20 and V5 alike for not particularly putting a lot of weight on the way you want the game to be working? I mean, feel free to dislike these incarnations of the game, hey, I think V5 is a disaster area, but it doesn't change that you are saying one thing, and the actual game is saying something else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plagiarism is the Ravnos equivalent of a Shanghai Ventrue being restricted to Chinese blood. </div> </div> </div>That your response to actual content of the game Vampire the Masquerade, in the face of how you instead seem to wish the content of the game Vampire the Masquerade works, seems to be to ignore or dismiss it (&quot;writer fiat&quot;) would make it helpful if you would start tagging or titling your posts with some acknowledgement that you're not in any way talking about published VtM material, but rather how you wish the game worked and was defined. The confusion for the rest of us is we keep thinking we are discussing the game, Vampire the Masquerade as based on the content that exists for it to use as a basis to then go forward in discussion with.<br /> <br /> You attempted to make an argument about how crippling, extreme and disruptive the Ravnos clan flaw makes them. It would thereby seem like a valid point to make in the face of that argument would be that there are any number of canonical npc Ravnos who have vices less extreme and or that consume them in a less extreme fashion than you want them to have.<br /> <br /> But really, why even gripe about this particular, once again, canonical detail? According to you as it stands, you were only ever talking about the inaccurate, prejudicial perspectives of other vampires in any event. Not that you felt that it should be functionally impossible for the Ravnos to join the Camarilla due to how disruptive and exploitable their clan mechanics make them. And similar takes thus on the Lasombra, Assamites, so forth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":"yes yes, irony) 11-08-2021, 01:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T06:18:12-08:00","id":1467160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467155#post1467155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The confusion for the rest of us is we keep thinking we are discussing the game, Vampire the Masquerade as based on the content that exists for it to use as a basis to then go forward in discussion with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I detest this &quot;the rest of us&quot; argument. It is isolating. Nothing personal, just a bugbear of mine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T08:13:49-08:00","id":1467165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467153#post1467153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The disconnect, I think,</div> </div> </div> </div>No. The disconnect is that you refuse to engage in the same conversation as others.<br /> <br /> You clearly think the Camarilla <i>should</i> keep the other clans outside and it is how you run things. That's fine, no one here said you can't have your table your way. But you're not satisfied with that, you're constantly trying to sell your view as A) the only intelligent one, B) the only we should talk about and C) the only that could be correct. To the point that you refuse to engage even with canon when it goes against your view.<br /> <br /> The thread's title is <b>What goals do the Camarilla have?</b> You said one of those goals is to keep &quot;undesirables&quot; outside the sect. <b>Why?</b> This is the question you failed to answer, now pretends to not be there. <b>Does it, really?</b> You're the only one arguing it does, <b>defend your thesis.</b><br /> <br /> Stop changing goal posts, stop ridiculing others' opinions, stop ignoring what other people or the <b><i>actual books</i></b> say, just defend your thesis if you can, by its merits and engaging with others' arguments, without trying to make everyone that disagrees with you seems dumb so you can pretend to be the only smart person in the room.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467153#post1467153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most Vampires believe what their sire tells them,</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt. Can you back it up? Will you even try?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467153#post1467153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bPlagiarism is the Ravnos equivalent of a Shanghai Ventrue being restricted to Chinese blood. Weak.</div> </div> </div> </div>You not liking a possibility because you don't think it's fun enough for your game doesn't make it impossible, unlikely, or unfun for everyone else.<br /> <br /> A Ravnos may have a compulsion to steal. Or may have a compulsion to pick their nose in public. <b>Live with that</b>, nothing in the book ever said if one is more or less likely than the other.<br /> <br /> Oh, but the book <b>did said</b> that, on a second thought, now a Ravnos may have a compulsion to brew soup for the poor once a night, <i>and this is a retcon, so they were always like that</i>. You don't like the retcon? Fine. But you can't forbid other from liking and running it. <b><i>Or say it is less canon just because you don't like it</i></b>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467153#post1467153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lasombra are scared into faith by the INFINITE DARKNESS.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except this is not a rule. No Lasombra is required to understand the Abyss in the same way, <b><i>or even to personally have Obtenebration</i></b>.<br /> <br /> So if a given Lasombra just think they access the Dimension of Scary Giant Black Blob, that's it. Not everyone worship things that make them scared.<br /> <br /> Quite the opposite, as despite horror movies having legions of fans, it is Star Wars the one that started an actual religion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T08:45:07-08:00","id":1467169,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Guys, please lower the hostility. If you have issues with other posters please report them.</span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T10:51:46-08:00","id":1467176,"title":"","content":"The real headscratcher in terms of assamite defection isn't the diablerie addition. It's that they defected to the sect engaging in ancient worship after fleeing an ancient.<br /> <br /> Then again the ancient worship is dumb and contributes nothing anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T10:57:24-08:00","id":1467178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467176#post1467176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The real headscratcher in terms of assamite defection isn't the diablerie addition. It's that they defected to the sect engaging in ancient worship after fleeing an ancient.<br /> <br /> Then again the ancient worship is dumb and contributes nothing anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the revised era version of the defection worked fine, there was no sect wide open ancient worship going on in the Cam then V5 styles. And even after taking it out/saying it didn't happen, V20 was very slowly putting the defection back in, and it still would have worked in those circumstances as far as narrative rigor (which, I suppose it's worth asking, why even take it out as a plot event if you're just going to put it back? But eh, we'll never know). It's just the V5 version where things start to go bizarre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T11:01:41-08:00","id":1467181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467176#post1467176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The real headscratcher in terms of assamite defection isn't the diablerie addition. It's that they defected to the sect engaging in ancient worship after fleeing an ancient.<br /> <br /> Then again the ancient worship is dumb and contributes nothing anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, the Methuselah cults we've seen are:<br /> <br /> * Michael worship<br /> * Helena worship<br /> * Menele worship<br /> * Mithras worship<br /> <br /> It's not general worship of ancients in general. They're very specific ancients that we've known forever. They're also depicted as weird cults within the Camarilla that are no longer officially oppressed.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T11:03:33-08:00","id":1467182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467178#post1467178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, the revised era version of the defection worked fine, there was no sect wide open ancient worship going on in the Cam then V5 styles. And even after taking it out/saying it didn't happen, V20 was very slowly putting the defection back in, and it still would have worked in those circumstances as far as narrative rigor (which, I suppose it's worth asking, why even take it out as a plot event if you're just going to put it back? But eh, we'll never know). It's just the V5 version where things start to go bizarre.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah it's almost like v5's fluff is a bunch of headcannon lore crudely grafted onto the developing setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T11:47:04-08:00","id":1467189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467182#post1467182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah it's almost like v5's fluff is a bunch of headcannon lore crudely grafted onto the developing setting.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>No Edition Warring.<br /> <br /> I'm about ready to shut down the thread guys. This is very off topic and hostile to other posters.</b></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T07:05:38-08:00","id":1467259,"title":"","content":"Great we're aware of the problem.<br /> If I may, I'd like for you all to forget my prior arguments, clean the slate, so I may explain my view without too much erhm... heat. Right? Forget everything I said before.<br /> <br /> I think the OG 7 clans would benefit from discriminating against the other clans, and since this is the world of Darkness where everything's ever so slightly more awful, and we're talking about vampires, of course they're going to discriminate.<br /> <br /> The 7 work well together because they each provide services the others aren't so good at, which outweighs the conflicts of interest. The most perfect example would be Ventrue working with Nosferatu: They've got utterly different skillsets, generally focus on very different resources, and have very different feeding grounds; It's all positives and it's extremely beneficial for both parties to cooperate.Of course there are exceptions, but generally, they can hold hands in friendship, though the Ventrue will want to wash his hands after. This may be less clear with other clans; The Toreador in particular do overlap in terms of skills and what resources they want with the other clans, but their broad range of skills really enables them to fill gaps and maintain balances of power: The positives outweigh the negatives.<br /> <br /> The other 6 clans are all more specialized, but excluding the Tzmisce and perhaps the Giovanni, have far too much of an overlap in interests with the 7 clans. The most obvious example: Ravnos are direct competitors with Gangrel in everything, but with more reliability problems. (You might think of Chimestry as a possible service, but generally Money&gt;Chimestry so it's rather niche) But Lasombra certainly step on some toes and Settites are resource hogs. Assamites with their caste system are like their own little cooperation with specialists in every field.<br /> <br /> The Lasombra compete with The Brujah for skills and the Ventrue for resources. That's two enemies right off the bat, they've got fingers in the interests of the other clans and they make worse neighbours than either of these clans so.. isn't it good to take advantage of how the Lasombra are difficult to produce and ensure that the clan remains small and marginal? The positives of the Lasombra (They're sociopathic living weapons with mind control powers, obsessed with hierarchy) are outweighed by the negatives of the Lasombra (they're sociopathic living weapons with mind control powers, and they dress poorly). They're bad for the vampire... economy.<br /> <br /> IMO.In the Camarilla. There's <i><u>very likely</u></i> some informal protectionist agreement. The Gangrel don't want others dealing much with the Ravnos, their competition, The Ventrue don't want others to raise up the Lasombra, and so on and so forth. Of course they can't make this actual policy, because there are very powerful people from the 6 clans in the Cam and many Camarilla cities are dominated by one of the 6. and many would certainly enjoy the Assamites devaluing the sorcery of the Tremere, but ultimately such a move would push the Tremere to deal more with the Lasombra, Ravnos and... they don't want that (I don't really think the Assamite Sorcerers could really challenge the Tremere overmuch since they lack the numbers and unity, but a hit is a hit) On the street level, this manifests as a lot of slander, sensationalist stories, and general discrimination. To work fairly with an outsider can be considered a faux pass. Working with A Settite/Assamite/Giovanni/Ravnos/Lasombra/Tzmisce is usually a dirty, shameful thing, and you best be secretive about it. Even if the individual rejects their clan's sect, older vampires put a lot of attention on lineage and filial piety, so rejecting your independent sect to be with the Camarilla is a sign of disloyalty and rebeliousness that few elders are keen on seeing.<br /> <br /> It helps that most of the non-camarilla clans are unlikely to have sufficient members in a Camarilla city to really stop such defamation. They are kept as minorities and are treated as such. To make things worse, The six mostly don't like eachother and are far more likely to kill a different member of the six than they are to band together and better their place in the Cam.<br /> Equally hateful is the Camarilla fixation on the Masquerade. The Cam, in my view and supported by a few texts, doesn't actually need to try so hard to keep the Masquerade, rather the masquerade is often used as a pretense to punish neonates and keep them afraid of the law. The 6 clans all have disciplines that are horrific masquerade breaches. You may argue that Protean and Thaumaturgy are pretty flashy, but most of Thaumaturgy is very subtle, and of Protean, it does more good than bad when you think about it (Sinking into dirt&gt;finding a &quot;corpse&quot; and calling the authorities.) Quietus and Vicissitude leave behind permanent evidence of things-that-aren't-right while chimistry? Oh boy. Obtenebration and Serpentis are horror shows and Necromancy is... fine, if you're just dealing with ghosts. Are these disciplines so bad if used responsibly? Of course not. But are neonates punished proportionately for their masquerade risking crimes? Not in the slightest.<br /> <br /> Are Vampires from these clans in the Camarilla? Yes.<br /> In some cities, they may be completely equal to the 7, if not superior.<br /> But in many cases there will be many caveats and a good chunk of prejudice. Elders will impress bad attitudes on neonates. It's going to be difficult to get permission to embrace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 11-09-2021, 10:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T11:07:12-08:00","id":1467271,"title":"","content":"The published setting doesn't agree with your take on things, with numerous examples already given. The Assamites alone, in multiple editions now, either outright joined as a clan, or were on the verge of doing so, to the point that V20 itself, slow that it was with the process, went outright with &quot;when/if the Schismatics join, their justicar will be..&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But in many cases there will be many caveats and a good chunk of prejudice. </div> </div> </div>Victorian London, the most powerful Camarilla city in the world at that point, had its court draw ranks around the Lasombra antitribu that lived there and protected him with repeated active murder, so valued was he. In fact this is a pretty solid example of things not working as you wished. Oh sure, the guy encountered initial prejudice, but on the majority of his sectmates in the city functionally realizing the value of his particular quality to them, it fell away but for one particularly prejudiced Ventrue, who when he ruled the city in Mithras' absence, nearly brought the city to the brink of catastrophe anyway as far as his overall competence. And sure, when said Ventrue was in charge, he started acting on his prejudices and used his power to isolate said Lasombra, but he had to work to do it, and when he was removed from power, the Lasombra pretty much re-achieved his former status.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Ravnos start joining the sects in numbers&quot; plot thread in V20 has the Camarilla Ravnos produce primogen on a multi continent scale, to the point of managing one in Paris, one of the pre V5 Camarilla's major cities.<br /> <br /> The prejudice of vampires does not get in the way of particular things in setting to the degree that you feel they do.<br /> <br /> I could say more, particularly again note things like the Camarilla's own intent at its founding, but I guess the question I'm really asking is this, in a direct, non rhetorical way, because it feels impossible to proceed forward without getting an answer on to this question, as far as addressing and defining why your view on things seems so sharply to depart from numerous published instances of VtM:<br /> <br /> Do you think what you are saying is how the game Vampire the Masquerade works, based on the game material published for it, or are you saying that you wish this was how it worked, and trying to offer a rationale as to why? These are different things. The first thing, you're just incorrect about, due to actual published game content having a variety of instances showing outright the opposite of what you say it should, particularly as VtM developed over time. The second thing, hey, feel free to think that, there are lots of ways almost everyone wishes VtM has worked at some point, in comparison to how it actually works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 11-09-2021, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T11:13:58-08:00","id":1467272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>My Wife Is Scary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lasombra compete with The Brujah for skills and the Ventrue for resources. That's two enemies right off the bat, they've got fingers in the interests of the other clans and they make worse neighbours than either of these clans so.. isn't it good to take advantage of how the Lasombra are difficult to produce and ensure that the clan remains small and marginal? The positives of the Lasombra (They're sociopathic living weapons with mind control powers, obsessed with hierarchy) are outweighed by the negatives of the Lasombra (they're sociopathic living weapons with mind control powers, and they dress poorly). They're bad for the vampire... economy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some vampires may believe this. However, I think the problem is that you assume the majority of vampires will have their primary concern be the benefit to vampire society. What is the biggest reason for any Ventrue to support Lasombra in the Camarilla?<br /> <br /> It's not, &quot;What can they do for the Camarilla?&quot;<br /> <br /> It's &quot;What can they do for <i>me</i>?&quot;<br /> <br /> Why did Kevin Jackson support the Lasombra making Chicago their base of operations for the Camarilla? Because it increases his prestige and power in the Camarilla.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-09-2021, 02:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T11:40:40-08:00","id":1467273,"title":"","content":"1-When discussing the Camarilla, I'm using it's 500 year line-up of the OG 7, not whatever happened post 2000, which as far as canon may care might as well be a gehenna fever dream. V20 is mostly agnostic, which is a win.<br /> <br /> 2. exceptions don't make rules. iirc Freaking Montano is a cam vampire right? it means little for your average lasombra anti outside his jurisdiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T11:55:22-08:00","id":1467274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467273#post1467273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1-When discussing the Camarilla, I'm using it's 500 year line-up of the OG 7, not whatever happened post 2000, which as far as canon may care might as well be a gehenna fever dream. V20 is mostly agnostic, which is a win.<br /> <br /> 2. exceptions don't make rules. iirc Freaking Montano is a cam vampire right? it means little for your average lasombra anti outside his jurisdiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was enough exceptions it was considered a bloodline and they had things like an entire city defecting. The Lasombra Antis were never small in number in the Camarilla. They weren't a main clan but they were a presence.<br /> <br /> But yes, your view the Camarilla was gatekeeping is pretty wrong as I take it from V20 and earlier canon.<br /> <br /> 1. Obviously, the Assamite defection.<br /> <br /> 2. The Setites WERE offered a position in the Camarilla. They just turned it down.<br /> <br /> 3. The Giovanni were only denied a place at the Camarilla due to a preexisting treaty.<br /> <br /> 4. Officially the Assamites, Setites, Giovanni, and so on ARE Camarilla. They just have no representation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T12:28:46-08:00","id":1467278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467259#post1467259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I may, I'd like for you all to forget my prior arguments, clean the slate, so I may explain my view without too much erhm... heat. Right? Forget everything I said before.</div> </div> </div> </div>Done. Let's start anew.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467259#post1467259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the OG 7 clans would benefit from discriminating against the other clans, and since this is the world of Darkness where everything's ever so slightly more awful, and we're talking about vampires, of course they're going to discriminate.</div> </div> </div> </div>So this is more a focus on an unofficial Protectionism pact instead of a Defense pact.<br /> <br /> I don't think this is a necessarily conclusion, but I do see it happening with some frequency. I don't agree that the Camarilla itself would have a hand in it, but I don't think it's needed, either, but this is a valid take on the matter and I'll explain my own later.<br /> <br /> Lets call it <b>Camarilla as Cartel</b> for now, so it's easier to differentiate this take from the objective content in the books (regardless if they agree or not).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467259#post1467259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 7 work well together because they each provide services the others aren't so good at, which outweighs the conflicts of interest.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, the weak spot in this view is the Malkavian. Their skill set overlap with Ventrue and Nosferatu, and I'd say their abilities have more synergy for both (indeed, I think they have the best Discipline synergy around).<br /> <br /> At the same time, their weakness is really hard for others to deal with, and a huge historical source of prejudice. In this Cartel perspective, I don't see how the Malks would have a niche in the Cam that couldn't be better filled by some the other six.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467259#post1467259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Toreador in particular do overlap in terms of skills and what resources they want with the other clans, but their broad range of skills really enables them to fill gaps and maintain balances of power: The positives outweigh the negatives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although I don't quite think that they are the most powerful or real masters of the Cam, I still think the Toreador have actually a better place than you give them credit.<br /> <br /> They are indeed the social glue of the Cam, and their work means a lot to create the kind of ambient those predators need to convene. They're less interesting on how they can use their abilities on enemies or kine, than on how they can use them for &quot;positive&quot; effect among peers. For all the strife they create, they still defuse a lot of direct confrontation, and that's key for Elysium to work properly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467259#post1467259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other 6 clans are all more specialized,</div> </div> </div> </div>That they are, and I do agree that it make things more tricky. Still, I think they have more to offer for the Cartel, although they may need more work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467259#post1467259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ravnos are direct competitors with Gangrel in everything, but with more reliability problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing the Camarilla currently lacks a lot is scouts and messengers. A Gangrel is a good warden for the outskirts of cities, but the Ravnos got to be the best at seeing what's actually happening <i>between</i> cities and deliver news from one place to another.<br /> <br /> That has been a glaring weakness in Camarilla cities since always. Few in a given city keep reliably on touch with other cities, and technology does have its own issues even if you don't go with the overblown attitude of V5 Camarilla on the matter.<br /> <br /> But most importantly, the vampires always had a bad time finding out what is happening outside their urban domains. While a city-bound Ravnos will only have Chimerstry to offer this Cartel (which is still good IMO), Ravnos on the road may learn a lot about what's going in the dark spots of Cam's information networks (that are actually a dark sea).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467259#post1467259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lasombra compete with The Brujah for skills and the Ventrue for resources.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely can picture the spot of the <i>Antitribu</i> as exactly that, at least sometimes. If the local Ventrue go with their original write-up of endorsing power from behind the throne, then the Lasombra may work as the ones whiling to take the actual throne with all the bad that comes along.<br /> <br /> And If local Lasombra tone down their ambitions, I can see them working along with the Brujah, the two of them covering different enough niches to team-up instead of conflict.<br /> <br /> But without such unlikely dispositions, the Lasombra are hard to work with from a Cartel perspective, indeed. Sometimes almost impossible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467259#post1467259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Settites are resource hogs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind to elaborate? I don't see them as resource hogs, but the opposite.<br /> <br /> Every write-up on the Setites that isn't focusing on &quot;Movie's Thulsa Doom&quot; highlight their work as dealers and brokers. More than any discipline, they specialize in crafting elaborate prestation networks into superlative supply chains: a Setite may get you whatever you want or need.<br /> <br /> Indeed, their powers are far less focused on making you want them than on just getting the damn thing done, and what they can't do themselves, the clan will find someone who can for a fair price.<br /> <br /> And indeed, since their goals are long term, their work ethics are pretty good for Kindred standards. They usually have fair prices as their goal is to keep the wheels of the business running, and they're straight with their deals.<br /> <br /> Serpentis is almost straight up Protean, with few significant tweaks, so I don't see it being significantly problematic. Not to say that Protean should have been more versatile since always and Serpentis basically do nothing I don't think Protean should do, except maybe by the &quot;rip your heart&quot; last power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467259#post1467259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assamites with their caste system are like their own little cooperation with specialists in every field.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still think they could find their niche, as they do in the Ashirra, especially because they do their thing in their particular way. I picture the Viziers and the Ventrue working a lot together, and the Toreador wanting them around more than shunning them. Warriors add a level of professional approach to Kindred combat techniques that is otherwise lost since the Salubri even if you don't mention their ability as assassins.<br /> <br /> Of course, it isn't without problems. Warriors and Viziers have to find their sweet spot between two clans each. If it goes well, all clans involved grow stronger, but if not they'll have two rivals to deal with. And while I think it is easy for the Viziers, Warriors are in a tighter spot. Sorcerers have to deal with the Tremere, and that clan is definitely protectionist to the extreme as written, no interpretation needed.<br /> <br /> There is also the thing with their Disciplines, since they depend on which version you'll take for each non-warrior sect. I personally don't think the Viziers would have Presence, as their shtick is more to create than exhibit art, and the hyper-focus of their attention instead of wanting attention.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467259#post1467259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I don't really think the Assamite Sorcerers could really challenge the Tremere overmuch since they lack the numbers and unity, but a hit is a hit)</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Although Revised did so anyway, so the Tremere have to suck it up.<br /> <br /> Due to the Sorcerer's low numbers and take on magic, I think it actually works far better in practice than the Tremere fear it can. They simply can't and won't even try to be a threat to the Pyramid, even because they're not so keen on selling their magic. They would sell counsel and protection far more than an assortment of spells with listed price.<br /> <br /> But the Tremere carved their niche eliminating potential competition, so it isn't ever something they'll accept willingly, from Assamites, Tzimisce, Setites or anyone else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467259#post1467259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To make things worse, The six mostly don't like eachother and are far more likely to kill a different member of the six than they are to band together and better their place in the Cam.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not so sure about this, where did you get it? I don't remember any particular feud among them. I may just be missing one or two things, but as a general rule I don't think they're that indisposed at working together.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467259#post1467259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 6 clans all have disciplines that are horrific masquerade breaches.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't completely disagree, but I think it is heavily overstated. While I do agree that they may be argued as such when the actual goal is to keep them out, but discussing their actual effect on the Masquerade:<br /> <br /> Quietus depends first on version used, but even with the Warrior's classic version I don't think they leave so much evidence. Less, actually, than Path of Blood. And the evidence it does leave isn't so permanent in the sense that it can be cleaned.<br /> <br /> A corpse isn't a Masquerade-breaching evidence, despite how much it is evidence of murder. It takes a lot of work to find out any evidence of the death cause of a victim of Quietus, and even then it would be an unlikely leap of thought to conclude it has anything supernatural to it. Poisons are a common and varied thing that can't always be identified, even Dagon's Call causes an actual symptom common to a great number of diseases, called haemoptysis.<br /> <br /> Vicissitude can be used in quite overt ways, but can also be used in minor and subtle ones, despite level used (in terms of permanent evidence). You have the advantage that any dangerous use is usually obvious enough to raise concerns before it gets out of hand and easy for the same individual to correct. I don't think the typical demon-faced Sabbat Tzimisce would be welcome, but if not on their art, at least on text this kind isn't that common.<br /> <br /> Chimerstry is temporary by nature, and can be used in many ways. Only a really incompetent user will make it unsubtle, as it actually miss the point of using an illusion. I'd say it is easier to use it for Masquerade protection than to break it, by far, <b>even</b> for a moron.<br /> <br /> Obtenebration can't be helped. Every use is meant to be as overt as could be possible since if the product don't interact with a target there's no point. I don't think it is much worse than Protean, but that's a bad comparison to begin with.<br /> <br /> Serpentis isn't that far from Protean, though, and I don't think it is harder on the Masquerade. The first three levels can be concealed while active, and the last one isn't a Breach. Protean have a similar record, give or take particularities that sometimes make it better, sometimes worse at subtlety.<br /> <br /> Necromancy is pretty much in the same spot as Thaumaturgy. Actually I'd say there are proportionally more subtle Paths.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467259#post1467259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IMO.In the Camarilla. There's <i><u>very likely</u></i> some informal protectionist agreement.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it is an impossible perspective, and certainly V5 goes for this take on the matter. But for the four previous editions I don't think that's the case.<br /> <br /> First of all I see the Camarilla as a Defense Pact, not a Cartel. Its purpose includes non-interference on domains without good reason. Second they have this claim that all vampires belong under their laws, their Traditions. And last bot not least their overall goals benefit more from playing the part than keeping protectionism.<br /> <br /> Pragmatically speaking, by adopting a protectionist stance the Camarilla just creates unneeded resistance to their claims. The other clans won't cease to exist and the Camarilla doesn't have anything to gain from such a conflict. Wherever other clans are present, let then be. Absorb them. If you want to keep then in line you must have then at hand, not on the other side of a gun.<br /> <br /> Which particularly brings the question of unsubtle powers. The Camarilla's purpose does include Masquerade maintenance, be it overly done or not. And then it is more effective to have the ones with such powers under you to rule them, than keeping them as outsiders left to their own devices.<br /> <br /> Now, I do believe prejudice and systemic oppression goes a long way on most Camarilla cities. It's just the difference between city politics and sect politics. The Inner Council have little use to not welcoming other clans to the sect. In fact, having others in the Council don't mean any of them have to give up on power or position, just that the Council as a whole have that more resources and will bring those other Methuselah to somewhere they can see.<br /> <br /> But since the Camarilla have little actual interference on how a city is run, a lot of places just run their own protectionism and prejudices as they see fit. After all, as long as the Prince don't call a preemptive Blood Hunt over an entire clan, there's little else they can't do to make staying there all but impossible to whomever they want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T12:36:56-08:00","id":1467280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467273#post1467273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1-When discussing the Camarilla, I'm using it's 500 year line-up of the OG 7, not whatever happened post 2000, which as far as canon may care might as well be a gehenna fever dream. V20 is mostly agnostic, which is a win.<br /> <br /> 2. exceptions don't make rules. iirc Freaking Montano is a cam vampire right? it means little for your average lasombra anti outside his jurisdiction.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Then you are not talking about the game Vampire the Masquerade as it exists, you are talking about it as you want it to exist. Saying every edition showing you are incorrect doesn't count isn't really discussion. You are beyond that using words like &quot;500 year lineup&quot; while ignoring things like the Camarilla's own intent at its founding. The Convention of Thorns was an explicit attempt to get the Assamites, Lasombra and Tzimisce to join the Camarilla, by the Camarilla. One of the explicit questions of Thorns was &quot;what do we do to keep the Assamites in check if they instead refuse membership.&quot; The arrangement that happened instead with the Assamites was straight up plan B. And part of the Ravnos not joining was Durga Syn addressing the convention and going, more or less, &quot;this whole thing is stupid and you are all stupid.&quot; It was multiple days of discussion and debate on these things, with delegates from a wide variety of clans able to speak their peace and argue back and forth. That's straight up from the books. There's an outright sequence about the Convention of Thorns in the Transylvania Chronicles that is described at length as something to interact with, where one Assamite outright tries to argue that the players should support the idea of preventing the Assamites joining the Camarilla and instead coming up with some other arrangement from the line of reasoning of &quot;do you really want to give the Camarilla our clan as a weapon?&quot; as though the nascent Camarilla totally wanted to have the Assamites as a weapon, and were ultimately foiled in that by the Assamites own refusal to become such, leading to plan B.<br /> <br /> V20, while we're there, was putting the Assamite schism back in, with Lore of the Clans reintroducing it through the idea of the Preservationist Conspiracy and then having BJD pull the trigger on it acting, and was the edition that offered &quot;Ravnos becoming Camarilla enough that there are primogen in major cities&quot; as a plot thread in the same book (BJD, again).<br /> <br /> I'm not sure at this point how read your posts as not saying that you refuse to acknowledge content from three different editions of a gameline (four editions really, the Convention of Thorns as an encounter is associated with Vampire: The Dark Ages as far as the brand Transylvania Chronicles II was published under) when talking about how you think that gameline works.<br /> <br /> So again, is the idea here that we're talking about actual published content for the game, or how you think the game should work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":".  clarified a source 11-09-2021, 07:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T13:06:28-08:00","id":1467283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467272#post1467272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some vampires may believe this. However, I think the problem is that you assume the majority of vampires will have their primary concern be the benefit to vampire society. What is the biggest reason for any Ventrue to support Lasombra in the Camarilla?<br /> <br /> It's not, &quot;What can they do for the Camarilla?&quot;<br /> <br /> It's &quot;What can they do for <i>me</i>?&quot;<br /> <br /> Why did Kevin Jackson support the Lasombra making Chicago their base of operations for the Camarilla? Because it increases his prestige and power in the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's extremely true, and one major reason why prejudice among Kindred wouldn't work so close to prejudice among mortals.<br /> <br /> Vampires of any clan can acquire relevant resources and offer something in return for their allegiance. Most Kindred don't ask if your service will conflict with other's interests, even their own clan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467273#post1467273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1-When discussing the Camarilla, I'm using it's 500 year line-up of the OG 7,</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair, but it bears stating.<br /> <br /> You can't just <i>assume</i> that and tell no one, as every edition <b><i><u>IS</u></i></b> canon, like it or not. Otherwise, it's edition war.<br /> <br /> Even V5 I only state separately because the Camarilla <i>does</i> change enough for it to make a difference. Yet, I treat as two equally valid Camarillas from a canon standpoint, no matter my dislike of one of them.<br /> <br /> All clans were invited to the Thorns. All of them the Camarilla instigators wanted on the sect. There was no exception and this is in the time span proposed. Alternative treaties or outright refusal only happened after the founders effectively tried to rally everyone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467274#post1467274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. Officially the Assamites, Setites, Giovanni, and so on ARE Camarilla. They just have no representation.</div> </div> </div> </div>This bears repeating over and over, especially if only 1st and 2nd edition lore is to e taken. Because only from Revised is ever mentioned the idea that a clan is a member or not.<br /> <br /> For 1st and 2nd edition this concept is as true as possible. No clan is outside the Camarilla. No bloodline, either. No matter what you may think, the sect does regard you as a member and under Prince authority and protection. As they're <b>the</b> state, there's no one without the other.<br /> <br /> You may try to hold any official or unofficial office no matter who you are. You may even get it if you have good cards and play them right. You can even become a Primigen, Archon, Justicar or Councilor, as hard as such a thing may be, if you set yourself on the goal and face the challenges.<br /> <br /> Is it easy? Not by any stretch of the imagination. Is it feasible? Plainly put, yes, it is. No particular reason it shouldn't be.<br /> <br /> And it is again important to keep in mind that only one commonality exists between the &quot;Other Six&quot; about the Camarilla: <b>they</b> didn't wanted to join. It was never about them being denied (until recently, of course). And as far as anyone can tell the lack of things like Justicars is pretty much because no one with the competence to try actually wanted or cared.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T16:18:12-08:00","id":1467299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467272#post1467272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Some vampires may believe this. However, I think the problem is that you assume the majority of vampires will have their primary concern be the benefit to vampire society. What is the biggest reason for any Ventrue to support Lasombra in the Camarilla?<br /> <br /> It's not, &quot;What can they do for the Camarilla?&quot;<br /> <br /> It's &quot;What can they do for <i>me</i>?&quot;<br /> <br /> Why did Kevin Jackson support the Lasombra making Chicago their base of operations for the Camarilla? Because it increases his prestige and power in the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>This pretty much nails it on the head. Kindred are going to do things that benefit them first and their Sect and everyone else a distant second. All the stuff Jackson's been doing in V5 while it certainly helps plenty of Kindred in Chicago, it makes him look good, both locally and aboard. In a lot of ways Jackson is attempting to build himself up as the new Gold Standard for Princes and in turn becoming more powerful and influential within the Cam.<br /> <br /> Supporting the defecting Lasombra and setting them up within his city plays into that. If it pays off, Jackson will get to take a ton of credit for making the Lasombra a card-carrying members of the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467278#post1467278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing the Camarilla currently lacks a lot is scouts and messengers. A Gangrel is a good warden for the outskirts of cities, but the Ravnos got to be the best at seeing what's actually happening <i>between</i> cities and deliver news from one place to another.<br /> <br /> That has been a glaring weakness in Camarilla cities since always. Few in a given city keep reliably on touch with other cities, and technology does have its own issues even if you don't go with the overblown attitude of V5 Camarilla on the matter.<br /> <br /> But most importantly, the vampires always had a bad time finding out what is happening outside their urban domains. While a city-bound Ravnos will only have Chimerstry to offer this Cartel (which is still good IMO), Ravnos on the road may learn a lot about what's going in the dark spots of Cam's information networks (that are actually a dark sea).</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I rather loathe the V5 Ravnos and how after years of developing the Clan into something V5 tossed that out to return to the purely nomadic Ravnos of old. The Indian Ravnos would have been great for getting a chunk of the Clan into the Camarilla, providing the Cam a solid foundation in India and the surrounding nations (a region that is noted to have weak SI presence currently) while in return the Indian Ravnos get Camarilla support to help them maintain their territory and recover from the ravaging of their Clan.<br /> <br /> Well maybe someone working on V5 will remember the Indian Ravnos and do something with them down the road.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467278#post1467278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed. Although Revised did so anyway, so the Tremere have to suck it up.<br /> <br /> Due to the Sorcerer's low numbers and take on magic, I think it actually works far better in practice than the Tremere fear it can. They simply can't and won't even try to be a threat to the Pyramid, even because they're not so keen on selling their magic. They would sell counsel and protection far more than an assortment of spells with listed price.<br /> <br /> But the Tremere carved their niche eliminating potential competition, so it isn't ever something they'll accept willingly, from Assamites, Tzimisce, Setites or anyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I could see plenty of non-Tremere Princes and Primogen being fine with or even happy about the Tremere's monopoly on Blood Sorcery taking a hit by bringing in Clans with their own Blood Sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T17:28:47-08:00","id":1467303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Honestly I rather loathe the V5 Ravnos and how after years of developing the Clan into something V5 tossed that out to return to the purely nomadic Ravnos of old. The Indian Ravnos would have been great for getting a chunk of the Clan into the Camarilla, providing the Cam a solid foundation in India and the surrounding nations (a region that is noted to have weak SI presence currently) while in return the Indian Ravnos get Camarilla support to help them maintain their territory and recover from the ravaging of their Clan.<br /> <br /> Well maybe someone working on V5 will remember the Indian Ravnos and do something with them down the road </div> </div> </div>The Ravnos have the worst luck because Ravnos Revised gave them an intricate and interesting new backstory before the Week of Nightmares. However, V5 is very clear that they don't want to restrict any Clans to one region or not. So you can have Banu Haqim in Gary, Indiana like Faith Corrigan and india probably has its own version of the Ventrue, Toreador, and Gangrel now. Clans are more now about archetypes and the Ravnos are the wandering tricksters again.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T17:35:07-08:00","id":1467305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467303#post1467303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Ravnos have the worst luck because Ravnos Revised gave them an intricate and interesting new backstory before the Week of Nightmares. However, V5 is very clear that they don't want to restrict any Clans to one region or not. So you can have Banu Haqim in Gary, Indiana like Faith Corrigan and india probably has its own version of the Ventrue, Toreador, and Gangrel now. Clans are more now about archetypes and the Ravnos are the wandering tricksters again.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The issue (amongst several) is that they did that with the Assamites/Banu Haqim without completely obliterating the growth they had been given, but decided it wasn't even worth trying to preserve growth with the Ravnos. Who honestly come off like a grudging afterthought given their place in an online pdf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T17:43:10-08:00","id":1467306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467305#post1467305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue (amongst several) is that they did that with the Assamites/Banu Haqim without completely obliterating the growth they had been given, but decided it wasn't even worth trying to preserve growth with the Ravnos. Who honestly come off like a grudging afterthought given their place in an online pdf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps but the thing is that lovable rogues and Tricksters are certainly not a bad thing when divorced from....well, the whole Ravnos deal.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T17:48:12-08:00","id":1467309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467306#post1467306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps but the thing is that lovable rogues and Tricksters are certainly not a bad thing when divorced from....well, the whole Ravnos deal.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly it's kind of bland and narrow to have that as what's the entire deal of a group to work with. It's not exactly helpful and does a lot to encourage stereotyping. This is another problem of taking an archetyptal approach. Depth, nuance, conceptual range, they all go flying out a window.<br /> <br /> Which is ironic for an edition whose current team include people who like to practically scream how clans should not be monoliths, but guideposts, and all that kind of thing.<br /> <br /> It's also sort of baffling when the current dev will go on about how they don't want the rationale for things in V5 to be so deeply buried in metaplot and then turn around give the V5 Ravnos a curse/bane that only makes sense as coming purely from metaplot. <br /> <br /> It doesn't give a lot of hope for future consistency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T18:04:06-08:00","id":1467310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467303#post1467303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Ravnos have the worst luck because Ravnos Revised gave them an intricate and interesting new backstory before the Week of Nightmares. However, V5 is very clear that they don't want to restrict any Clans to one region or not. So you can have Banu Haqim in Gary, Indiana like Faith Corrigan and india probably has its own version of the Ventrue, Toreador, and Gangrel now. Clans are more now about archetypes and the Ravnos are the wandering tricksters again.</div> </div> </div> </div>True but we're in an age where geographic barriers aren't as much of a thing anymore. I live just outside of Winnipeg and it's by no means a huge city here in Canada but it has multiple ethnic groups with their own community centers and temples in the city, including a Sikh one. It wouldn't be any stranger to have Indian Ravnos in North America than it would to have Assamites from the Middle East or a European Ventrue.<br /> <br /> There have been groups of people from India that have moved from their homeland. Is it really that much of a stretch that some Ravnos wouldn't follow their mortal kin out of India?<br /> <br /> And that's not even factoring ideas like the Indian Ravnos joining or considering to join the Cam and sending agents aboard to Cam Cities to assess if the Camarilla is worth joining up with. Hell, with all Jackson's been doing to make Chicago the Crown Jewel of the Camarilla, sending a couple to the city wouldn't be out of the question.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T00:36:55-08:00","id":1467333,"title":"","content":"Lots of good counter arguments and I'm on a computer that isn't so good for quotes so I'll try address the points made even if not everything's quoted. <br /> <br /> I think going with the original camarilla is fair, and I think I stated what I was going with explicitly enough. I realize &quot;OG&quot; isn't exactly common parlance but I did refer explicitly to the Gangrel. Why do i think this is fair? On one hand, the Camarilla has kept it's original lineup for 500ish years, and all the shakeups have occured within a fraction of it's history. Some people like to play outside of the present day, where smartphones aren't ubiquitous or where they can comfortably have century long timeskips without waking up in Megacity 1. On the otherhand, V1 and V2 have the OG 7, Revised has optional Gehenna scenarios and it's debatable as to whether events like the Week of Nightmares or Gangrel leaving are also optional. V20 is agnostic and is happy to go either way (when/IF the Assamites join... like it's entirely up to the ST) As respectfully as I can describe it: V5's Camarilla is a fundamentally different Beast to the point that it needs a name change because it has very little in common. <br /> <br /> Yes. The Camarilla explicitly invited every clan into the Camarilla. I'm well aware. However, how sincere was that offer? I think the Camarilla knew damn-well that the other clans would say no, but extended the olive brand so that nobody would accuse them of not-trying or deliberately excluding a clan; such behaviour would be unfitting for a global body that claims to support all vampires. &quot;we offered, you refused&quot; is a good way of justifying why some clans should get better political representation than others. <br /> <br /> The Malkavians are indeed a clan with a lot of overlap and I was thinking about them a lot during my post. But I think that what ultimately seperates the Malks from the Lasombra or anyone else is.. Tact. Malks are more symbiotic or parasitic than competitive. They don't show off what they own, they find oppertunities others don't. A Malkavian can own part of a Ventrue's company and not bother the Ventrue, Both of them might gain from the event, or the Malkavian might leave the Ventrue non the wiser. A stereotypical Lasombra, on the otherhand, will either try to take the Ventrue's company, hedge their bets against it, or establish a competitor. In terms of espionage competition with the Nosferatu, the Malkavians have different strengths but more importantly they have a different approach: A Nosferatu is like a private investigator; you hire one and they'll go out and learn all about something for you. A malkavian is more often like an inside man who just happens to be in the field you're interested in, or they have a friend in such a field. <br /> <br /> Even if the Assamites join, they're in a rather shakey possition due to the effects of the schism and the parts where they're newcomers. Vampires are slow. They take centuries to get established. It'd be foolish to think they could just join a global organization en mass and then be equals within 30 years. Until V5 overturned the boat, the remaining Camarilla clans were in a good possition to exploit the Assamites. (also I've got a lot of doubt about the Gangrel leaving the Camarilla permanently. They'll be back, it's in their best interests) <br /> <br /> The Assamites in the Ashirra were renegades, outcasts and spies anyway. Schismatics before the Shism. It's completely wrong to think the Assamites will adapt well to the Cam because they did alright with the Ashirra. Maybe I'm standing with Ur-Shulgi too much but Islam isn't at all compatible with Assamite Orthadoxy, and things like Shih sorcery were always considered a sick parody few Assamites embraced. Correct me If I'm wrong but we still know fuck all about the Ashirra in modern nights. One of the earliest sources suggested it was a Saudi/Iran thing and meta wise this was a shot at how overly religious White Wolf thought they were. Other people suggest the Ashirra is the Cam but way better because it's Asian and thus spiritual and we all know how WW had skewed perceptions of anything asian back in the day. <br /> <br /> On the outsider clans having more issues with one another: <br /> This is obviously more true for some than it is for others. But they do tend to have more extreme outlooks than the more moderate 7 clans. If you could describe the Ventrue as Conservative and the Brujah as liberal, then you can describe the Assamites as Fascist and the Settites as AnCaps (The Snake imagery is not a coincidence) It's order VS Chaos. The Assamites are <i>The Law</i> and The Ravnos are all too frequently outlaws. Assamites protect mortals, Lasombra abuse them. Lasombra and Giovanni are in general just more agressive. Half of these clans are likely to compete over the drug trade. The Tzmisce are arch-conservatives while the Lasombra and Giovanni are modern go-getters... ok... yeah, that's not a great reason. But it's undeniable that these clans are politically a lot further out than their more center-right compatriots in the OG 7. Assamites, Lasombra and Giovanni are obsessed with order; Settites and Ravnos are creatures of Chaos, and the Tzmisce just want everyone to stay the fuck out of their territory with no law but their own (because they are doing some very questionable things there. Also feudalism is the end result of being an ancap so...) <br /> <br /> The Giovanni, I think, have the least issues. But they're obviously out of the Cam because Augustus had a bullshit plan. Honestly, I don't think the Cam would want necromancy to get big. Once the Necromancers come in, the hauntings begin, and people will start to ask the necromancers to get rid of the ghosts. Creating problems to sell solutions. Obviously, this is quite undesirable, and the Cam would do a lot better working with small scale necromancers like the Samedi or Nageraja rather than something large scale, well organized and threatening like the Giovanni (or worse, the Hecata) <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T05:13:13-08:00","id":1467341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467333#post1467333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even if the Assamites join, they're in a rather shakey possition due to the effects of the schism and the parts where they're newcomers. Vampires are slow. They take centuries to get established. It'd be foolish to think they could just join a global organization en mass and then be equals within 30 years. Until V5 overturned the boat, the remaining Camarilla clans were in a good possition to exploit the Assamites. (also I've got a lot of doubt about the Gangrel leaving the Camarilla permanently. They'll be back, it's in their best interests)<br /> <br /> The Assamites in the Ashirra were renegades, outcasts and spies anyway. Schismatics before the Shism. It's completely wrong to think the Assamites will adapt well to the Cam because they did alright with the Ashirra. Maybe I'm standing with Ur-Shulgi too much but Islam isn't at all compatible with Assamite Orthadoxy, and things like Shih sorcery were always considered a sick parody few Assamites embraced. Correct me If I'm wrong but we still know fuck all about the Ashirra in modern nights. One of the earliest sources suggested it was a Saudi/Iran thing and meta wise this was a shot at how overly religious White Wolf thought they were. Other people suggest the Ashirra is the Cam but way better because it's Asian and thus spiritual and we all know how WW had skewed perceptions of anything asian back in the day.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. I think the retcon in The Dark Ages and Assamite Revised was the fact the Ashirra Assamites were NOT schismatics. That it was just the Camarilla only encountered the Web of Knives assassins and that virtually the entire Vizier Clan of the Assamites acted more like Middle Eastern Toreador or Ventrue than they ever acted as fanatical Blood Cultists.<br /> <br /> 2. Assamite Orthodoxy is, essentially, whatever the leader of the Clan says is and Islam was accepted as the default of the Clan by the Old Man of the Mountain before ur-Shulgi. It should also be noted that &quot;worship only Haqim&quot; is EXPLICITLY against Haqim's will as Haqim was stated numerous times to be a deeply devout Antediluvian. It was just he presumably worshiped whatever gods were around during his time.<br /> <br /> (Which undoubtedly pissed Caine off)<br /> <br /> 3. Shih magic may be heretical to mainstream Islam but it's not heretical to ASSAMITE Islam, which is inherently a heretical offshoot of Islam. I also think this is a questionable thing for you to bring up because you've already stated you don't think any vampire could remain Islamic and be a vampire while the Assamites as well as Ashirra have both been stated to be VERY Islamic. So the Sorcerer caste may almost all be great believers in Islam and practice their forbidden magic.<br /> <br /> Hypocrisy, they name is Cainite.<br /> <br /> 4. We know what the Dark Ages Ashirra is and we can guess that it is what the Modern Age Ashirra is by postulating how it changed 800 years later. However, <i>Veil of Night</i> actually explain straight up the Ashirra was a organization of vampires that united under Islamic government but that a huge number of its members (specifically those who predtaed the religion) only gave lip service to the religion and it was mostly a proto-Cam.<br /> <br /> V20 never updated the book but V5 is also going with the idea the Ashirra is formally officially allied, EU-style with the Camarilla and may actually be fully folded into it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is obviously more true for some than it is for others. But they do tend to have more extreme outlooks than the more moderate 7 clans. If you could describe the Ventrue as Conservative and the Brujah as liberal, then you can describe the Assamites as Fascist and the Settites as AnCaps (The Snake imagery is not a coincidence) It's order VS Chaos.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's explicitly a retcon but I think the Web of Knives was meant to be the extremist crazy fascist part of the Assamites that was culturally distinct from the rest of the Clan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is obviously more true for some than it is for others. But they do tend to have more extreme outlooks than the more moderate 7 clans. If you could describe the Ventrue as Conservative and the Brujah as liberal, then you can describe the Assamites as Fascist and the Settites as AnCaps (The Snake imagery is not a coincidence) It's order VS Chaos.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this helps illustrate why we never quite jelled on the Followers of Set and Ministry because I think of them as quite literally the least chaotic Clan with the possible exception of the Tremere. Yes, the Followers of Set espouse FREEDOM but that's a hypocritical statement that reflects their leaders' doublespeak in the same way the Sabbat does.<br /> <br /> The Followers of Set are an intensely orthodox and totalitarian religion with all the brainwashing as well as conservative views expected of an extremely well-entrenched religion. It's why I suppored the break with the Ministry because I never believed they would be that good at converting people to pure Set worship or forgiving of deviancy.<br /> <br /> Religions have schisms, divisions, and orthodoxy debates unless one side suppresses all dissent. Which tends to result in breakway churches in RL, be it Buddhism, Christianity, Islam, or other faiths where the doctrine is written down. The Followers of Set are many things but not CHAOTIC. They are the pinnacle of Lawful Evil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-10-2021, 08:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T05:21:40-08:00","id":1467342,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Just checking in that the argument has been going on and while I'm enjoying this deep dive, a reminder to everyone [myself included] this is meant to be fun and respectful to everyone.</span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T06:50:10-08:00","id":1467351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467310#post1467310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True but we're in an age where geographic barriers aren't as much of a thing anymore. I live just outside of Winnipeg and it's by no means a huge city here in Canada but it has multiple ethnic groups with their own community centers and temples in the city, including a Sikh one. It wouldn't be any stranger to have Indian Ravnos in North America than it would to have Assamites from the Middle East or a European Ventrue.<br /> <br /> There have been groups of people from India that have moved from their homeland. Is it really that much of a stretch that some Ravnos wouldn't follow their mortal kin out of India?<br /> <br /> And that's not even factoring ideas like the Indian Ravnos joining or considering to join the Cam and sending agents aboard to Cam Cities to assess if the Camarilla is worth joining up with. Hell, with all Jackson's been doing to make Chicago the Crown Jewel of the Camarilla, sending a couple to the city wouldn't be out of the question.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it was more the fact that V5 seems to be about culling the ethnic ties of Clans and making it so that every region can have a broad collection of them. Hence why one of the first books (Camarilla) showed us meeting a Tzimisce Japanese Prince of high generation.<br /> <br /> The problem with the Revised Ravnos being brought into the V5 era was the fact most of their reforms and changes were explictly tied to them being an in-depth and respectful take of Indian culture. If you're looking for archetypes, it basically is not going to be helpful.<br /> <br /> Modern Ravnos are also going to be, in-universe, doubly removed from their past because so much of their Clan culture was annihilated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T06:52:09-08:00","id":1467352,"title":"","content":"I believe you're very wrong about the Followers of Set (If we ignore V5 for a moment) <br /> The Followers are, essentially, a de-centralized collection of cults where every member starts their own thematically similar but drastically re-written cult, and people join the main cult after graduating from one of the lesser cults. This, naturally leads to a lot of Settites confused as to what's actually the real story because all they've got is third-hand chinese whispers. But that's like... the point. The FoS have rarely had the chance to be draconian about their beliefs because they don't actually know the truth at the origin of their mythos. They have always been extremely happy to acknowledge Settites using other Pantheons. It's only in cases where things have been radically different and political conflict has occured that the Settites have actually taken issue, like they have with the indian branch (No YOU are excomunicated) but even then the only heretics worthy of war are the Osiris kids and the serpents of the light lot. I'm convinced the Followers of Set genuinely believe in their cocaine laced no-age-of-consent branch of Freedom. So long as you don't threaten the bottom line or start advocating clear heresy, Settites don't care what you do. Want to suck up to the prince and live a relatively normal unlife with the Camarilla? Go right ahead. Sure, there are going to be actual conservatives among the FoS, but there are some pretty whack people claiming that to be anti-racist we have to be anti-white and that's... There are morons in every group and you shouldn't judge the majority based on a minority. <br /> <br /> The Web Of Knives is only a fraction of the Loyalist Assamites. They simply go a little further than most in terms of training their neonates. The Web of Knives is not a replacement for radical assamites. There are plenty of fanatical adherents to the path of blood that aren't the Web of Knives. It's like saying all white supremicists are part of the KKK and all the white people who aren't part of the KKK aren't racist at all. it's simply not true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T07:51:49-08:00","id":1467355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467352#post1467352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe you're very wrong about the Followers of Set (If we ignore V5 for a moment)<br /> The Followers are, essentially, a de-centralized collection of cults where every member starts their own thematically similar but drastically re-written cult, and people join the main cult after graduating from one of the lesser cults. This, naturally leads to a lot of Settites confused as to what's actually the real story because all they've got is third-hand chinese whispers. But that's like... the point. The FoS have rarely had the chance to be draconian about their beliefs because they don't actually know the truth at the origin of their mythos. They have always been extremely happy to acknowledge Settites using other Pantheons.<br /> <br /> It's only in cases where things have been radically different and political conflict has occured that the Settites have actually taken issue, like they have with the indian branch (No YOU are excomunicated) but even then the only heretics worthy of war are the Osiris kids and the serpents of the light lot. I'm convinced the Followers of Set genuinely believe in their cocaine laced no-age-of-consent branch of Freedom. So long as you don't threaten the bottom line or start advocating clear heresy, Settites don't care what you do. Want to suck up to the prince and live a relatively normal unlife with the Camarilla? Go right ahead. Sure, there are going to be actual conservatives among the FoS, but there are some pretty whack people claiming that to be anti-racist we have to be anti-white and that's... There are morons in every group and you shouldn't judge the majority based on a minority.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehhh,<br /> <br /> I think there's quite a few things that contradict that that I'd like to bring up regarding the Followers of Set.<br /> <br /> 1. The first thing is the fact the Orthodox Followers of Set purging the Unorthodox Followers of Set is not a product of V5. This is something that is important to note as it is a product of OPP's original plan for V:TM 4th Edition and the ground was laid in V20 with Beckett's Jyhad Diary. Originally, the Ministry was just undergoing a &quot;rebranding&quot; but OPP got the chance to carry their idea over to COTBG as well as the write-up in Anarchs. So this is a V20 idea that OPP got the chance to expand on.<br /> <br /> 2. The Cohorts of Wepwawet were a product of Followers of Set Revised rather than something new. So the idea of, &quot;We're going to worship Egyptian style mothersuckers and that is the ONLY WAY&quot; is something that was present as early as Revised. <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Cohort_of_Wepwawet\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Cohort_of_Wepwawet</a><br /> <br /> It was BJD that gave them the approval of the Fire Court but they've been a thing awhile. Indeed, they were the people that drove the Haitian Voudan Setites to join the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> 3. The Fire Court of the Setites has been the orthodox headquarters of the Followers of Set for 4000 years and basically serves as their version of the Vatican. Setite religion is not disorganized, individualized cults or not, due to the fact that it has its very own version of Alamut or the Chantry in Vienna.<br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Fire_Court\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Fire_Court</a><br /> <br /> (And yes, even then it had a rivalry in the Cult of Ectasy Path vs. its Orthodox Typhonist)<br /> <br /> 4. The Followers of Set are probably the group that has the best continuity of any Vampire: The Masquerade Clan in terms of direct link to their Antediluvian and his mythology. I mean, Nefertiri is a 4th generation Followers of Set and childe of their Antediluvian up and around in Berlin. As much as we like to chide that book, its still mostly canon.<br /> <br /> Which is to say the Followers of Set don't have much ambiguity about their faiths.<br /> <br /> 5. The Followers of Set believe you're either a face of Set (Satan, Eris, Loki, and so on) or you're an Aeon. They're not actually that good about polytheism and this is the original Orthodox write up of the Setites and not V5 that said, in fact, plenty of Setites are polytheists and find the Typhonists to be wack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Web Of Knives is only a fraction of the Loyalist Assamites. They simply go a little further than most in terms of training their neonates. The Web of Knives is not a replacement for radical assamites. There are plenty of fanatical adherents to the path of blood that aren't the Web of Knives. It's like saying all white supremicists are part of the KKK and all the white people who aren't part of the KKK aren't racist at all. it's simply not true. </div> </div> </div>I think the depiction in Assamite Revised was that the Web of Knives was the majority of the clan (albeit by a slim majority) and the vast majority sided with Ur-Shulgi--though not all of them since the Web of Knives included plenty of die-hard Islam believers. The Vizier caste went all Camarilla Schismatic and the Sorcerer caste split down the middle. Given Ur-Shulgi wanted to war against all of the Cainite race, the distinction between Loyalist and Web of Knives was immaterial.<br /> <br /> This is where I actually think V5 did a decent job with Ur-Shulgi because the Sabbat fighting a Gehenna War against the Methuselah-worshiping Assamites and it lasting twenty-years with immense casualties is probably the only thing about the Gehenna War that would make perfect sense. It also would mean Ur-Shulgi wasn't sitting on his ass this entire time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T09:51:25-08:00","id":1467363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467333#post1467333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think going with the original camarilla is fair,</div> </div> </div> </div>The question isn't the line-up, but what you consider canonical sect policy. The OG-7 was pretty clear, but it doesn't change that Revised, V20 and V5 canon is still canon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467333#post1467333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Revised has optional Gehenna scenarios and it's debatable as to whether events like the Week of Nightmares or Gangrel leaving are also optional.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only optional thing in Revised's metaplot before the Scenarios is the date of the Week of Nightmares, and even then with the caveat that any development in books published after ToTB is also after the event.<br /> <br /> Gehenna itself states that everything up to and including The Withering is canon, period. V20 is mostly metaplot agnostic, but mostly isn't completely and BJD is there to be canon.<br /> <br /> And while I do agree that V5 changes the Camarilla a lot, it is still canon. By the way, I find it actually more forthcoming to your idea of the Camarilla gatekeeping clans and working as a Cartel, you're only pissed off because it doesn't agree with your exact idea of perfect line-up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467333#post1467333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, how sincere was that offer?</div> </div> </div> </div>As sincere as the reader wants to assume. You're welcome to think it was complete BS, but that's not what's in the books, they have nothing hinting that it was just a ruse. As far as anyone can tell by reading the actual text, it was completely sincere, despite not unanimous in every case.<br /> <br /> Even because they really received their representatives and everyone that came took a part in the discussions. This is the very definition of political representation, and they didn't left because they weren't being heard, they were engaged with for the entire Convention.<br /> <br /> \u200bThis is, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12141\" data-vbnamecard=\"12141\">MarkK</a> said, what is actually written in the books, like it or not. You can think it is silly, you can disagree, you can apply alternative readings, but you can't say the actual writing isn't the actual official canon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467333#post1467333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Malkavians are indeed a clan with a lot of overlap and I was thinking about them a lot during my post. But I think that what ultimately seperates the Malks from the Lasombra or anyone else is.. Tact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forget the Lasombra, you can compare the Malks to the FoS, Assamites or Ravnos, that I think would be better comparisons, and I don't picture them being a better fit at <b>Cartel Camarill</b><b>a</b> than <i>any</i> of those clans. They all have more distinct assets to offer with less problems for the sect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467333#post1467333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A malkavian is more often like an inside man who just happens to be in the field you're interested in, or they have a friend in such a field.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never heard of the Malks operating that way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467333#post1467333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if the Assamites join, they're in a rather shakey possition</div> </div> </div> </div>That's debatable and wholly irrelevant to the discussion at hand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467333#post1467333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Assamites in the Ashirra were renegades,</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they weren't, they were never written as such. Quite the contrary, they were the mainstream clan, where the renegades were their Sabbat <i>Antitribu</i>. This is what is actually written in the books.<br /> <br /> I'll talk more on the matter in another post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467333#post1467333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it's undeniable that these clans are politically a lot further out than their more center-right compatriots in the OG 7.</div> </div> </div> </div>I deny. I hardly see these clans as more extreme in political view with very few caveats. Definitely not the Giovanni and Ravnos. Setites and Assamites have indeed some relevant points, but are far more flexible about them than you pretend. Lasombra and Tzimisce can compromise on their political stances so much that they formed the Sabbat, where they share leadership.<br /> <br /> By the way, the idea that the Lasombra can't compromise on sharing power or the Tzimisce don't think beyond their personal domains is ludicrous when you simply consider their roles in the <b><i>main sect</i></b>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467333#post1467333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Giovanni, I think, have the least issues. But they're obviously out of the Cam because Augustus had a bullshit plan. Honestly, I don't think the Cam would want necromancy to get big.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree fully to the part about Augustus. He inherited from Cappadocius a variation on the second worse Ante goal in Kindred history, only Lasombra is worse (Absimiliard is a greater looser, but doesn't actually have a goal).<br /> <br /> But I don't see why the Camarilla wouldn't want Necromancers, much less why they wouldn't want the strongest group of them, especially since they would be in a better position to stop the clan from doing exactly what you described (something they currently can do anyway without concerns).<br /> <br /> ------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> I'll reserve my next post entirely to discuss the Assamites, FoS and Ravnos. Or maybe I'll split it into up to three posts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T10:34:01-08:00","id":1467365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think going with the original camarilla is fair, and I think I stated what I was going with explicitly enough. I realize &quot;OG&quot; isn't exactly common parlance but I did refer explicitly to the Gangrel. Why do i think this is fair? On one hand, the Camarilla has kept it's original lineup for 500ish years, and all the shakeups have occured within a fraction of it's history. Some people like to play outside of the present day, where smartphones aren't ubiquitous or where they can comfortably have century long timeskips without waking up in Megacity 1. On the otherhand, V1 and V2 have the OG 7, Revised has optional Gehenna scenarios and it's debatable as to whether events like the Week of Nightmares or Gangrel leaving are also optional. V20 is agnostic and is happy to go either way (when/IF the Assamites join... like it's entirely up to the ST) As respectfully as I can describe it: V5's Camarilla is a fundamentally different Beast to the point that it needs a name change because it has very little in common. </div> </div> </div>The original Camarilla, at its founding, attempted to include more clans then the 7, and it's honestly confusing why you keep trying to dismiss this. In Second Edition Vampire, for example, it was noted that the only reason the Tzimisce did not surrender alongside the Brujah at the end of the First Anarch Revolt at Thorns and become part of the Camarilla was their sheer hatred for the Tremere. Which is to say, even in Vampire 2nd ed, the idea that Thorns was an attempt by the Camarilla to in fact fold as many vampire clans as possible into itself was right there. 2nd edition is where we get the actual text of the Treaty of Thorns in the Storyteller's Guide to the Sabbat, where the Camarilla straight up notes its intent that everyone who declared themselves an Anarch in the revolt will be considered part of the Camarilla and receive the full state of being of becoming such. The best you can say is that the Lasombra looked at that and went &quot;it's a trap!&quot;, and said no, because they felt they personally had killed enough Ventrue elders and also their own founder (interestingly the idea that the Tzimisce killed theirs was not something that was considered as having happened in this section of the book at this time in the gameline), such that joining the Camarilla would be an excuse for punishing them. Even then, that's noted as something the Lasombra believed. The Tzimisce only did the same because of their hatred of the Tremere. This was a thing noted innn... 1992, in the Player's Guide to the Sabbat, with the actual text of the treaty provided in 1993. While the actual Convention of Thorns scenario in 1998 in Transylvania Chronicles II would present the situation with certainly more depth and nuance to it and broaden the idea that the Camarilla wanted even the Lasombra, include more clans, deal with various setting details added in the intervening years, the like, the idea that the Camarilla was in fact trying to found itself with more than the seven clans is almost as old as the gameline. They wanted multiple clans beyond the seven to join at founding, even in the game's early days.<br /> <br /> Even the 2e Assamite Clanbook, which is, just to take a personal moment, just hilariously one of the worst clanbooks ever put to print and responsible for a lot of insufferable Assamite player styles over the years (there's a reason a looot of stuff from it got sharp retcons), has the Assamites acknowledge that even from their perspective the Camarilla wanted them folded in (or &quot;subjected to their tyranny&quot;), that indeed, one of the reasons the Assamites hate the Camarilla is because the Camarilla tried to make all vampires Camarilla (which, again just as a side note, when the 2e Assamites of the Assamite Clanbook more or less hate all other clans/vampires, why would they care what the Camarilla wanted to do to other clans? Oh 2e Assamite clanbook, you are a horrible mess). So again, that the Camarilla wanted more than the seven clans they got is not some kind of new idea in the gameline, that clanbook is from the ancient days of... 1995.<br /> <br /> Your attempted definition of the Camarilla and its perspectives requires looking at stuff in canon noted as being part of its very founding and stating you will not acknowledge that. To again remind, the Convention of Thorns was the thing that happened hundreds of years ago at the founding of the Camarilla. Attempting to say the Camarilla was intended as a protection racket for the 7 clans, or some effort to exclude the others, requires ignoring this.<br /> <br /> Revised did not treat the Assamite schism as optional, it defined their entire clanbook by it. That's not actually debatable. Revised did enough metaplot changes it considered canon that one of the things people who were not a fan of revised griped about, was that. Certainly not to the degree that people would gripe about the way Mage Revised non optionally changed its setting, but it was there. You are mistaking the book that for a time ended the entire VtM line and brand in an intended for good way, Gehenna, with several years of books that came before it during a time when VtM still existed. People seem to forget that VtM was straight up shuttered as a brand line for years in favour of the attempt at restarting with the NWoD. There is a period of several years where Vampire the Masquerade was a dead gameline.<br /> <br /> Vampire 20 liked to say it was metaplot agnostic, but frankly as the 20th line rolled onwards, even it started indulging (particularly with the Anarchs and updating them with some choices I found dubious for not thinking out their implications for sheer monstrosity, but that's a different topic). Had Vampire 5th not happened, books like Beckett's Jyhad Diary were helping to set the stage/imply what Onyx Path's looming attempt at a vampire 4th ed would look like (which certainly we'll never see and all).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes. The Camarilla explicitly invited every clan into the Camarilla. I'm well aware. However, how sincere was that offer? I think the Camarilla knew damn-well that the other clans would say no, but extended the olive brand so that nobody would accuse them of not-trying or deliberately excluding a clan; such behaviour would be unfitting for a global body that claims to support all vampires. &quot;we offered, you refused&quot; is a good way of justifying why some clans should get better political representation than others. </div> </div> </div>What you think then is wrong going by actual published setting material. There was a prolonged convention effort to bring in as many clans as possible whose explicit intent was to fold in as many clans as possible. That's just the game material. There's a full out sequence meant for player interaction with that entire basis.<br /> <br /> Again, it's fine if you want to discuss your personal VtM headcanon. The problem is instead putting forward that this is the actual way to read the setting. It's not. The books disagree with you repeatedly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even if the Assamites join, they're in a rather shakey possition due to the effects of the schism and the parts where they're newcomers. Vampires are slow. They take centuries to get established. It'd be foolish to think they could just join a global organization en mass and then be equals within 30 years. Until V5 overturned the boat, the remaining Camarilla clans were in a good possition to exploit the Assamites. (also I've got a lot of doubt about the Gangrel leaving the Camarilla permanently. They'll be back, it's in their best interests) </div> </div> </div>The books did not handle the Assamites joining in the way you feel the Assamites joining should have been handled then. Again, are you wanting to discuss why you feel your headcanon makes sense, or the game material? These are different things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's completely wrong to think the Assamites will adapt well to the Cam because they did alright with the Ashirra </div> </div> </div>Are you arguing that the books that had the Assamites adapt then are wrong?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Assamites in the Ashirra were renegades, outcasts and spies anyway. Schismatics before the Shism. It's completely wrong to think the Assamites will adapt well to the Cam because they did alright with the Ashirra. Maybe I'm standing with Ur-Shulgi too much but Islam isn't at all compatible with Assamite Orthadoxy, and things like Shih sorcery were always considered a sick parody few Assamites embraced. Correct me If I'm wrong but we still know fuck all about the Ashirra in modern nights. One of the earliest sources suggested it was a Saudi/Iran thing and meta wise this was a shot at how overly religious White Wolf thought they were. Other people suggest the Ashirra is the Cam but way better because it's Asian and thus spiritual and we all know how WW had skewed perceptions of anything asian back in the day. </div> </div> </div>There have been Assamites working within the Ashirra since the medieval period who were treated as full venerated members of the Assamite clan while they did so. Major leading figures even. Hillel El Massari, the Prince of Cordoba, a Dark Ages Assamite featured in both Iberia by Night and Veil of Night and referred to as Ashirra was a living legend in his clan. What book are you taking the &quot;the Assamites in the Ashirra were renegades, outcasts and spies&quot; from? Where does it say that? In which book? There are otherwise multiple references in the Dark Ages period that a considerable chunk of Assamites viewed the Ashirra as brothers in arms. The one reference we get in 2e to the Assamites and Ashirra in the modern nights in A World of Darkness refers to them as outright partners with the Hajj (the Ashirra Nosferatu who are a major power within the Ashirra and something of its spiritual leaders) with an alliance apparently so firm, enduring and respectful that there are rumours the Hajj let the Assamites into Mecca whereas they refuse that to all other clans.<br /> <br /> That said, the Ashirra of 2e will get later retconned everywhere from Vampire: the Dark Ages (which presents the fullest take on them that exists as an Islamic sect of vampires that stretches across multiple nations and clans that is present across North Africa, the Middle East, and Spain until the Reconquista boots them out), to Cairo by Night in the modern era in revised (which mostly lines up with the DA version really as far as presenting them as a sect of Islamic vampires of multiple clans and varying levels of influence that exists from North Africa to the Middle East), to Lore of the Bloodlines in V20 (which mostly notes that they buckled so hard to the Camarilla that they gave up the Salubri to them in the early 20th century) to the V5 version of them (that basically lines up with the Dark Ages version of them like all the others, so really it's mostly the one retcon after 2e that just gets further details added to a generally similar thematic umbrella). Of course one of the things about that retcon is that the Assamites, certainly the Islamic ones, regard the Ashirra as allies at least. It's not even much of a retcon as far as the connections between the two considering the way Ashirra/Assamite relations were otherwise described in 2e.<br /> <br /> In 2e, the Ashirra are mostly the Vampires of the Arabian peninsula, who formed a sect largely for reasons of protecting Medina and Mecca, and things got more political from there. They're noted as being loosely affiliated with the Camarilla as an autonomous entity within it, with a concern that they may fully split off into their own thing. The Ashirra and Assamites are referred to as regarding each other with mutual respect and the Assamites are at a point of being quasi affiliated with the group on the whole, working with it to keep the Tremere out of the area and otherwise contest the Followers of Set.<br /> <br /> Where does it say &quot;Shih sorcery were always considered a sick parody...&quot;?<br /> <br /> And indeed, part of what will fuel the schism is Islam being popular enough in the clan such that when Ur Shulgi rises up and goes &quot;nope to that&quot;, a sizable number of Assamites are infuriated by this. So I'm not sure what point you feel you're making there? Enough of the various ways the members of the clan live, regardless of Islam, are incompatible with hardcore Assamite Orthodoxy as defined by Ur Shulgi. It's a plot point. It's why they leave. It's why the loyalist clan loses a majority of the viziers and sorcerers, all the Islamic warriors, and all the warriors otherwise moderate enough to just look at hardcore Assamite Orthodoxy and go &quot;nope&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But it's undeniable that these clans are politically a lot further out than their more center-right compatriots in the OG 7. </div> </div> </div>It's pretty deniable as it again requires taking these clans by their most extreme interpretations while not doing the same for the 7 other clans. The Ventrue alone get explicit mentions as being outright sociopaths, with a clan system designed to produce sociopaths, who do things like pick out mortals and play horrifying games with their lives and wager on if they will break as far as their perception of humanity and what they are willing to do to it. That they are a clan who produces feeding restrictions like &quot;victims of sexual assault&quot;, and well worse beyond that. Now, it could be fairly said that this is taking the most extreme reading of the Ventrue possible. That on the whole the clan, simply for the sheer reason that it still exists, is more varied, nuanced and overall moderate than that. But to be consistent by the standards you are putting forward, we can't say that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Assamites, Lasombra and Giovanni are obsessed with order </div> </div> </div>So are the Ventrue, by this standard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Settites and Ravnos are creatures of Chaos </div> </div> </div>So are the Brujah and Malkavians, by this standard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and the Tzmisce just want everyone to stay the fuck out of their territory with no law but their own </div> </div> </div>So do the Gangrel, by this standard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":".  clarified a thing 11-10-2021, 02:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T11:19:30-08:00","id":1467366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> you're only pissed off because it doesn't agree with your exact idea of perfect line-up. </div> </div> </div>You make it sound like I'm difficult. V5's lineup is... a seperate matter. <br /> I agree; V5 supports my argument far more than the first editions. But I think it's a massive over... well it's not a correction. I think what the V5 Cam are doing is too extreme. I'm thinking about discrimination, not full-blown apartheid. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> they have nothing hinting that it was just a ruse. As far as anyone can tell by reading the actual text, it was completely sincere, despite not unanimous in every case </div> </div> </div>It's not a ruse. I think, at least in part, it was sincere.<br /> But for these clans it meant giving up something. Their Identity perhaps. The Camarilla is a secular institution that officially does not like cults or paths of enlightenment which aren't humanity. The Settites are all in a cult. The Assamites are almost entirely within a cult. The Ravnos have some pretty interesting religion, and most crucially these clans and their leaders are some of the the least agreeable with humanity and are far more road-oriented (even if it's &quot;good&quot; roads like Heaven or Chivalry). I think the Camarilla really would have appreciated the Settites joining them, provided the Settites became secular... which of course the Settites can't do because their magic and perhaps Serpentis is tied so heavily to their faith. At this time, especially For Tzmisce, Lasombra and the Assamites and to some extent the other clans, Joining the Cam was essentially surrender. The Cam knew it was a longshot. <br /> <br /> Then we've got the 7 clans in the Camarilla. Perhaps they didn't intend to make a Cartel when they invited every clan to join, but it's entirely possible they formed protectionist agreements as a result of joining. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I don't see why the Camarilla wouldn't want Necromancers, </div> </div> </div>Other than the distasteful and gratuitous Necrophilia? <br /> <br /> The way I imagine it. Nobody has a ghost problem. And then the people who solve ghost problems show up. And now there are ghosts everywhere (not a coincidence), and now the people who solve ghost problems are solving the ghost problems and making a fortune. Those that don't buy into this scheme have bigger and bigger ghost problems... <br /> <br /> The Small bloodlines are easy to bully if they try this shit. The Giovanni are big enough that they can hold a city hostage with ghosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T11:25:03-08:00","id":1467368,"title":"","content":"The following clans are deeply affected by changes in outlook from the authors. A.K.A. <i>retconing racism out</i>. They all start off as heavily racist and simplistic stereotypes of entire religions.<br /> <br /> So, for them, you have actually two versions that seem the same in the surface, but work differently, and applying the same argument to both isn't constructive. For all of them it is also extremely recommended that you take the retconned version.<br /> <br /> Although no one will stop you from using the first version on your game, <b>the first version is extremely racist, must be acknowledged as such and is unlikely to be well received in the forum as acceptable canon</b>.<br /> <br /> None of those retcons happened at once, and many started early in the WoD publication history but only fully developed at Revised, so it is a process.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Banu Haqim/Assamites</b></i><br /> <br /> The entire idea of the Ashirra and the Web of Knifes are part of the transition from &quot;Old Assamites&quot; to Banu Haqim. And it is far more sensible than many people think, because a lot of aspects that seem as discrepancies and poetic license from the authors to create a more diversified thing <i><b>are actually how the region and the Quran in fact work</b></i>.<br /> <br /> So, the solution of the <i>Assamite Problem</i> was three-fold. On one hand, in the Dark Ages they are reinterpreted as fighting in the Anarch Revolt as allies to the Anarchs, and later fighting the Camarilla, so the European contact with them is mostly through Warrior Caste in an actual war. <i>Those Banu Haqim are actively promoting prejudice against them as to instigate fear</i>, so this creates the stereotype as such IC.<br /> <br /> On the second hand, the <b><i>Web of Knifes</i></b> is created as their modern group of extremist assassins. The Web isn't the majority of the clan and it isn't the majority of the Warrior caste, it is a very strict group while the majority of the clan is far more reclusive or occupied with their business in the Middle East. <i>Those Banu Haqim, very few, but active under several aliases, are the ones the Camarilla really interacts with, explaining their modern interpretation</i>.<br /> <br /> Finally, the Ashirra solves the other problems by providing an actual Middle Eastern vampire community, a reason for the Islamic overtones and a place for the <b>real (Second Version)</b> Banu Haqim to be in. In that, the entire thing ceases to be <i>how the other clans see the Assamites</i> and becomes <i>how the Europeans see the Banu Haqim,</i> as every clan has Middle Eastern members and this version of the clan simply isn't a mystery for them.<br /> <br /> And about how the region and the Quran really work?<br /> <br /> 1 - In the 14th and 15th centuries the <u><b><i>gigantic</i></b></u> region known as the Middle East is objectively more developed than Europe, wealthier, safer, and they never had anything resembling the Inquisition. Receiving and allying with refugees to stop senseless carnage in Europe ( and its spilling to Turkey) is pretty much on spot;<br /> <br /> 2 - The Quran distinguishes between the Faith and the Law. Although it does require that Muslims work towards making the Law of Muhammad in the law of the land, it does not require that unfaithful be persecuted or any similar nonsense, and it didn't happened at the time. So the Ashirra being under Islamic law but not requiring its members to convert, and the same happening inside the clan, is also on spot;<br /> <br /> 3 - Actually, the Quran have three clear definitions that apply not only to all people, <i>but all living things, material or spiritual</i>. They are divided into the Faithful, the Unfaithful, and the Shayatin. The Unfaithful are any person that does not recognize the truth in the Quran, and they are second class citizens to the Faithful, but that's about it. The Shayatin are those who work directly to deviate the Faithful, and while they're kind of equivalent to Christian demons, being the ones who the Muslims must fight against in a Holy War (Jihad), <i>they're not defined by species, power or spiritual nature.</i> They have IRL legends about supernatural creatures, Djinns and Ifriti who were good Muslims. So the idea of vampires being accepted as Muslims? On spot;<br /> <br /> 4 - Just as Christians and Jews at the time, Muslims didn't define sorcery as any work of magic when they condemn it. In fact, the Quran emphasize the positive role of those who study the laws of nature as Allah made them and that includes forms of magic. Bad sorcery is the magic you learn from Shayatin and not just because it is magic, but because it is a lure to make you a sinner. So much so that in the Quran there are angels and saints that not only use magic, but <i>explicitly use the same magic</i><i> as the Shayatin or the Shayatin try to teach people</i>. So, a caste of scholar sorcerers, is, as you see, on spot.<br /> <br /> 5 - More than anything, the Islam is extremely based on the study and the application of law as a science. The Quran is as much a book on Theory of Law as a religious text can be, and it put a greater emphasis on judges than priests. Priests are irrelevant, the Word of Allah is already with you. Judges, though, study and teach the Law and apply it. So a clan of judges and executioners dedicated to making Kindred follow suit, converting <i>en masse</i> to Islam? On spot.<br /> <br /> What else can be said about the Banu Haqim? Canonically they refused to join the Camarilla because they saw the end of the war against the elders who wronged their childer as cowardice and the Anarchs who went with the Cam as traitors. Already at the time the majority of the clan was Muslim, as canonically most of the older members converted. Haqim never asked them not to do such a thing and the Quran never required them to force the change upon others, so non-Muslims existed and were accepted.<br /> <br /> No religious-based schism happened until Ur-Shulgi, and otherwise the creepy bastard blatantly ignored many aspects of the culture of the clan that were already in place at his time. The Schism drove a lot of them out of the clan and I'm not sure if anywhere it is hinted that a majority stayed with him. Viziers and Sorcerers mostly went to the Cam while Warriors go to Sabbat, with very few exceptions in the opposite direction and some of them going Autarkis. It is made clear that the new &quot;Loyalists&quot; of Ur-Shulgi are actually more distant from how the clan were under Haqim than the Muslim version (if Haqim would actually approve of it is another matter).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T11:59:21-08:00","id":1467369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Ravnos have some pretty interesting religion, and most crucially these clans and their leaders are some of the the least agreeable with humanity and are far more road-oriented (even if it's &quot;good&quot; roads like Heaven or Chivalry). </div> </div> </div>The Ravnos leader that spoke out against the Camarilla at Thorns the strongest, calling it a garbage plan for a garbage sect by garbage people (I'm... paraphrasing, but not as much as you might think), did so for reasons of humanity, regarding the Camarilla as nothing but another doomed attempted manipulation of them and calling for humanity to be left alone (she also read the nascent Sabbat for filth, if you're wondering. I don't regard any of her own suggestions for going forward as remotely viable, but all the same, the Ravnos clan delegate calling the Convention of Thorns out did not do so for reasons that have anything to do with what you're talking about).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At this time, especially For Tzmisce, Lasombra and the Assamites and to some extent the other clans, Joining the Cam was essentially surrender. The Cam knew it was a longshot. </div> </div> </div>No, they didn't. They thought that their functional victory in the Anarch Revolt gave them the leverage to create an ecumenical body over all vampires, hence wanting delegates from as many clans as they felt viable and that what they ended up doing with the Assamites was Plan B. Honestly if anything they mucked it up by putting too much stock in believing they would be regarded as victors who could not be denied, to the point that they straight up regarded even attending the convention as acknowledging the authority of the Camarilla. Rafael De Corazon had to outright publicly shame and call out Hardestat to get him to back down from a position towards both vampires and mortals best summed up as:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VZ_ViQxKYL4\" data-code=\"VZ_ViQxKYL4\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/VZ_ViQxKYL4/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> (This is barely an exaggeration. His kind of hilarious dialogue options consist of how much he hates humanity and how as far as vampires he intends to punish everyone who transgressed against him until he decides they are worth forgiving.)<br /> <br /> <br /> While I'm there, for the Brujah, joining the Camarilla actually was surrender, as it required the actual surrender of a rather sizable portion of the clan to even be possible. While some of the Brujah were working with the Founders, a huge chunk of their own clan were one of the main bodies waging the Anarch Revolt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Assamites are almost entirely within a cult. </div> </div> </div>The Assamites are far enough from almost entirely being within a cult that when Ur Shulgi rose and tried to act like that was true, at minimum half the clan left.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then we've got the 7 clans in the Camarilla. Perhaps they didn't intend to make a Cartel when they invited every clan to join, but it's entirely possible they formed protectionist agreements as a result of joining. </div> </div> </div>The Brujah particularly were near literally beaten into joining. That's not what a protectionist agreement is.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":".  better video clip link 11-10-2021, 03:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T12:04:29-08:00","id":1467370,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Remember people that this is not meant to be frustrating.</span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T12:21:28-08:00","id":1467371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467366#post1467366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But for these clans it meant giving up something.</div> </div> </div> </div>No more than for the others. The Ventrue definitely weren't keen on being on Humanity more than any of the Six. Gangrel, Toreador, Nosferatu, Malkavian and Brujah all gave up some of their &quot;identity&quot; as they joined, since Dark Ages also shows they had a lot of other things about them at the time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467366#post1467366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Camarilla is a secular institution</div> </div> </div> </div>And there's a key difference between Secular and Atheistic. A secular institution doesn't care about your religion as long as you don't push your religion on others. The idea is that the laws and works of the institution shouldn't be defined by religion.<br /> <br /> Something most religions are actually ok with. Even Islam does not care if the law is defined by religion, as long as it follows their vision of the law. And depending on your reading of the Quran it isn't a big deal.<br /> <br /> The Setites, Assamites and Ravnos don't care if the rest of Kindred society follow their particular religions, the Camarilla only cares about their religions if it goes against its laws, and if you go for the second version of Path of Paradox as a way to understand Ravnos religion, none of them goes. Are there caveats to this? Yes, but nothing that affects everyday life.<br /> <br /> Even the biggest religious enemy of the Cam, Noddism, they barely did anything about except offer the official party line that &quot;this is bullshit&quot;. No crime on believing bullshit, though. And those clans don't care about other people thinking their beliefs are bullshit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467366#post1467366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">officially does not like ... paths of enlightenment which aren't humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true, and again something that every one at Thorns had to come at gripes with as almost no clan had that many Humanity followers. But few Kindred religions are actually sufficiently contrary to Humanity for that to matter in the political scale of Thorns.<br /> <br /> Assamites? Defend mortals from predators. Setites? Find truth (and help Set, which is actually just as arcane and undefined for most of them). Ravnos? Also find truth, with differing overtones. No one is required to kill outside defense of others or self, no one is required to commit crimes, no matter how much some of them like those unsavory interpretations.<br /> <br /> Nothing different from the OG-7.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467366#post1467366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Cam knew it was a longshot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unlikely. As the say goes, everything is clear in hindsight. As things could be seen at the time, every outcome was possible. The only person who was sure even about their own clan joining was Goratrix, because he's an idiot. The clan actually joined because of Meerlinda's work behind the scenes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467366#post1467366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but it's entirely possible they formed protectionist agreements as a result of joining.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possible, not canon. And I don't think it is likely, just possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467366#post1467366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other than the distasteful and gratuitous Necrophilia?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it really more distasteful and gratuitous than anything else vampires do?<br /> <br /> You must remember they are all walking corpses. The most necrophiliac clan is by far the Toreador, in the end.<br /> <br /> But I already addressed your proposal of Ghost Hunting scheme. Nothing stops the Giovanni doing it now, except fear of reprisal. The difference would be that it is actually easier to enact reprisal against a clan in the fold than an independent force.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T15:15:24-08:00","id":1467383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467365#post1467365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even the 2e Assamite Clanbook, which is, just to take a personal moment, just hilariously one of the worst clanbooks ever put to print</div> </div> </div> </div>Why's that? Maybe you disagree with the original concept and scope of the Assamite clan, I don't know, but I don't see how the actual writing of <i>Clanbook: Assamite</i> is subpar compared to any other clanbook. Graeme Davis was an industry veteran who cut his teeth on Warhammer in the 80s and came into RPG freelance work from an academic background. &quot;One of the worst clanbooks ever put to print&quot; are pretty bold words to describe the work of someone with Davis's merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T15:24:23-08:00","id":1467385,"title":"","content":"Recapitulating:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467368#post1467368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The following clans are deeply affected by changes in outlook from the authors. A.K.A. <i>retconing racism out</i>. They all start off as heavily racist and simplistic stereotypes of entire religions.<br /> <br /> So, for them, you have actually two versions that seem the same in the surface, but work differently, and applying the same argument to both isn't constructive. For all of them it is also extremely recommended that you take the retconned version.<br /> <br /> Although no one will stop you from using the first version on your game, <b>the first version is extremely racist, must be acknowledged as such and is unlikely to be well received in the forum as acceptable canon</b>.<br /> <br /> None of those retcons happened at once, and many started early in the WoD publication history but only fully developed at Revised, so it is a process.</div> </div> </div> </div><b><i>Followers of Set</i></b><br /> <br /> One interesting aspect of the FoS is how subtle the transition went. That is a strikingly good work at storytelling, but had the downside of being hard to notice the transition and getting the new form without a lot of attention.<br /> <br /> What made this possible was their choice at new core religion for the Setites: Gnosticism, a dualism philosophy that teaches the separation between a Real world of Pure Knowledge and a False world of Fictional Matter. For this philosophy the goal of humans is Gnosis (Enlightenment), but Gnosis can be obtained only through personal experience. The goal is freedom from the material world and its bindings, and ascendance into the sphere of God.<br /> <br /> For Gnosticism strict doctrines are traps for the soul, and gods that teach a ritualized life are jailers for their followers. It doesn't mean that the teachings are wrong by themselves, but that following them out of blind obligation keep you from achieving spiritual knowledge over the matter. Some gods, though, offer guidance to achieve Gnosis instead of seeking blind obedience.<br /> <br /> This theological construct is at the same time flexible in form but distinct in its implications. Conflicting myths, for example, aren't a problem, as no doctrine is far from the truth if it leads you to seek personal Gnosis instead of claiming to be Gnosis in itself. But any teaching that deviates you from seeking truth on your own is heretical.<br /> <br /> So the actual Setite religion has nothing to do with the trappings of Egyptian Mythology, no more than it have with any other religion. Yet at the same time they have no reason to abandon it, either. They may accept freely variations that use other trappings, other names for entities, and even discuss openly if the gods act out of malice or ignorance. At the same time, they combat heresies whose teachings seem like almost the same to outsiders, but just because they have the same trappings, but not the principles.<br /> <br /> Practically speaking, what does that means?<br /> <br /> 1 - Followers of Set aim for enlightenment and ascension. Some only for themselves, some for the clan, others for everyone;<br /> <br /> 2 - Corruption is a looser term than it seems. They differ on what they mean by it and on what they do with it;<br /> <br /> 3 - Set is seen as a teacher more than a lord. Although he is important to them all, nothing else about him means the same for every Setite;<br /> <br /> 4 - There's a difference between institutions with clear rules and purposes, and institutions you follow just out of tradition. This isn't lost on all of them;<br /> <br /> 5 - Most of them see indulgence as a means to free yourself from desire. Other paths may exist and the goal is asceticism, not vice in itself;<br /> <br /> 6 - Roads and Paths are just sample guides to Gnosis. A faithful Setite may follow almost any Path, even Humanity;<br /> <br /> 7 - Denouncing tradition, institutions, religion and morals isn't the same as saying you should be an evil bastard. Some Setites think so, others don't;<br /> <br /> 8 - You can iterate those teachings in infinite ways and add whatever trappings you want and the end result will still be an &quot;orthodox&quot; Setite;<br /> <br /> 9 - Not all of them are orthodox, though. The clan's disposition towards an actual heresy depends a lot on context, going from indifference to war.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T15:37:31-08:00","id":1467388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467383#post1467383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why's that? Maybe you disagree with the original concept and scope of the Assamite clan, I don't know, but I don't see how the actual writing of <i>Clanbook: Assamite</i> is subpar compared to any other clanbook. Graeme Davis was an industry veteran who cut his teeth on Warhammer in the 80s and came into RPG freelance work from an academic background. &quot;One of the worst clanbooks ever put to print&quot; are pretty bold words to describe the work of someone with Davis's merits.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It approaches the Clan from a perspective that sets them above all other vampires, while also setting them as holding all other vampires in murderous contempt with an ultimate goal of destroying them, and thus weds the two perspectives together, and a lot of players took that for truth, everything from the &quot;Haqim embraced himself&quot; to &quot;the Assamite Clan fought the entire Camarilla by itself, without any help, for three straight years after the Anarch Revolt ended because the Clan was just that badass&quot; on down. There's a level of sheer pervasive smugness coursing through it, that is just eyerolling. If the goal of the book was to make the clan feel as unplayable in groups as it possibly could have, it certainly came very close to hitting that mark. If that wasn't the goal of the book, then I have no idea what was. <br /> <br /> Also it just has a really narrow take on the clan. Now, that's not a unique sin of the Clanbook, early VtM pretty often treated the clans as stereotypes, but just piled with everything else and ugh. I bounced off the book pretty hard.<br /> <br /> And all of that is without even touching the unfortunate way it handled cultural and religious issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 11-10-2021, 06:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T19:06:18-08:00","id":1467402,"title":"","content":"What Goats Do The Camarilla Have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T19:34:03-08:00","id":1467405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467385#post1467385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Recapitulating:<br /> <br /> <b><i>Followers of Set</i></b><br /> <br /> One interesting aspect of the FoS is how subtle the transition went. That is a strikingly good work at storytelling, but had the downside of being hard to notice the transition and getting the new form without a lot of attention.<br /> <br /> What made this possible was their choice at new core religion for the Setites: Gnosticism, a dualism philosophy that teaches the separation between a Real world of Pure Knowledge and a False world of Fictional Matter. For this philosophy the goal of humans is Gnosis (Enlightenment), but Gnosis can be obtained only through personal experience. The goal is freedom from the material world and its bindings, and ascendance into the sphere of God.<br /> <br /> For Gnosticism strict doctrines are traps for the soul, and gods that teach a ritualized life are jailers for their followers. It doesn't mean that the teachings are wrong by themselves, but that following them out of blind obligation keep you from achieving spiritual knowledge over the matter. Some gods, though, offer guidance to achieve Gnosis instead of seeking blind obedience.<br /> <br /> This theological construct is at the same time flexible in form but distinct in its implications. Conflicting myths, for example, aren't a problem, as no doctrine is far from the truth if it leads you to seek personal Gnosis instead of claiming to be Gnosis in itself. But any teaching that deviates you from seeking truth on your own is heretical.<br /> <br /> So the actual Setite religion has nothing to do with the trappings of Egyptian Mythology, no more than it have with any other religion. Yet at the same time they have no reason to abandon it, either. They may accept freely variations that use other trappings, other names for entities, and even discuss openly if the gods act out of malice or ignorance. At the same time, they combat heresies whose teachings seem like almost the same to outsiders, but just because they have the same trappings, but not the principles.<br /> <br /> Practically speaking, what does that means?<br /> <br /> 1 - Followers of Set aim for enlightenment and ascension. Some only for themselves, some for the clan, others for everyone;<br /> <br /> 2 - Corruption is a looser term than it seems. They differ on what they mean by it and on what they do with it;<br /> <br /> 3 - Set is seen as a teacher more than a lord. Although he is important to them all, nothing else about him means the same for every Setite;<br /> <br /> 4 - There's a difference between institutions with clear rules and purposes, and institutions you follow just out of tradition. This isn't lost on all of them;<br /> <br /> 5 - Most of them see indulgence as a means to free yourself from desire. Other paths may exist and the goal is asceticism, not vice in itself;<br /> <br /> 6 - Roads and Paths are just sample guides to Gnosis. A faithful Setite may follow almost any Path, even Humanity;<br /> <br /> 7 - Denouncing tradition, institutions, religion and morals isn't the same as saying you should be an evil bastard. Some Setites think so, others don't;<br /> <br /> 8 - You can iterate those teachings in infinite ways and add whatever trappings you want and the end result will still be an &quot;orthodox&quot; Setite;<br /> <br /> 9 - Not all of them are orthodox, though. The clan's disposition towards an actual heresy depends a lot on context, going from indifference to war.</div> </div> </div> </div>My take on the subject of the Setites coming down on the non-Typhonists is based around multiple motivations.<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Power</b>: The Fire Court wishes to reign in the rest of the Clan and accusations of heresy are as good a reason to come down on them as any.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Doctrinal drift</b>: I am fully of the mind that orthodox Typhonism is a morally bankrupt horrifying philosophy that revels in evil. It is against most traditions of Gnosticism and their views are only superificially similar as Set represents the worst of behaviors as a way to liberate the soul.<br /> <br /> Other Setites, not the least being Damballa, are heretical because they're not a bunch of evil bastards or at least don't consider reveling in your own depravity a form of enlightenment.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>The Nature of Paths</b>: Kindred morality is, in simple terms, not as flexible as that of regular humans. A human being who wanders from the way is going to have to go through some soul-searching and maybe find a new way to live. A Kindred who loses faith may end up eating rats out of a dumpster and sleeping under cardboard because he's forgotten how to speak.<br /> <br /> Doubly so with Path followers.<br /> <br /> 4. <b>Spite</b>: You can bet that the internal conflict of the Ministry is as much driven by ancient grievances and petty grudges as anything real.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T22:39:51-08:00","id":1467415,"title":"","content":"The thing is, at the convention of thorns, the Brujah surrendered to... Other Brujah, who helped reassure them that they wouldn't get fucked for joining the Camarilla. The Brujah aren't a very united clan and the Anarch revolt was a conflict of Young Vs Old, it was only when clans were exceptionally successful on one side, Like with the Lasombra or Tzmisce or Giovanni, or when young and old were on the same page, as with the Assamites and very probably the Settites and Ravnos, that the convention of thorns became a clan-wide surrender. I think if the Convention of thorns didn't occur when it did, many of the factors that caused resistance to it would've faded, however if it didn't occur when it did, maybe the imputus for it wouldn't have been there. I think the Camarilla should've repeated the invitations at least every 100 years if they really wanted to get everyone in on it. <br /> <br /> Augustus probably feared that the Camarilla would use this opportunity to eat him. He would lose a lot of control over his family if he joined the Camarilla. <br /> <br /> The Tzmisce and Lasombra didn't have anyone of sufficient age that was willing to join the Camarilla and appeal for good surrender terms for the rebellious unfilial neonates that devestated them. There's some very inhumane roads among these clans too. <br /> Honestly, I do question the Tzmisce's hatred for Tremere. By this point, the omen wars are a conflict so long that nobody can really remember why it's still going, and the Tzmisce have killed most of their own veterans and the elders that pushed them into the war. It's probably a red herring. <br /> <br /> The Assamites under the Camarilla would lose a lot of their ability to cure the Tremere curse within the Camarilla. I find it funny that they join the Camarilla as soon as they lose the curse, as if Ur-Shulgi was some kind of Haquim 4d chess move. IIRC the path of blood wasn't such a big thing at this point in time, or it wasn't as bad... or something. So joining the Cam now is surrender, but joining later would be a good idea... Yet at the same time, the Cam probably only wants the Assamites to join at this moment because Peace keeping Tremere curse&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Horrifically dangerous Baali curse. <br /> <br /> Most Settite roads are extremely inhumane. Also, I suspect the FoS wouldn't really &quot;Anarch revolt&quot; as hard as other clans, being a brainwashed cult and all. No was an inevitable answer to the Camarilla at this point. <br /> <br /> Ravnos are mostly on Paradox. Even the nicer variations of Paradox hate Humanity specifically, and push Ravnos towards independence as they complete their individual destinies. Most Vampires have significant dislike of Ravnos. At this point, it's fairly certain that the Ravnos would only be invited into the Camarilla because the Camarilla wants to control them. No Ravnos would feel comfortable representing all the Ravnos in the Camarilla, as that would harm fulfilling their individual destinies. Only something like the Week of Nightmares would really get the Ravnos to submit as a whole to the Camarilla, and no such thing happened during the Anarch revolt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T02:27:19-08:00","id":1467420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The thing is, at the convention of thorns, the Brujah surrendered to... Other Brujah, who helped reassure them that they wouldn't get fucked for joining the Camarilla. </div> </div> </div>In Lore of the Clans in Vampire 20th, the edition you say you want to acknowledge, according to the Brujah themselves, the considerable majority of their elders were themselves Anarchs, and they surrendered because they thought that the Ventrue imposed terms in the Treaty of Thorns could be exploited for their arrogant mistakes and oversight that they believed gave them massive loopholes to the point of going &quot;ha ha! we somehow secretly won!&quot; (I am not, it should be said, a personal fan of this narrative, but it's there. At least it's only what the Brujah think to themselves happened.)<br /> <br /> In the Transylvania Chronicles in-depth take on Thorns before that, they surrendered because they lost and didn't have the reasons the other clans did to decide after Thorns to keep fighting anyway, as far as those clans' deep ideological objections to ideas like the Masquerade (which, it should be noted, even significant portions of the 7 Camarilla clans were not themselves fully onboard with until the negotiations of Thorns itself and Corazon's big ol speech. It was entirely the case that they themselves had to be sold on the idea as well), or too much pride in the end to want to yield.<br /> <br /> So neither of these things from the game agree with you.<br /> <br /> Now, in much earlier vampire 2e this is more accurate, save for that this was only possible because the Other Brujah were composed of former Anarch elders who broke earlier and abandoned their own cause to become Camarilla. But, if you now want to acknowledge early Vampire 2e as the only thing you want to acknowledge, you're left with the problem of that you also don't want to acknowledge the early 2e reason for why the Tzimisce didn't join. It feels inconsistent.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Brujah aren't a very united clan and the Anarch revolt was a conflict of Young Vs Old, it was only when clans were exceptionally successful on one side </div> </div> </div>Enough Brujah fought on the Anarch side that at times it came off like the entire clan within considerable geographic areas was doing so. Things like the Furore and Promethean movements going full violent made it seem like the Brujah were at times the leaders of the movement (or certainly that is what the Brujah like to tell themselves as far as their own narratives in revised and other places, but there are places that objectively note that there were stages of the Anarch revolt where the Brujah were basically its third pillar just fine, that make the Camarilla siding Brujah feel like a far smaller group). What it came down to for that clan was that they lost and they broke, some earlier and some later (or, if you go by V20's Brujah in clan perspective, apparently they thought this was a grand opportunity to take advantage of a badly written treaty offer. That narrator is at times hilarious. Stating that while the odds were insurmountable, that the real reason they feel the Anarchs lost was because they lost their moral purity, thereby &quot;defeating ourselves&quot;, near verbatim dialogue). Part of why Thorns happened, particularly in earlier stages of the game, was that the Anarchs themselves were suing for peace, an appeal that had the Anarch Brujah out at the front of making in response to the kicking they took. There was a reason the Camarilla thought it was holding all the cards this time to establish its widespread rule and succeed where a somewhat earlier attempt to proclaim all vampires Camarilla didn't manage to take. Even the Lasombra and Tzimisce delegates that came to Thorns admitted they had lost. As demonstrated by the fact that they showed up to Thorns to engage in its discourse, sending important figures to do so even, and also that even when later deciding to remain defiant, they outright admitted &quot;we lost&quot;, in those words. They just ultimately decided they could not accept the negotiations that then ensued and the terms they resulted in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the Camarilla should've repeated the invitations at least every 100 years if they really wanted to get everyone in on it. </div> </div> </div>They straight up tried twice. The first time was met with a varied mix of disinterest, disbelief due to the failure of vaguely similar efforts centuries before, or an inability to respond due to being in the middle of open warfare, depending on the clan or given vampire. The second time came decades after, when they had won their battles and could now present themselves as the victors of the Anarch Revolt, being sued for peace by those very Anarchs. You can keep doubting that they really wanted to get everyone in on it, but the explicit narration of the build up to Thorns it is noted that those who were working to create the Camarilla did so from the belief that it would serve to unite all vampires. The actual line from Chronicles being &quot;they believed that such an organization would bring together all Cainites*, thus leading the childer back into the fold and ending their destructive rampages.&quot; It doesn't get much clearer than objective third person narration going &quot;they believed that such an organization would bring together all Cainites&quot; as far as what the Camarilla intended and how they straight up believed they could get whole clans beyond the 7 to join.<br /> <br /> (*it was pre Thorns, kindred was not a popular term for vampires yet)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Tzmisce and Lasombra didn't have anyone of sufficient age that was willing to join the Camarilla and appeal for good surrender terms for the rebellious unfilial neonates that devestated them. There's some very inhumane roads among these clans too. </div> </div> </div>Again, the Brujah themselves believe that the terms of Thorns were set down by the Ventrue in an effort to cruelly oppress them and not offer good surrender terms, just that the Ventrue were big ol dummies and or possibly sabotaged by the Tremere, and the Brujah thus secretly conned them by accepting (I feel like I need some flashing &quot;This is what the Brujah actually believe&quot; subtitles to underscore just how out there this perspective is, but it is their perspective). They refer to their own elders as having in the majority been with the Anarchs at the time. That's from V20, the edition you have put forward as the one you want to acknowledge other than very early second edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Honestly, I do question the Tzmisce's hatred for Tremere. By this point, the omen wars are a conflict so long that nobody can really remember why it's still going, and the Tzmisce have killed most of their own veterans and the elders that pushed them into the war. It's probably a red herring. </div> </div> </div>The book in which it is stated, states it as the objective reason. It's not from first person narration. It's the guy who wrote both the 2e player's guide to the Sabbat and 2e storyteller's guide to the Sabbat writing that as objective definition. There's no room it allows for you to claim that. When I ask if you want to discuss your headcanon, or the actual game, this is part of why.<br /> <br /> Actual line:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Tzimisces were the bitter enemies of the Tremere and<br /> would never accept defeat to them. </div> </div> </div>You've stated you want to base your take on things from pre revised content. This is pre revised content so far before revised that it's from the very beginning of second edition. I'm not really sure what can otherwise be said there.<br /> <br /> Certainly later products in the game will broaden and deepen and even somewhat change the reasons those clans refused the Treaty of Thorns (the Tzimisce refusal becomes for far more for ideological reasons for example), but even those reasons don't intersect with the claims you want to make.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I find it funny that they join the Camarilla as soon as they lose the curse, as if Ur-Shulgi was some kind of Haquim 4d chess move. </div> </div> </div>They joined the Camarilla out of a mix of terror and disgust at Ur Shulgi and the way of existing he demands they abide by, as far as canon.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So joining the Cam now is surrender, but joining later would be a good idea... </div> </div> </div>The Assamites as they existed at the Convention of Thorns did not have the motivating factor of a horrifying godlike methuselah demanding they forsake all ways of life it deems unworthy or be killed to make them look at the Camarilla as something to jump ship to for safety. They also thought that if they joined the Camarilla at Thorns they would be turned into its weapons. Their entire goal at Thorns was to still surrender to the Camarilla to save themselves, but to achieve doing so in a way that preserved some scrap of their independence outside of the Camarilla/let them refuse to join it, thinking they had the leeway to negotiate to do so. The entire goal of the Schismatic Assamites during the time of the schism changed to &quot;not be wiped out by Ur Shulgi.&quot; I'm not sure why you want to downplay the horror and revulsion he stoked within them? The setting is pretty clear and explicit on all these sorts of things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ravnos are mostly on Paradox. </div> </div> </div>In the era of time in which Thorns occurred, big ol chunks of the clan were not, to the point of entire Ravnos sub units not being on it, as regards groups like the Phaedymites and several others beyond them. In the modern era, there are any number of Ravnos not on Paradox just fine (even before the Week of Nightmares), to the point of a variety of Ravnos npcs being nowhere near it. Even Khalil, the Ravnos npc who got a ton of face time in the material, horrible piece of crap that he is, was just low humanity.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even the nicer variations of Paradox hate Humanity specifically, </div> </div> </div>You mean the ones that consider killing a human being a path sin once you're even at 7 on it, or the ones that go so far as to say the embrace should rarely if ever be given for that it generally robs humans of their destiny? These paths only hate what they term &quot;excessive&quot; humanity in vampires, and given.. most vampires, that's not likely to come up a lot. It's largely some specific issue with ultra humane vampires/those seeking Golconda. To say this is a tiny portion of vampires is to put it mildly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most Vampires have significant dislike of Ravnos </div> </div> </div>And yet, the original intent of the Camarilla was, as noted above &quot;bring together all Cainites.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No Ravnos would feel comfortable representing all the Ravnos in the Camarilla, as that would harm fulfilling their individual destinies. </div> </div> </div>The Clan's entire Indian hierarchy disagrees with this statement pretty hard. Even beyond that, once again, Beckett's Jyhad Diary had Ravnos joining the Camarilla as a plot thread and becoming primogen of their own kind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Only something like the Week of Nightmares would really get the Ravnos to submit as a whole to the Camarilla, and no such thing happened during the Anarch revolt. </div> </div> </div>It's difficult to parse what point you feel you are making in this statement? Yes, the Ravnos had any number of reasons not to submit to the Camarilla. That doesn't change that the Camarilla totally wanted them to submit to them/join. Even the Camarilla's very first &quot;hey guess what, everyone is Camarilla now&quot; attempt was specifically directed at the Ravnos as well. The Ravnos were noted as refusing due to &quot;being concerned with their own agendas.&quot; That's the actual line. In fact the actual line is &quot;The Setites and Ravnos were too concerned with their own agendas to join as a clan.&quot; And again, the actual, direct from the books line is that the Camarilla really believed they would be a unifying force to all vampires. That they didn't manage it, doesn't change that.<br /> <br /> You attempted to say things like, the Camarilla never wanted anyone besides the OG 7 to join, or that the Camarilla thought the other clans joining was a longshot, or that the Camarilla was intended as a protection pact between the 7 clans, etc. etc. The quotable setting material I am citing to you does not agree with these things that you say. It's difficult to see how much more clearly this can be demonstrated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":".  there were more than two sub families who didn't go for paradox especially. 11-11-2021, 05:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T02:46:32-08:00","id":1467424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467388#post1467388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It approaches the Clan from a perspective that sets them above all other vampires, while also setting them as holding all other vampires in murderous contempt with an ultimate goal of destroying them, and thus weds the two perspectives together, and a lot of players took that for truth, everything from the &quot;Haqim embraced himself&quot; to &quot;the Assamite Clan fought the entire Camarilla by itself, without any help, for three straight years after the Anarch Revolt ended because the Clan was just that badass&quot; on down. There's a level of sheer pervasive smugness coursing through it, that is just eyerolling. If the goal of the book was to make the clan feel as unplayable in groups as it possibly could have, it certainly came very close to hitting that mark. If that wasn't the goal of the book, then I have no idea what was.<br /> <br /> Also it just has a really narrow take on the clan. Now, that's not a unique sin of the Clanbook, early VtM pretty often treated the clans as stereotypes, but just piled with everything else and ugh. I bounced off the book pretty hard.<br /> <br /> And all of that is without even touching the unfortunate way it handled cultural and religious issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems to me that your primary objections fall under the umbrella of &quot;disagreeing with the original concept and scope of the Assamites,&quot; which is fair enough. The original clanbooks were not intended for reimagining the clans as initially presented in the core and the various player guides -- that was the explicit goal of the <i>Revised</i> project -- but to be faithful to the original vision for each clan. As a consequence, if you hate the original Assamite concept, or the original Ravnos concept, or whatever, you are without a doubt going to hate the first clanbooks for them as well.<br /> <br /> In later years I've come to terms with the way the early writers approached 'clan' as a concept. Although the 13 largest groups of vampires in the setting were referred to using the same term, they were not designed to be used equally by players and GMs alike. That is to say, 1st and 2nd Edition <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> did not assume that players were as equally likely to play an Assamite as they were, say, a Brujah. There was a fairly sharp distinction between the original seven clans, which expressed very broad and instantly recognizable archetypes, and all the additional groups that did not fit established vampire society. The independents (and later the Sabbat) were deliberately designed to be much more narrow in scope.<br /> <br /> I would rather leave aside the cultural and religious issues of the original Assamite depiction. Talking about the matter is nearly always an endless swamp of minute disagreements and accusations of bigotry. In general, anonymous users disparaging the work of authors who have since moved on from the franchise and thus have little chance of responding to the points raised tends to leave a bad taste in my mouth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T03:25:22-08:00","id":1467425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467424#post1467424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems to me that your primary objections fall under the umbrella of &quot;disagreeing with the original concept and scope of the Assamites,&quot; which is fair enough. The original clanbooks were not intended for reimagining the clans as initially presented in the core and the various player guides -- that was the explicit goal of the <i>Revised</i> project -- but to be faithful to the original vision for each clan. As a consequence, if you hate the original Assamite concept, or the original Ravnos concept, or whatever, you are without a doubt going to hate the first clanbooks for them as well.<br /> <br /> In later years I've come to terms with the way the early writers approached 'clan' as a concept. Although the 13 largest groups of vampires in the setting were referred to using the same term, they were not designed to be used equally by players and GMs alike. That is to say, 1st and 2nd Edition <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> did not assume that players were as equally likely to play an Assamite as they were, say, a Brujah. There was a fairly sharp distinction between the original seven clans, which expressed very broad and instantly recognizable archetypes, and all the additional groups that did not fit established vampire society. The independents (and later the Sabbat) were deliberately designed to be much more narrow in scope.<br /> <br /> I would rather leave aside the cultural and religious issues of the original Assamite depiction. Talking about the matter is nearly always an endless swamp of minute disagreements and accusations of bigotry. In general, anonymous users disparaging the work of authors who have since moved on from the franchise and thus have little chance of responding to the points raised tends to leave a bad taste in my mouth.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can't really agree that second edition particularly didn't want to treat all kinds of clans as playable. Second edition is the edition where the Sabbat got their own player's and ST guides almost right out of the gate for the sole purpose of making them playable. The Clanbooks themselves (at least until you started getting stuff like Baali, and even there..) weren't meant as some &quot;GM only&quot; thing, they were meant for players to encourage them to buy these books with their offers of funky new powers and merits and takes and etc.<br /> <br /> Said another way, I am pretty sure that the idea was to make whatever all things playable as 2e rolled along, even if only for the purpose of selling more books. It's just that the execution sometimes failed really hard. Sometimes things in VtM are just badly written. This is true of every edition, even the ones I personally really like.<br /> <br /> For example, the 2e Assamite clanbook in fact specifically goes out of its way to have guidelines for playing Assamites in mixed groups. It just does so in some of the most acrimonious, poor gaming advice ideas ways it can, even admitting its suggestions are bad/probably doomed. It goes full Doylist/Watsonian (or Thermian logic, if you prefer) clash by saying that the best way to play Assamites are in all Assamite or all Black Hand groups, without acknowledging that the only reason this is true is because the Clanbook decided to double down and write the Clan as that deeply abrasively awful and incompatible.<br /> <br /> It would not take long for various things from this book to start getting retcons/reframing, even in second edition.<br /> <br /> That aside, Vampire: The Dark Ages would come out not that long after this clanbook (1 year after) with the Assamites included as one of the 13 core rulebook clans and just straight up listed as a player choice in that usual creation summary chart thing. There was definitely an intent within VtM for them to be considered just as playable as anything else as 2e rolled along. The game was just bad at this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would rather leave aside the cultural and religious issues of the original Assamite depiction. Talking about the matter is nearly always an endless swamp of minute disagreements and accusations of bigotry. In general, anonymous users disparaging the work of authors who have since moved on from the franchise and thus have little chance of responding to the points raised tends to leave a bad taste in my mouth. </div> </div> </div>That's fine, but I would note that it doesn't make the issues go away. Honestly the main reason I don't cite it as a primary objection is not feeling like I have the energy to dive into what would be the acrimony of that particular topic.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also being real an earlier poster in this thread tackled a variety of it way better than I could have when talking about the Assamites and the problems of their pre revised depiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 11-11-2021, 06:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T03:48:58-08:00","id":1467426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467405#post1467405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My take on the subject of the Setites coming down on the non-Typhonists is based around multiple motivations.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is that isn't canon either way. The official lore presents far many variations on the clan, and only some really get the hammer by the central temple. By the way, the Damballah aren't considered heretical, although observed for eventual branding.<br /> <br /> And the reasons why I don't think this is common, despite the fact that the clan does have a centralizing &quot;Vatican&quot; and Typhonists are usually jerks:<br /> <br /> 1 - On a matter of doctrine, two very common and quite important tenets, that are included on Typhon, are to always work towards Set resurrection and never impedes the work of fellow Followers. This puts a direct barrier on overt or frequent actions against divergence, as you need justification to act against them far more than they need to be quirky.<br /> <br /> Isolating, bullying and focusing on spreading the Faith more than them is a more effective way to work your own power base in this regard.<br /> <br /> 2 - <b>Path is not religion</b>. Despite their link, they are not the same. You can believe in many different things and still follow a given Path. It is perfectly possible for a FoS that strictly observes Typhon's teachings to be on Path of Humanity.<br /> <br /> Of course, the authors don't have a consistent understanding on this regard, but the simple truth of it is revealed in the distinction between the two most common FoS Paths, Typhon and Sutekh: they're actually the same Path, but under very different reasoning and ethics. Typhon wants you to be a jerk, Sutekh wants you to be a guide for the lost.<br /> <br /> While religion and philosophy are integral aspects of any Path, the goal of a Path isn't to reflect your beliefs, but to placate the Beast. The Cult of Set isn't all that concerned with placating the Beast, though, but with following its own religion of personal enlightenment. Curiously, enlightenment that isn't equated to rank in your Path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T06:37:51-08:00","id":1467438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467425#post1467425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't really agree that second edition particularly didn't want to treat all kinds of clans as playable. Second edition is the edition where the Sabbat got their own player's and ST guides almost right out of the gate for the sole purpose of making them playable. The Clanbooks themselves (at least until you started getting stuff like Baali, and even there..) weren't meant as some &quot;GM only&quot; thing, they were meant for players to encourage them to buy these books with their offers of funky new powers and merits and takes and etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>No no, I did not mean to imply that the additional clans after the core seven were at any point intended to be for GMs only. They were, as you rightly point out, initially introduced in various <i>Player's Guides,</i> after all.<br /> <br /> The distinction I would make is more subtle than a binary idea of player clans versus NPC clans. It seems self-evidently clear to me that the original seven clans were intended to be the primary player clans, and that the additional clans introduced afterwards were for character concepts on the fringes of Kindred society. This is why all the independent clan concepts in particular are much more narrow than any of the core clans, even including the Tremere -- weird and insular cults, a single family line, and so on.<br /> <br /> It's precisely the notion that the early game 'failed really hard' or was 'badly written' that I want to push against. Like you, I used to think that all the 13 clans were supposed to have conceptual 'parity', since I was introduced to the game well after the Revised era had rolled in, and during that edition the independent clan depictions in particular had developed toward broader concepts than initially written. However, while all the clans introduced later into the game were explicitly playable from the start, they were by no means meant to have the broad appeal and archetypal nature of clans like Brujah or Ventrue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1190,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","user":"Elphilm","date":". 11-11-2021, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T08:36:05-08:00","id":1467449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467424#post1467424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems to me that your primary objections fall under the umbrella of &quot;disagreeing with the original concept and scope of the Assamites,&quot; which is fair enough. The original clanbooks were not intended for reimagining the clans as initially presented in the core and the various player guides -- that was the explicit goal of the <i>Revised</i> project -- but to be faithful to the original vision for each clan. As a consequence, if you hate the original Assamite concept, or the original Ravnos concept, or whatever, you are without a doubt going to hate the first clanbooks for them as well.<br /> <br /> In later years I've come to terms with the way the early writers approached 'clan' as a concept. Although the 13 largest groups of vampires in the setting were referred to using the same term, they were not designed to be used equally by players and GMs alike. That is to say, 1st and 2nd Edition <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> did not assume that players were as equally likely to play an Assamite as they were, say, a Brujah. There was a fairly sharp distinction between the original seven clans, which expressed very broad and instantly recognizable archetypes, and all the additional groups that did not fit established vampire society. The independents (and later the Sabbat) were deliberately designed to be much more narrow in scope.<br /> <br /> I would rather leave aside the cultural and religious issues of the original Assamite depiction. Talking about the matter is nearly always an endless swamp of minute disagreements and accusations of bigotry. In general, anonymous users disparaging the work of authors who have since moved on from the franchise and thus have little chance of responding to the points raised tends to leave a bad taste in my mouth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although I understand your grievance against talking about someone's work without that person being able to defend themselves, being too cautious about not judging their writing ability just hinder our ability to discuss their work meaningfully.<br /> <br /> I'll say what leaves a bad taste in my mouth:<br /> <br /> 1 - Stating that a new work isn't responsible for furthering the problems of previous work just because &quot;wasn't intended to change original concept&quot;. If the original concept have a problem, it must be addressed as soon as possible, not deepened;<br /> <br /> 2 - Assuming that going for a stricter concept justifies stereotyping things that do have real-world equivalents. The 4 Independents didn't needed to be better developed just because too strict a concept is a bad choice, but because they have clearer RL counterparts than any other clan. The 2 Sabbat ones too, but to a lesser extent;<br /> <br /> 3 - Leaving aside matters of depiction that affect RL people when defending a work, dismissing it as not worth the amount of nuance it brings up, given that it brings nuance precisely because it affects real people. The whole phrase &quot;endless swamp of minute disagreements and accusations of bigotry&quot;, despite not being necessarily wrong on some conversations, push no less than 3 red buttons for me.<br /> <br /> 4 - Putting the well being of the author above the well being of the people directly or indirectly depicted. That leaves a terrible taste in my mouth.<br /> <br /> You are right that talking low of other's work isn't always fair. But bringing up the author's credentials isn't doing it favors. For what matters, it was the early 90's and it was one of the worse periods for design theory on RPGs ever, so I do accept the idea that doing such limited scope for the new clans probably seemed like a good idea, even for the best authors of the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T09:26:49-08:00","id":1467451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467438#post1467438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No no, I did not mean to imply that the additional clans after the core seven were at any point intended to be for GMs only. They were, as you rightly point out, initially introduced in various <i>Player's Guides,</i> after all.<br /> <br /> The distinction I would make is more subtle than a binary idea of player clans versus NPC clans. It seems self-evidently clear to me that the original seven clans were intended to be the primary player clans, and that the additional clans introduced afterwards were for character concepts on the fringes of Kindred society. This is why all the independent clan concepts in particular are much more narrow than any of the core clans, even including the Tremere -- weird and insular cults, a single family line, and so on.<br /> <br /> It's precisely the notion that the early game 'failed really hard' or was 'badly written' that I want to push against. Like you, I used to think that all the 13 clans were supposed to have conceptual 'parity', since I was introduced to the game well after the Revised era had rolled in, and during that edition the independent clan depictions in particular had developed toward broader concepts than initially written. However, while all the clans introduced later into the game were explicitly playable from the start, they were by no means meant to have the broad appeal and archetypal nature of clans like Brujah or Ventrue.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, I get the idea being put forward, I'm just saying, take even just the Sabbat Clans/the Sabbat itself. They got a huge push in 2e. If the idea wasn't to present them as play options of equal parity, that was a lot of space and time wasted on both a player's guide, an st guide, a &quot;by Night&quot; citybook for Montreal, and individual clanbooks for the Lasombra and Tzimisce. That's a lot of fleshing out. This doesn't mean the material was necessarily good, it just means it was certainly present to the point that it would be hard to say that once the decision to make the Sabbat playable was made, parity wasn't a goal.<br /> <br /> And the take on the Assamites from their clanbook was already getting pushback all of a year later when in A World of Darkness Second Edition they were portrayed as being able to build bonds of honest respect, alliance and friendship with non Assamite vampires as entire groups with the introduction of the Ashirra. That's something that their clanbook would regard as being categorically impossible. And again, this itself doesn't mean the material was necessarily good, but it was happening. (A World of Darkness Second Edition has its flaws)<br /> <br /> And then you have Vampire: the Dark Ages, a book/gameline that predates the revised era, in which the 13 clans (well, Cappadocians instead of Giovanni), were presented as literal corebook playing options of equal parity.<br /> <br /> What I'm trying to put forward is that while the idea of the 13 clans with conceptual parity might see its full flourishing in Revised, the idea existed and was developed in second edition, even as second edition would undermine itself in specific execution in places through dubious writing choices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T10:43:17-08:00","id":1467455,"title":"","content":"As someone who came into the game late, I hold onto the idea that I should never just look at the newest version as the truth. If 1e wants the Assamites as monsters and Revised has them as enlightened kindred protecting the kine, I feel like I need to weigh the value of both and compromise; Perhaps they're both true from different points of view, or perhaps neither is true and the truth is somewhere in the middle. Throw in some armchair sociology in there because VTM is a Satire and it's supposed to make you think (and perhaps a healthy distrust of some of the authors) I like my Independent clans as <i>difficult </i>but with plenty of appeal and reason to exist. <br /> <br /> The main issue concerning what the Camarilla's goals are is that, well, the Camarilla is really a hands-off kinda deal. The Archons, nevermind the justicars, don't stoop to deal with princes all that much.<br /> Perhaps in talking about protectionism (Camarilla as Cartel if you must) we're really looking at a local level issue, rather than some idea the Inner circle cooked up. Or perhaps we're looking at the natural results of racism or individual clans with a foothold driving out competitive clans without; The Ventrue are inclined to supress the Lasombra, the Gangrel have always warred with the Ravnos, the Tremere... Tremere. <br /> <br /> Ultimately, there just aren't that many of the other 6 clans in the Camarilla, or at least well integrated within the camarilla (Like, If the Lasombra or Giovanni have territory in the Cam, but still act as outsiders, I'm not counting that) and I feel there needs to be a good, multifaceted reason why. The best I can think of is that the big-boys resist such interlopers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T11:19:33-08:00","id":1467458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ultimately, there just aren't that many of the other 6 clans in the Camarilla, or at least well integrated within the camarilla (Like, If the Lasombra or Giovanni have territory in the Cam, but still act as outsiders, I'm not counting that) and I feel there needs to be a good, multifaceted reason why. The best I can think of is that the big-boys resist such interlopers. </div> </div> </div>The best you can think of requires ignoring a variety of published game content across multiple editions that can be outright quoted, from 2e to revised to V20 is the thing being noted. If you're saying you don't personally like the provided reasons, i.e. that the Camarilla wanted, tried and ultimately failed to get a variety of other clans to join, hey sure. If you're saying you need to personally headcanon why things are the way they are and your intent is to specifically ignore game material across three to four different editions because you personally disapprove of them, hey sure. Every time you imply the things you think are in fact canon and how VtM actually works, the game material presented to this point itself shows you are wrong, unless you can at this point name an actual book where it legitimately says these things. Which would be notable, when the actual books noted so far by people talking about the content of VtM can be directly quoted saying in many cases the complete opposite of what you want to be true.<br /> <br /> According to VtM itself, the Camarilla wanted as many clans beyond the 7 as possible to join. They just were not able to make that go at sect founding, due ultimately to those other clans not wanting to join, for their various reasons. When, as VtM went along and further developed, those circumstances and desires changed for some of those clans, they were able to join the Camarilla. That's the game as it is and even V5, with its Lasombra and Assamites joining the Camarilla, rolls with that notion in some ways. Everything else you keep trying to say to this point is what you personally want the game to be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel like I need to weigh the value of both and compromise; Perhaps they're both true from different points of view, or perhaps neither is true and the truth is somewhere in the middle. </div> </div> </div>Then you're not talking about VtM, you're talking about what you want VtM to be. When VtM is making objective statements about its own setting, trying to say &quot;well it's this instead&quot; means you are no longer talking about anything but your personal, non canon view of VtM. It's also very difficult to see where in your posts you have done the thing you are talking about as far as claiming that what you are doing is compromising between editions. For example: Your response to the early 2e Tzimisce reason for not joining the Camarilla was &quot;I don't believe it.&quot; Your response to the later Tzimisce reason for not joining the Camarilla was &quot;no, I'm sure it was that the Camarilla didn't really want them to join or just thought there was no real chance of it.&quot; Your response to direct quotes of that the Camarilla wanted to unify all kindred at its founding is to now say it doesn't matter, because the Camarilla is hands off. Your response to that other clans indeed were actually able to later join the Camarilla despite everything you claim about how it works was &quot;I don't acknowledge this as having happened.&quot; It's difficult to see how it's possible to read that as anything but wanting to say that setting material that gets in the way of what you want the setting to be, doesn't exist. The early 2e material doesn't exist for you, the later 2e material doesn't exist for you, the revised era material doesn't exist for you, the V20 material you disagree with doesn't exist for you, the V5 material doesn't exist for you. What compromise between these things are you talking about?<br /> <br /> The problem I think you keep crashing into is that for some seeming reason you don't want to acknowledge the idea that you're discussing your personal preference and ideas for VtM, instead of what the setting has actually provided. I assure you, there's nothing actually wrong with preferring your personal headcanon VtM to canon VtM. Storyteller's Vault operates in part on an entire principle of people preferring their personal headcanon VtM and wanting to try to market it a bit, with some decent results. Wanting VtM to work how you say it does instead of how it actually does has a long and proud history. There is however something difficult to understand about you seeming to insist that's not what you're doing, in the face of repeated examples to the contrary.<br /> <br /> There is a difference between &quot;I think logically the setting should work like I say it does.&quot; and &quot;the setting works like I say it does, even though it clearly doesn't in a variety of places across its published history&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel there needs to be a good, multifaceted reason why. The best I can think of is that the big-boys resist such interlopers. </div> </div> </div>The game has given its reasons why. You just personally don't like them. Which hey, that is absolutely your right not to like them. I can't think of anyone who likes everything about VtM, even for the editions they like the most. It just also means the reasons you are attempting don't intersect with the actual game, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 11-11-2021, 02:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T11:49:54-08:00","id":1467461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467455#post1467455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main issue concerning what the Camarilla's goals are is that, well, the Camarilla is really a hands-off kinda deal. The Archons, nevermind the justicars, don't stoop to deal with princes all that much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed the Camarilla <b>is</b> a hands-off thing.<br /> <br /> That's on design, so you focus on describing your city instead of bringing a lot of pre-made plots and <i>status quo</i>. And that's the OoC reason for the Camarilla to be open and hands-off. It does, in fact, reduces the feel of the Camarilla as a presence on the characters lives unless in conflict with other sects.<br /> <br /> For most games that's a feature. You may throw almost anything in your chronicle as long as it is geographically limited, including all your ideas. Nothing needs to be a sect-wide truth to be truth for a given region. It also let you solve the distribution of clans just by changing then to your taste. A given city may have any clan spread whatsoever and anyone may be Camarilla. And for globe-trotting chronicles you have an easier time to focus on the moments and areas where the Camarilla is hands-on.<br /> <br /> Ultimately I don't think your take is unlikely to appear in any given city or not fun to use in a chronicle. It's not my favorite take, but just because I like to mess with local clan distribution anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T12:59:26-08:00","id":1467464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466535-what-goals-do-the-camarilla-have-beyond-survival-masquerade?p=1467451#post1467451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I get the idea being put forward,</div> </div> </div> </div>But... this is not how you presented my argument above when you responded to it. What you wrote was <i>&quot;I can't really agree that second edition particularly didn't want to treat all kinds of clans as playable&quot;</i> and <i>&quot;The Clanbooks themselves weren't meant as some 'GM only' thing.&quot;</i> I argued for neither of those things -- I think the exact opposite of the views that you were responding to. I chalked up the misunderstanding to perhaps expressing myself inadequately, so I offered a clarification of my views in response. It is frustrating that you would then respond as if you had clearly understood my argument from the start, when you demonstrably represented my views above in a way that I do not agree with.<br /> <br /> I am fully on board with the sentiment that a lot of Revised era developments had their roots in the early editions. Revised Edition does not represent some kind of clean break with the past, but a continuation and reinterpretation of the earlier material. However, looking at the original texts you cited in support of your argument, I'm not sure the narrative you present really pans out. To take just one example, the 2nd Edition of <i>A World of Darkness</i> offers very little new information about the Assamites. There are only a couple of paragraphs about the clan scattered here and there, and only a single sentence about trust between the Assamites and a group of non-Assamites in the entire book: <i>&quot;While they are not present in great numbers, the Hashashin have powerful allies within the courts of the Middle East. The strongest alliance rests with the Hajj and is based on a deep sense of mutual trust.&quot;</i> If this is pushback against <i>Clanbook: Assamite,</i> it's almost imperceptibly mild pushback.<br /> <br /> However, I will grant you that simply looking at the published products from the early 90s supports your position. My argument about the conceptual disparity between the original clans and the latecomers is not based on just the books, but also on contemporary and later developer comments. Mark Rein-Hagen in particular has stressed in interviews that he spent the vast majority of development before the publication of the game drilling down on the original seven clan concepts. In contrast, the additional clans did not receive nearly as much design and development. I simply argue that this was not an oversight, but a deliberate design decision to emphasize the original seven clans as the core of the game, and to leave the rest of the clans quite literally as supplemental material.<br /> <br /> At least for me, looking at the additional clans through this lens solves a lot of the problems I used to have with their narrow scope. In my view, none of the non-core clans have ever really overcome their initially limited concepts, and later reinterpretations have only served to muddle rather than to clarify what each of the non-core clans is about. Your mileage may of course vary, and that's really the crux of the disagreement here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T13:17:06-08:00","id":1467469,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">I think the arguments here have kind of exhausted themselves and we've received multiple complaints. As such, I'm shutting this thread down.</span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}